(410,'Web Developer / Designer w/ecommerce',4,'You will be responsible for designing the layout, visual elements, and usability of a website. Your goal is to create something that is not only visually appealing but also streamlined for ecommerce and easy to use.  You will utilize your UX, UI skills as an information architect (establishing the site\'s structure and hierarchy for SEO) to visually design a website catered specifically to supporting the user experience.\r\n\r\nThe Job Overview\r\nWe are looking for a web designer/ developer, e-commerce implementation specialist. You will be involved in the design and development of our website, from the earliest conception to final release. As our web designer, you will be responsible on both the front and back ends to create intuitive, attractive user interfaces to engage customers, encouraging them to sign up for our programs. Your duties will include taking requirements (i.e site mapping), creating mock-ups, and designing layouts while balancing the usability, visual appeal, and technical feasibility of the designs. You will also have the opportunity to potentially plan and execute ongoing projects as the site evolves, while improving the overall quality of the website.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\nCreate wireframes or mockups for web pages and applications for approval\r\nDesign layouts for mobile, tablet, and desktop devices\r\nCreate branding and identity systems for websites, apps, and other media\r\nEnsure the website’s ecommerce (Woocommerce) application flows smoothly\r\nEnsure site optimizes best practices for SEO\r\nDesign relevant graphics, icons, and logos\r\nDesign or populate selected or custom WordPress themes\r\nWork with CEO and marketing to implement visual elements of websites\r\nEstablish and maintain design standards and best practices\r\n\r\nJob Qualifications and Skill Sets:\r\nProficiency with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\r\nBachelor’s degree or diploma in design or a related field\r\nExperience a