(617,'Need experienced Social Worker or Counselor to design training',2,'Howdy!\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for an experienced social worker (or person who has worked with vulnerable people) to create infographic(s) for our upcoming Substance Abuse training. In creating the infographics you are essentially designing the entire 60-minute training. You will decide what tools are taught (and explain why they work), what research is relevant, and how to explain it visually. While on the surface this may appear to be a simple task, it is not. We spend 30+ hours on infographics for a single training before the training itself is designed.\r\n\r\nWhile the training will apply to dealing with any drunk/high/detoxing customer, the focus will be on homeless customers who are under the influence.\r\n---------------------------\r\nABOUT US\r\n\r\nOur team at www.HomelessTraining.com creates online training courses that teach people about homelessness (how to compassionately manage problem behavior from troubled people).\r\n\r\nWe take the work VERY seriously (if we don’t try to end homelessness, who will?).\r\n\r\nWe don’t take ourselves seriously, though… at all. We like to have fun and be playful and creative with the work.\r\n\r\nYou can watch a clip from our Mental Illness training at this link: https://vimeo.com/734096453\r\n\r\nYou can watch a clip from our Prejudicial comments training at this link: https://vimeo.com/734096453\r\n------------------------------\r\nABOUT THE PROJECT\r\n\r\nThis is a fixed price project. We anticipate it will require up to 20 hours to complete. The project must be submitted within 14 days.\r\n\r\nFor the project, we will provide you a long (very academic) research report on substance abuse and detailed instructions. We will also provide you with copies of our other infographics for reference. I have attached a copy of the infographics for one of our Mental Illness trainings (how to handle delusions) so you can see what our infographics typically look like.\r\n\r\nYou will develop up to 3 single-page infographics that will form the basis of the training on substance abuse.\r\n\r\nThe infographics:\r\n• Must convey the primary teachings of the training (which you will decide based on your de-escalation experience and the provided research)\r\n• Include research-based information/tools explained in an understandable way (6-grade level)\r\n• Do not have to be “designed” but must be constructed well enough that it is clear what the lessons are\r\n\r\n------------------------------\r\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\r\n\r\nIf we like your infographics, we’ll have more work in the future. We are constantly creating new trainings and updating old trainings.\r\n\r\nWhat we are looking for in a person:\r\n• You MUST have experience with de-escalation and vulnerable populations (homelessness preferred). We will not consider anyone who does not have highly relevant professional experience.\r\n• You MUST be able to read and understand very complicated academic research.\r\n• You MUST be the type of person who loves to learn new information/ideas but is able to identify what is most relevant to a training.\r\n• You MUST be able to draw from your own experience and combine that with research findings to develop tools others can use.\r\n• You MUST be able to simplify advanced concepts so you can teach them to others.\r\n• You MUST believe in the inherent dignity and worth of every human being.\r\n\r\n------------------------------\r\nYOUR PROPOSAL\r\n\r\nIn your proposal, please include:\r\n• Your experience with de-escalation and working with vulnerable populations\r\n• Your experience training others\r\n• The minimum and maximum hours per week you would be available in the future.\r\n• Your hourly rate\r\n\r\nOh, and please include AT THE VERY TOP OF YOUR PROPOSAL the name of your favorite Emilio Estevez movie (so I know that you actually read this the whole way through).\r\n\r\nThanks!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1587830946126766081?success','NA',7,'United States','Sugar Grove',1000.000,'fixed',850.000,'2022-11-02',1,'2022-11-02',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-02 15:42:03',NULL,6,3,NULL,111),
(618,'Wordpress developer to revamp website',3,'We are a company looking to revamp our website with a new Wordpress theme and new designs.\r\n\r\nWe are looking to bring in a Wordpress developer to help us with the following:\r\n\r\n- manage the plugins (they need to be updated -we tried and got a critical error)\r\n- change the wordpress theme (currently Elementor Pro) to a new faster theme (we\'d welcome suggestions on fast themes too)\r\n- build the 6/7 new pages on the new wordpress theme following the designs that we will provide\r\n\r\nWe\'d like to ideally have the website switched to the new theme and the new revamped pages live early December.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/job/~01983a0aa068cd54b2/apply/','NA',7,'United States','London',30.000,'perhour',40.000,'2022-11-02',1,'2022-11-02',1,'Hourly',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-02 15:44:18',NULL,6,3,NULL,111),
(619,'Freelance Website Designer for White Label Projects',4,'Are you a freelance website designer who excels at creating clean, elegant, and modern website designs in XD, Figma, Photoshop, or a related platform?\r\n\r\nBuddy Web Design & Development (www.buddywdd.com) is a growing and entrepreneurial website design and development company headquartered in the Grand Rapids, Michigan area. Buddy has built a portfolio of clients across the United States, and is currently seeking a talented and experienced website designer who would be able to help take on occasional project work as Buddy’s workload grows. This work can be done remotely and part time, according to a schedule of your choosing, provided development milestones are met, and that you are available to join occasional project calls with clients, as needed per the project.\r\n\r\nFor this role, Buddy is searching for an independent contractor who can spearhead the design of functional, elegant, easy-to-use, and mobile-responsive websites. Commonly Buddy develops marketing and e-commerce websites for small to mid-sized businesses, most often built using WordPress and Elementor.\r\n\r\nAn ideal person for this opportunity will have experience working in a freelance and independent contractor capacity, coupled with expertise in designing websites with an outstanding aesthetic. An ideal candidate will bring high attention to detail and best practices, a high degree of professionalism and integrity, coupled with a comfort in working in an evolving, entrepreneurial environment that can have ambiguity at times. If this sounds interesting to you, please apply!\r\n\r\nSolo freelancers only, please -- no agencies :)','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1587832524850024449','NA',7,'United States','Wyoming',80.000,'perhour',80.000,'2022-11-02',1,'2022-11-02',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-02 15:44:33',NULL,6,3,NULL,111),
