(717,'Build Ecommerce Website for D2C Food Product',3,'Phase 1 - building an informational website that captures potential member (customer) information.\r\n-Interactive conversational-style lead form\r\n- The conversational-lead form will allow us to gather more information on people while keeping the experience engaging. This data then can be stored or used to create community and/or commerce accounts. It can also be used to target specific users for marketing or follow up research\r\n- Community aspects of engagement, feedback and learning.  An area where people can login to communicate or share ideas.\r\n- Automated Marketing emails to clients.\r\n- Blog Posts\r\n\r\nPhase 2 - Launch commerce platform. This would be ideally launched soon after we gathered research and or product feedback/interest in Phase 1.\r\n- Product recommendation quiz for new clients\r\n- For clients who were part of Phase 1 targeted marketing to suggest products based on what we\'ve learned\r\n- Subscription offerings\r\n- Sell products in person at events\r\n- Possibility to sell via other channels (Facebook, Instagram, Google, etc.)\r\n\r\nPhase 3 -  launch of our membership and content/community area and strategy. This would be a hybrid think Amazon Prime where different membership levels get exclusive pricing, shipping benefits, or access to content.\r\n\r\nWe believe Phase 1 is fully managed with the exclusion of reporting & customer data. We would like to have access to reports that we can use for our research and product development. We would like to be trained on how to use these tools so that our team can use the data to support our operations.\r\n\r\nFor phase 2, initial build out to be fully managed, with training on how to make basic modifications (sales, pricing, inventory, etc.) or how to add additional products. This then could transition into assisted management or self-management depending on our team\'s bandwidth and availability.\r\n\r\nFor phase 3, the initial buildout be fully managed and the content management be self-managed allowing you to quickly add new content (videos, blog posts, comments) as needed.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a complete solution including tech stack recommendations and options, design, implementation, integration and training around the use of the solution.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a site with the best solution and are highly open to working with Shopify, Wordpress and pre-existing tech.\r\n\r\nOpenness to work with a graphic designer is preferred.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01fb4d20b256ff6484','NA',7,'United States','Ashland',65.001,'perhour',90.000,'2022-11-03',1,'2022-11-03',0,'Ahmed Nayeem',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-03 08:48:33',NULL,6,3,NULL,111),
