(1043,'designer for new Company Logo',2,'Your Sixth Man Logo should be 2-3 colors and should work as a single color as well. \r\n\r\nIt should be embroidery and screen print friendly and work well on white or black backgrounds. \r\n\r\n\r\nI would like t have the logo done by November 22nd if possible. \r\n\r\n\r\nBackground on company name: Your Sixth Man \r\n\r\nI played college basketball and have been in leadership positions in the business world for over 30 years. I will be providing leadership development and business coaching to businesses and individuals.\r\n\r\n\r\nBelow is more info about Your Sixth Man to give your more insight:\r\n\r\n\r\nIn basketball the presence of a good sixth man is a sign of team excellence. Every team needs bench strength that compliments the contributions of the starting five.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe sixth man comes in and out of the game depending on the situation most often specializing in a specific area. The sixth man should be a positive force while enhancing the skills of the other team members. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIn business a sixth man can be even more valuable than in basketball. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSteve Truett is here to be Your Sixth Man and provide that bench strength for you. Steve has over 30 years of leadership experience and success leading franchise and sales organizations. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSteve has teamed with the Improving Performance and Results Organization (IPR) which specializes in increasing the performance of people by bringing out the best in leaders and those they lead. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nHe helps individuals and teams set and achieve goals, become self-motivated and have a positive mental attitude with proven time-tested leadership and development programs and including:\r\n\r\n    Getting Results Through Others\r\n    Improving Performance and Results\r\n    Strategic Planning Facilitation\r\n    Leading with Passion and Performance\r\n    The Game of Work\r\n    One on One Coaching\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSteve also does Keynotes and speaking engagements. Popular topics include\r\n\r\n    Business is a Sport, Play to Win\r\n    Creating a Values Driven Organization\r\n    Keeping Score for Success\r\n    Bridging the Leadership Gap','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/1963083','n/a',7,'United States','-',250.000,'fixed',250.000,'2022-11-09',1,'2022-11-09',1,'fixed',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-09 20:51:50',NULL,6,1,NULL,136),
