(1612,'Video intro/transition animation with logo',2,'Hi\r\n\r\nTogether with my business partner we are in the course of creating online video tutorials which will be hosted behind a firewall and would love to have a 3-5 second introduction animation we can add to each video.\r\n\r\nThe purpose is for us to add it immediately after we have given a short introduction to viewers on what to expect, a bit like a transition from intro to the real deal.\r\nWe would like to have “Simplification Works” as main title and our hashtag logo animated.\r\nAs our logo is based on a simple hashtag and has 4 lines which plays out nice to also give a very very short glimpse on the 4 complexities we teach the viewers to address:\r\n➸ Horizontal complexity- consolidating functions across the enterprise\r\n➸ Vertical complexity - shedding obsolete roles, layers and reporting structures\r\n➸ Spatial complexity - preparing distributed and remote teams for success\r\n➸ Technical complexity - removing technical debt\r\nMaybe a bit like: here is logo intro & then very very rapidly each complexity with it’s how.\r\nWe have the idea to have the logo been build up in 4 pieces and while each piece is flying in or something else one of the complexities is addressed. Once entire logo is out there “Simplification Works” can be shown. How does that sounds? Something doable?\r\n\r\nColour codes we general use in our communication:\r\nDark: #0b0c10\r\nLight dark: #1f2833\r\nGreen/blue: #45a29f\r\nLight green/blue: #66fcf1\r\nGrey: #c4c6c8\r\n\r\nLogo we can deliver in ai, psd, png files.\r\n\r\nWe’ll use the intro movie within Adobe Premiere Pro while editing our video tutorials.\r\n\r\nDoes this sound as something in your alley?\r\n\r\nGrtz\r\n/Jurgen','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1592532739782213633','NA',7,'United States','Kortrijk',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2022-11-15',1,'2022-11-15',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-15 15:01:41',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
