(2048,'Pitch deck',2,'My company, Hotspot, is fundraising from Venture Capital investors (VCs).\r\n\r\nHere\'s how the process works. I meet entrepreneurs who know VCs. The entrepreneur asks VCs they know if they would like to meet me and send our pitch deck. If the VC is impressed with the pitch deck then they will schedule a meeting. The deck is successful if the VC reviews it on their own and decides to have a meeting with me.\r\n\r\nDeck requirements:\r\n1. Clarity - far and away the most important thing. Most decks fail because the VC does not understand what’s going on.\r\n2. Eye catching - this is where you come in. The deck should be visually appealing and draw in the investor. VCs view hundreds of ugly decks per year. Ours needs to be beautiful.\r\n3. Consistent - the deck must have consistent fonts, font sizing, font weights, colors, spacing, imagery, icons etc.\r\n\r\nOur current deck is made in Figma (attached as PDF). Ideally the final deliverable is in Pitch.com or Google Slides so that I can edit it.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1593016323253075969?success','na',7,'United States','Claymont',80.000,'perhour',80.000,'2022-11-16',1,'2022-11-16',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-16 23:02:20',NULL,6,3,NULL,131),
