(2338,'small website for research',3,'Small website required for PhD student engaged in primary research: - \r\n\r\n\r\n1. Home Page\r\n\r\n2. About Page\r\n\r\n3. Content page\r\n\r\n4. Private Members Area (password protected)\r\n\r\n5. Blog Page\r\n\r\n6. FAQ page\r\n\r\n\r\nEnglish only.\r\n\r\nWill provide narrative, graphics and photos.\r\n\r\nWill provide MS PowerPoint decks.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe website must be secure as confidentiality and anonymity are guaranteed to the volunteers.\r\n\r\n\r\nPrivate Members Area and Content page must be able to host v\r\n\r\n   MS PowerPoint slide decks\r\n\r\n   Youtube or Vimeo channel.\r\n\r\n   Links Library to other websites and documents (easily updated)\r\n\r\nSee https://smilodon-octopus-9kmf.squarespace.com/ as an illustration of sample content, preferred style and structure.\r\n\r\n\r\nWebsite has to host an online forum within Private Members Area.\r\n\r\nParticipants will need to log in to access the Members area, its Content and this Forum.\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter registering, users\' real names must never be displayed on the site.  \r\n\r\nUsers must be prompted to use a site-specific nickname, so I need to control this for research purposes. It is vital that they cannot identify each other or be externally identified.\r\n\r\n\r\nHappy to respond to questions\r\n\r\n\r\nKieran\r\n\r\n\r\nA second phase for the website (Q42023) calls for the development of an online portal, where candidates can create profiles including documentation and possibly engage in ID verification. The portal would allow for searches of the candidate profiles by other research participants across a range of criteria - mostly relating to their employer, not the candidate themselves. Candidates will be then allowed engage with potential CSR partners and the website will have to track the extent, frequency and nature of these engagements over a given period of time. A full specification for this will be available around end Q2 2023.  Thank you.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/1968075','-',7,'United States','-',1000.000,'fixed',1400.000,'2022-11-18',1,'2022-11-18',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-18 19:45:49',NULL,6,1,NULL,136),
(2339,'High End Automotive Website Design',3,'We\'re looking for a designer who can help us build out a sleek, modern, and impressive website for our high-end auto technology business. We\'re looking for someone who can be attentive to detail and prioritize the user experience while keeping brand awareness in mind. Someone who values design aesthetics and understands how to create a visually appealing site that prioritizes the user experience while elevating the understanding of what this company does. The designer should be able to provide a visual narrative for this company such that users understand not only what they do, but why they are so successful in doing it.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who has experience in creating websites that are both visually appealing and intuitive to use. The ideal candidate may have experience working with content management systems (CMS) such as WordPress. They should also understand responsive web design (RWD) and be comfortable designing with a mobile-first mindset as well as providing a proper style guide to support design decisions.\r\n\r\nThis designer should also value and understand interactive elements on a website such as transitions or animations. While not expected to develop these elements, the designer should recognize how their design could incorporate and/or use these elements to better elevate the narrative of their design.\r\n\r\nCandidate must be able to produce figma or webflow files to support the vision.\r\n\r\nOther requirements:\r\n- Brand Guidelines\r\n- Interactive recommendations\r\n\r\nProcess will require check-ins throughout the design process to review direction and make any corrections before moving onto next steps.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1593695194301222913?success','NA',7,'United States','Troy',100.000,'Open this select menu',100.000,'2022-11-18',1,'2022-11-18',1,'hourly project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-18 20:00:17',NULL,6,3,NULL,143),
