(3264,'10-20hr/week Plastic-free Bottled Water Design',2,'RAIN Bottling Company is a single-sourced plastic free bottled water brand and manufacturer. From our own facility in North GA we bottle natural spring water in all-aluminum packaging.\r\n\r\nWe are a brand, RAIN first, but we also bottle aluminum bottled water for countless others, both on a one-time and ongoing contract basis. This includes promotional projects, hotel branded water, store branded water, new startup brands, retail stores, etc, etc. We have produced over 500 labels to date.\r\n\r\nWe recently lost our beloved contract designer to a full time role and are looking to fill the position again. This would be a 5-20 hr/week requirement depending on the needs of that moment. The bulk of the work would be producing new artwork(label) for our customers. We have found that a strong label and mockup typically can help to close the business, so this is a very important role to our success. Most often we start with a non-print ready mockup, something that you would be able to produce quickly that we can send off to the customer. From there and using a label template you would work with us, and the customer to produce a print-ready file. While we dont want to limit your our \"style\" many of our large customers do have brand guidelines that you may need to operate within. Other-times, the customer will give free range on the creative.\r\n\r\nLastly, RAIN the brand needs less-often marketing support. This includes small changes to the website, email banners, point of sale materials, electronic sales collateral, etc. This would also fall under your purview.\r\n\r\nFor convenience we have attached some past projects that our designer created to give a sense of the work.\r\n\r\nPlease do reachout if interested, and if possible send some relevant work you have done in the past. For bonus points, make a quick and dirty mockup of a sustainable bottled water brand you came up with!\r\n\r\nThanks in advance!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1598078613510930433','NA',7,'United States','Tiger',100.000,'perhour',100.000,'2022-11-30',1,'2022-11-30',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-30 22:17:52',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
(3265,'Edtech company website rework',4,'Our company is seeking a partner to help us harmonize a WordPress-based multi site into a single themed site, and modernize the consolidated site\'s appearance and capabilities.\r\n\r\nWe\'re envisioning an approximate 2-3 month engagement along the lines of:\r\n\r\n-New information architecture, folding two existing sites (https://www.edsby.com and https://www.edsby.com/unison) together; also seeking to optimize site\'s lead conversion with higher emphasis on social proof and reducing distractions; also contemplating rationalization of existing public tech support content vs. a forthcoming HubSpot-hosted customer knowledge base, and possible new community features, incl. feature voting\r\n\r\n-Re-theme, with a new mobile-first emphasis, and application of theme to HubSpot, so HubSpot forms and other content potentially hosted on HubSpot in future will be seamless\r\n\r\n-Assess whether to stay on WPBakery vs. other frameworks like Elementor\r\n\r\n-Convert certain proprietary technologies on current site to use off-the-shelf plugins where possible\r\n\r\n-Performing entire engagement within the lens of SEO improvement; our company is in a competitive space with commoditized keywords\r\n\r\nWe expect we\'d be doing the majority of writing for the new site, but are looking to our partner to bring fresh thinking on IA and best practices re: modern WordPress theming, mobile optimization and SEO. And the ability to quarterback the whole project while doing the heavy tech and design lifting.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~019ff3c70d25c6b8b6','NA',7,'United States','richmond',20000.000,'fixed',20000.000,'2022-11-30',1,'2022-11-30',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-30 22:23:18',NULL,6,3,NULL,125),
