(3304,'Website Developer for Ecommerce Sites',3,'OVERVIEW:\r\n\r\nPaylidify is currently seeking multiple website developers to help us grow our retail ecommerce and food & beverage online ordering campaign. The candidate would be responsible to build template (ex. Squarespace) or custom (ex. WordPress) websites for various small to medium sized businesses. The business demographics will include restaurants, liquor stores, clothing, consumer electronics, furniture, jewelry, etc. We will be leveraging select ecommerce shopping cart integrations, such as BigCommerce, Woocommerc, Shopify and Zuppler. Our goal is to help our clients evolve in the digital commerce landscape by providing them with the online tools to run their business better, and attract new customers. Specifically in the online ordering space, we be helping restaurants, liquor stores, and grocery stores convert from third-party delivery providers (i.e. Doordash, Grubhub, UberEats) to a website and custom-branded mobile app ordering model (via Zuppler). This will in turn help our clients save thousands of dollars every month in online ordering fees. As for the payment gateway integration, we will be leveraging Authorize.Net, NMI, and/or Braintree for the payment gateway.\r\n\r\nOnce our ecommerce campaign is fully ramped up, we anticipate a loading of 1-3 micro sites (pre-built framework, themed template design) per month and 1 - 4 custom sites (WordPress with Elementor, Yoast, BigCommerce, and Auth.net) per year.\r\n\r\nBENEFITS:\r\n\r\nThe work can be conducted entirely remotely. The candidates will earn a competitive commission per business/client plus a monthly compounded residual income on the monthly transaction fees, in addition to the hourly work done on the websites. The estimated residual monthly revenue is $7,920 after 12 months of work.\r\n\r\nThis will be an ongoing project with client website builds for many years to come.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1598062337433636865?success','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1598062337433636865?success',7,'United States','Newport Beach',70.000,'perhour',70.000,'2022-11-30',1,'2022-11-30',1,'hourly project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-30 23:06:56',NULL,6,3,NULL,138),
(3305,'Figma UX/UI Designer',4,'We are looking for a UI/UX Designer to turn software ideas into easy-to-use products for our clients.\r\n\r\nUI/UX Designer responsibilities include gathering user requirements, designing graphic elements, and building navigation components. To be successful in this role, you should have experience with design software and wireframe tools. We want to meet you if you also have a portfolio of professional design projects that includes work with web/mobile applications.\r\n\r\nUltimately, you\'ll create functional and appealing features that address our client\'s needs and help us grow our customer base.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities\r\nGather and evaluate user requirements in collaboration with product managers and engineers\r\nIllustrate design ideas using storyboards, process flows, and sitemaps\r\nDesign graphic user interface elements, like menus, tabs, and widgets\r\nBuild page navigation buttons and search fields\r\nDevelop UI mockups and prototypes that clearly illustrate how sites function and look like\r\nCreate original graphic designs (e.g., images, sketches, and tables)\r\nPrepare and present rough drafts to internal teams and key stakeholders\r\nIdentify and troubleshoot UX problems (e.g., responsiveness)\r\nConduct layout adjustments based on user feedback\r\nAdhere to style standards on fonts, colors, and images\r\nRequirements and skills\r\nProven work experience as a UI/UX Designer or similar role\r\nPortfolio of design projects\r\nUp-to-date knowledge of Figma\r\nTeam spirit; strong communication skills to collaborate with various stakeholders\r\nGood time-management skills','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1598065458598166529?success','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1598065458598166529?success',7,'United States','Boston',70.000,'perhour',70.000,'2022-11-30',1,'2022-11-30',1,'hourly project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-11-30 23:08:19',NULL,6,3,NULL,138),
