(3425,'Senior UX/UI designer',4,'We are looking for a talented UI/UX Designer to design software applications and platforms that meet people’s needs and create amazing user experiences. A strong portfolio of successful UX design and other technical projects is essential.\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate should have an eye for clean and artful design, possess superior UI skills, and be able to translate high-level requirements into interaction flows and artifacts and transform them into beautiful, intuitive, and functional user interfaces.\r\n\r\nAs a UI/UX Designer, you will be responsible for delivering the best online user experience, which makes your role extremely important for our success and ensuring customer satisfaction and loyalty.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n- Create wireframes, storyboards, user flows, process flows and site maps to effectively communicate interaction and design ideas\r\n-Create \"original\" and \"unique\" graphic designs (e.g. images, sketches, illustrations, etc.)\r\n- Propose innovative solutions for the product direction, visuals, and experience\r\n- Illustrating design ideas using storyboards, process flows, and sitemaps\r\n-Execute all visual design stages from concept to final hand-off to engineering\r\n- Build page navigation buttons and search fields\r\n- Develop UI mockups and prototypes that clearly illustrate how sites function and look like\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate will also be able to produce UX/UI design for both Web and Mobile applications, understanding the core characteristics of the navigation in each portal.\r\n\r\nConversational English is required.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who can join us either in a part or full-time capability.\r\n\r\nFurther details will be provided during the interview','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01f87a6b29e6091af6','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01f87a6b29e6091af6',7,'United States','Geneve',55.000,'perhour',55.000,'2022-12-01',1,'2022-12-01',1,'hourly project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-01 22:22:04',NULL,6,3,NULL,138),
