(3499,'Power Point Design',2,'Hi! We\'re looking for someone to help us design an eye-catching Powerpoint presentation.\r\n\r\nThe deck we\'re having you design is a deck that we send to clients after we\'ve already pitched them.\r\n\r\n- We have a 10-slide client deck that is ready for you to work with.\r\n- We don\'t have an official style guide but I can share our website, some colours we use, and other assets we have.\r\n- We must be able to modify the text within the slides.\r\n- We\'re a SaaS company and there are some product screenshots we\'d like to have where they are mocked up in a tablet or phone.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01c40759a9496dfbe0','no',7,'United States','Vancouver',200.000,'fixed',200.000,'2022-12-02',1,'2022-12-02',1,'Fixed budget',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-02 21:30:48',NULL,6,3,NULL,133),
(3500,'Senior UI/UX Designer',6,'Project Description\r\n\r\nFohlio(www.fohlio.com) helps organizations with many locations design, procure products and maintain their spaces so that they can provide consistent good experiences that represent their identity and value to the guests. Think restaurant chains, schools, retail stores, banks, churches, and many more that impact our day-to-day life! We are a NY-based B2B SAAS tech startup, servicing 400+ design firms and real estate developers worldwide. We help design teams manage the firm-wide digital material library and design standards and streamline the collaborations between designers, procurement teams, suppliers, and more.\r\n\r\nWe are hiring a mid to senior UX/UI designer with good communication skills and experience in B2B SAAS data and workflow management software to understand the pain points of our users and excellent skills in creating design proposals and prototypes.\r\n\r\nDeliverables\r\n\r\nKey responsibilities:\r\n\r\nWork closely with the pm, sales, and customer success team to understand the needs of end-users, evaluate market trends and competition, and use this information to determine what features to build.\r\nConduct user research with the intended audience of the product to engage in requirements elicitation\r\nOrchestrate the various activities associated with ensuring that a product is delivered that meets users\' needs.\r\nProduce UX/UI mockups, and conduct design validation with users.\r\nWork with business analyst, QA team, and software engineering team for acceptance testing of the product. Throughout all the stages of the product development process\r\nBuild & manage the design system\r\n\r\n\r\nQualifications\r\n\r\n\r\nExperiences and Skills required:\r\n\r\nMust-Have\r\n\r\nExperience in building design systems\r\nThe ability to do user research and usability testing independently\r\nThe ability quickly understands the design scopes and come up with design proposals.\r\nExpert skills in creating Figma prototypes.\r\nAttention to detail, methodology, good communication skills, and responsiveness.\r\nAt least three years of UX/ UI experience in B2B SAAS software with data and workflow management\r\n\r\nAt least four years of professional experience in UX/UI user research, design, and/or product development\r\n\r\nLanguage: Fluent in English.\r\nLocation: Anywhere that you can work 9am -5pm EST\r\n\r\nHours: 40h/week\r\n\r\n$40+/hourly\r\n\r\nIntermedia to expert level','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1598791778681950209','NA',7,'United States','Jersey City',40.000,'perhour',40.000,'2022-12-02',1,'2022-12-02',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-02 21:33:06',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
