(3536,'Branding & deck design',2,'Context\r\nWe are a Startup studio/venture builder. We identify opportunities to build startups in underserved market segments and work with founders to build fast-growing, profitable companies. After ~6 months of in-the-garage operations, *name* is gearing towards its soft launch which requires a more consistent and compelling visual identity.\r\n\r\nWith that in mind, we are looking for embarking on a design sprint to produce a basic design language.\r\nTo clarify: we recognize that we will not be able to have a full-on branding exercise in the time so we are only looking for basic design elements that will make us look compelling and organized.\r\n\r\nDeliverables needed\r\n1. Logo (prefer logotypes or a combination of logotypes + icon)\r\n2. Typeface selection (with a strong focus on font pairing in the presentation deck) + Prefer selections from Google font\r\n3. Brand core color scheme\r\nPotential use one color to reflect the main attribute of *name*, and dark and light colors to some options, play with it so it\'s interesting and clean\r\n4. A pdf brand guideline with the fundamental application of items 1,2,3\r\n5. Pitch deck base deck (Google slide)\r\n(A) 10 basic slide layouts for utilization\r\n(B) Reusable elements such as icons, color blocks\r\n(C) Sample slides with annotation of how to apply different layouts and elements\r\n\r\nWith time, we will likely require additional design support for the website, and communication materials (e.g., one pager, deck, etc)\r\n\r\nTimeline\r\nWe would like to start ASAP and get to the deliverables listed above no later than the end of the year\r\n\r\nPlease read the branding brief and **send back a portfolio example and/or 1-2 examples of work that might be **relevant/close to what we are looking for.\r\n\r\n(1) The budget is for the whole project, if you think you can accomplish more in this project (ie add a 1-pager, landing page layout, etc) - please let us know.\r\n\r\n(2) Also - we will break this project into 2 sections: preliminary design and logo sketches as first milestone before we complete to there rest of the world (the idea is that we could part ways without too much time wasted if we are not on the same wave lane)\r\n\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1m_-KwsMDEmiPOrSY3lfpGgHW3sjFdVtSpWHhwQDSe4k/edit?usp=sharing','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1599795201451945985','no link',7,'United States','New York',850.000,'fixed',850.000,'2022-12-05',1,'2022-12-05',1,'fix project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-05 16:05:25',NULL,7,3,NULL,115),
(3537,'Logo Design Fintech',2,'Looking for 3 concepts for a logo for a Fintech website that matches the overall design of the UI Figma file. Then choose one design to be finalised.\r\n\r\nJust want something that fits in with the modern world of digital banking.\r\n\r\nIf you have any experience making logos for fintech start-up’s that would help.\r\n\r\nWe have the Figma file for the UX / UI completed so looking for a Logo to match the overall design of the website and make it look more impressive. Will send this file.\r\n\r\nOnce finalised on the design all files transferred, and the favicon separated.\r\n\r\nAppreciate your time applying and reading this description.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01dced4bfbc9c78492','no',7,'United States','Hatfield',150.000,'fixed',150.000,'2022-12-05',1,'2022-12-05',1,'Fixed budget',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-05 16:08:19',NULL,6,3,NULL,133),
