(3884,'Graphic Design - Vector Logo &/or Graphic',2,'Looking for a logo/graphic of a dung beetle rolling a circular logo.\r\n\r\nPlease, when replying to this post, make your first word Banana. This is how I know you\'ve actually read the description :-)\r\n\r\nI am looking for a graphic to go on hats and t-shirts. I would like a side profile of a dung beetle pushing/rolling a perfect sphere. I have included examples that are close to what I am looking for. However, I would like the final result to differ from these examples in the following ways:\r\n\r\n1) Modular Dung\r\n\r\nMake the \"dung\" itself a perfect sphere. I would like it to be very easy to swap in a circular logo in place of a template sphere.\r\n\r\n2) Focus on the beetle\r\n\r\nNo need to put any detail or texture into the dung portion of the graphic, as this will be a circular logo. The effort and detail should go into the beetle itself, and the proportions between the beetle and the dung.\r\n\r\n3) Customizable format\r\n\r\nThe final file format should be vector format, with layers and/or filters. This will allow me to change what the sphere is with basic editing software. Please don\'t send me a format that requires an expensive adobe license to edit.\r\n\r\n4) Invert the beetle/use \"human\" posture for the beetle.\r\n\r\nI would like the beetle to be pushing the dung with its front legs, and have its back legs on the ground. All of the examples of beetles show the opposite, the beetle with its front legs on the ground, pushing the dung with the back legs. Please invert this. I have included two example graphics of a human pushing a large ball up a hill. Please use this posture as the general template for what the beetle posture should be. The graphic does not need to be on a hill or incline though, it can be flat.\r\n\r\n5) Simple and abstract, but not cartoony.\r\n\r\nThe closest example I have to what I am after is the file: \"dung beetle side profile.png\". This has a simplified and abstract beetle, side profile with a perfect sphere. I would prefer a slightly more detailed beetle with 4 limbs, with the inverted posture requested in #4.\r\n\r\n\"dung beetle side cartoon.jpg\" is also close to what I am after. The detail on the dung itself is not needed, and I find the shadow and shading to be a little too detailed.\r\n\r\n\"dung beetle cartoon bettle.png\" is also quite close (assuming the posture was invetered). I do like the simplistic \"human-looking\" body shape. But I REALLY don\'t like the cartoon face. Please do not include a cartoon face like this.\r\n\r\n\"dung beetle picture.jpg\" is just a real-life example of what all the graphics were depicting. Obviously, I don\'t want anything this realistic, but I am including it as a reference of what the end result is trying to depict. However, please use the \"human\" posture\r\n\r\nI look forward to working with you on this.\r\n\r\nThe end result should be a vector format graphic that I can print onto hats and t-shirts. I would like to use multiple logos as the \"dung\". The logos I have in mind are monochrome, so I am happy to provide that color if it would influence your coloring of the beetle and graphic.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01cfcd55ea2f3c5e18','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01cfcd55ea2f3c5e18',7,'United States','none',70.000,'Open this select menu',70.000,'2022-12-07',1,'2022-12-07',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-07 20:15:51',NULL,6,3,NULL,138),
