(3893,'Book Cover Design',2,'I am wanting a book cover design for my new book Fifty Shades of Darkness. I want it to be a little simple, but also have a \"creep\" factor. I was thinking of maybe a door opening with a face, or maybe just two eyes on a dark background... I am open to suggestions as well. Looking for someone interested in the paranormal maybe of help understand my ideas and viewpoint.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance...','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1600594449985040385?success','Na',7,'United States','Lake Dallas',50.000,'perhour',50.000,'2022-12-07',1,'2022-12-07',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-07 20:54:48',NULL,6,3,NULL,140),
(3894,'UI/UX Web Designer',4,'Savant is a web-based marketplace which allows anyone to invest in anything. We fractionalize equity within private market alternative assets, and tokenize these offerings on our portal for any type of investor around the world to purchase and freely trade on our secondary exchange. We offer both cash-flowing (single family houses, franchises, and brick and mortar businesses) as well as capital gains assets (investment grade wine, art collections, and vintage cars).\r\n\r\nSavant is looking for a UX/UI Designer to help us overhaul our current user interface, and design new features which are still conceptual. As of right now we have a large Figma file with our former UI, you job is to work with the CEO to revamp this! We are a start-up, and only have a handful of people on staff, so you will be reporting directly to our CEO. You will also be working alongside our Senior Developer, as he is going to implement your ideas!\r\n\r\nJob Description:\r\n\r\nThis is a full-time, remote position.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe job responsibilities for UX/UI Designer include:\r\n\r\n- Gather and evaluate user requirements in collaboration with CMO and Senior Developer\r\n- Illustrate design ideas using storyboards, process flows, and sitemaps\r\n- Design graphic user interface elements (menus, tabs, and widgets )\r\n- Build pages navigation buttons and search fields\r\n- Develop UI mockups and prototypes that clearly illustrate how sites/apps function and look like\r\n- Create original graphic designs (e.g., icons, images, illustrations, sketches, and tables)\r\n- Prepare and present rough drafts to internal teams and key stakeholders\r\n- Identify and troubleshoot UX problems (e.g., responsiveness)\r\n- Conduct layout adjustments based on user feedback\r\n- Adhere to company style standards on fonts, colors, and images\r\n- Test for intuitive and experience and optimize existing user interface designs\r\n- What we\'re looking for in a UX Designer:\r\n- 3+ years of professional experience in UX and or UI design\r\n- A high level of proficiency with Figma\r\n- Experience discovering solutions through research and user testing\r\n- A track record of synthesizing input from various sources into unified and useable functionality\r\n- Strong grasp of the best practices for designing mobile-first experiences\r\n- Ability to extend existing designs in a seamless fashion\r\n- Ability to explain your process and design decisions to your cross-functional partners\r\n- Experience in any of the following areas would be helpful: fintech, proptech, investing, visualizations, workflow software\r\n- Team spirit, strong communication skills to collaborate with various stakeholders\r\n- Good time-management skills\r\n- Working from 8:30AM-5:30PM in the Eastern Time Zone\r\n\r\nIt is vital that you present a portfolio highlighting your design process and showcasing the skills noted above. Please be sure to provide a link to your portfolio when applying.\r\n\r\nYou will thrive as a UX/UI Designer on our team if…\r\n\r\n- You enjoy turning complex problems into elegant solutions as part of a collaborative team\r\n- You believe it is important to understand and empathize with your users\r\n- You are driven to rapidly and iteratively work to improve your designs\r\n- You are willing to incorporate design feedback from all sources\r\n\r\nEducation Requirements:\r\n- Bachelor\'s degree preferred\r\n\r\nCompensation:\r\n- Bi-weekly compensation\r\n\r\nConsiderations:\r\n- How fast you are able to complete the work\r\n- How much you are charging\r\n- The quality of your work','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0174d672f5788630b4','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0174d672f5788630b4',7,'United States','Guilford',70.000,'perhour',70.000,'2022-12-07',1,'2022-12-07',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-07 20:56:23',NULL,6,3,NULL,138),
(3895,'Business Brand Identity designer Wanted',2,'Looking for experienced and high class Brand Identify designer to create Logo Design, Web design, Stationary Kits and Social Media Kits for my Export  business. Logo Design Concept should be eye catchy and attract my clients in the sense that it should win client\'s trust and hope over our business.\r\n\r\nPhase 1 - Logo Design (Upto 5 Concepts)\r\nPhase 2 - Stationary Kits (will be discussed the list of applicable stationaries)\r\nPhase 3 - Social Media Kits (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, Youtube, Twitter)\r\nPhase 4 - Build Responsive Web design and development (Complete Website)\r\n\r\nPlease apply only if you have real creative sense to imaging the nature of Goods Export Business.\r\n\r\nApply this Job with samples. If you have already created Logo design for Imports and exports business, you would highly preferred by me.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~018cec0566ecf2ca22','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~018cec0566ecf2ca22',7,'United States','none',600.000,'perhour',600.000,'2022-12-07',1,'2022-12-07',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-07 21:03:42',NULL,6,3,NULL,138),
