(3946,'Build/improve impactful PPT slides for MBA course on turnarounds & transformation',2,'=(Budget is negotiable, open to hourly as well).\r\n\r\nI am looking for a PPT intermediate-expert with business knowledge who can take some inputs and build out and improve some PPT slide decks for an MBA course on business transformations and turnarounds. Slides should not be busy and images must pack the most punch. You would not be starting from scratch on most of this, as I have a deck that needs refreshing.\r\n\r\nSome examples of the kind of work this entails:\r\n1. Clearly and succinctly demonstrate the different between a business turnaround and transformation with one slide and two pictures (give 1-2 options for me to choose from).\r\n\r\n2. Take the story of Ron Johnson\'s time at JCPenney and tell that story clearly on one slide (i.e. the business wasn\'t dying, so it wasn\'t a turnaround...it just wasn\'t doing much...but needed to be fixed/refreshed. What was the feeling when Johnson started...and how it came to an end).\r\n\r\n3. Same with Intel....show how that\'s another example of an organization that was not dying, but struggling to keep up. Use as an example to perhaps demonstrate why the organization which are harder to fix are the ones who are not \"failing failing\".\r\n\r\n4. Give me seminal examples of business turnarounds and business turnaround failures and show me the best way to show those on one slide.\r\n\r\n\r\nBonus points and chances for further work either concurrently or right after the above are finished:\r\n\r\n1. Create an overall framework for turnarounds and transformations...do you prefer McKinsey\'s over BCG\'s? Help on the overall structure of the course would be helpful.\r\n\r\n2. Read a Harvard Business Publishing case and be able to lay out in as few slides as possible:\r\nWhat’s behind the numbers? What’s really going on?\r\nStart with financials, running out of cash, EBITDA, revenue growth is stalling\r\nHad strategic meltdown, tried this, tried that\r\nLeadership challenge, come and go\r\nStrategic and Leadership breakdown\r\n\r\n3. Take a case and create study questions and a 1 or 2 slide explanation of takeaways/punchlines\r\n\r\nHappy to answer any and all questions!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~011fc8d202b8922781','no',7,'United States','Boston',800.000,'fixed',800.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'Fixed budget',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 15:57:22',NULL,6,3,NULL,133),
