(3952,'BigCommerce website build',3,'I am looking for an ecommerce developer that has experience in building BigCommerce websites.\r\n\r\nThe website will be fully briefed for you and you will need to follow the design template.\r\n\r\nThe website will contain 100-200 products, and must have the copy inputted into each product page etc.\r\n\r\nThe website will have various collections, that will distinguish different types of products.\r\n\r\nThe website must be able to link with our other shopping platforms, and feed in stock data sending data both ways. There will be an app for this that can be integrated.\r\n\r\nThe website must be able to take payments online\r\n\r\nPlease provide any examples of websites you\'ve built on BigCommerce and reply with the word \"carrots\" showing you\'ve read the whole message!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01188b003d1971c17a','no',7,'United States','Warrington',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'Fixed budget',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:17:27',NULL,6,3,NULL,133),
(3953,'New Company Branding & Logo Design',2,'We are currently investigating changing up our logo and overall branding of our company.\r\n\r\nThe project will be with a new logo and then expand into overall brand guidelines. Finally, we will be looking for a new website design using the new logo, colors and brand guidelines.\r\n\r\nWe are a tech firm that manages the website and website infrastructure for various-sized companies. We are looking for our brand to express a technical feel while being inviting to visitors who are not technical (slightly playful) and professional.\r\n\r\nWe are gravitating toward the red-eyed tree frog (images attached) as our company\'s mascot and using the colors that are on the frog as our company colors (blue, orange, green, red). We like bright colors as long as they are used in a way that compliments the items listed above.\r\n\r\nPlease apply if you have the skills and time to work on this project with us. We are motivated to get this done and you will work directly with us, getting immediate feedback for submitted work and/or ideas.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1600886029335334913?success','https://trello.com/b/eh32Y1Pm/task-list-arturo-digital/member/hasnain143',7,'United States','DOYLESTOWN',60.000,'perhour',60.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:21:57',NULL,6,3,NULL,123),
(3954,'Custom Infographic / Graphical Elements for Pitch Deck',2,'We are looking for a skilled illustrator to a couple of concepts to life in infographic form for a pitch deck related to high value art sales. Graphical style is to be determined, but we do have a clear idea of what the infographic needs to portray.\r\n\r\nPlease provide any samples of your work that might align with this project and let\'s chat!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/job/~01c1fd12aaeac1e367/apply/','Na',7,'United States','BROOKLYN',85.000,'perhour',60.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'Hourly',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:22:11',NULL,6,3,NULL,120),
(3955,'Install woo commerce shopping cart',3,'Current Setup: Products are created and exist on WooCommerce, a popular eCommerce\r\nsolution for WordPress. The Infusionsoft plugin is used as a payment gateway. Each product is\r\nspecified in this plugin as a recurring subscription with the cost and recurring time. When a\r\nproduct is purchased this information is sent to Infusionsoft, which processes the payment and\r\nstores the information for subscriptions. User rollout is handled internally. There is no automatic\r\nfunctionality for user creation or product delivery. It is assumed Infusionsoft handles billing\r\nreminders and/or recurring billing receipts.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nProposed Setup: Due to the complex nature of this change we would recommend using a development copy of the current website to test new functionality, keep the payment in test mode, and then move the development copy to the live platform. Backups should be made frequently.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 1: Add auth.net payment gateway. Client is using Authorize.net to process transactions in Infusionsoft and would like to continue that. This is not a native feature of WooCommerce so a plugin needs to be purchased. The cost is $80:\r\nhttps://woocommerce.com/products/authorize-net/?quid=5233a22e4d493de7c0b8be2c63018b45\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 2: Add and implement a subscription service. Woo doesn’t come with subscriptions built in, but they offer a plugin to do this work. The cost is $200 and can be seen here:\r\nhttps://woocommerce.com/products/woocommerce-subscriptions/\r\nAfter activating this plugin, we will go into each current product and enable the subscription plugin with the recurring cost/time and disable Infusionsoft. Additionally, we will need to create recurring billing reminders and/or recurring billing receipts as necessary since those seem to be currently handled on Infusionsoft.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 3: Move to live. With steps 1 and 2 done, we will switch the payment provider on the test site to auth.net and disable the Infusionsoft payment gateway, then make a test purchase. We should make a\r\nsecond purchase with a real credit card and then a refund, to make sure the gateway and\r\neverything else is working properly. When that is successful, we’ll make a backup of the current live website, and replace it with our test environment. At this point, all future sales will be processed on auth.net, and details are shown in WooCommerce for recurring billing.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 4: Migrate old users from Infusionsoft. The migration of old users can be tricky. There are import functions described here:\r\nhttps://woocommerce.com/document/migrating-subscribers-woocommerce-subscriptions/\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThere are several methods we can use here. If you don’t have many recurring orders and have\r\nthe staff do it, they could add these into the new system manually. If you have a significant amount of recurring orders, we can likely use an import tool here to do the work, which is a fairly involved process but is designed to complete this specific task successfully.\r\nhttps://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce-subscriptions-importer-exporter#csv-formatting-guide\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nProject Cost: We see this project as two separate projects; the implementation of the new gateway and subscription software and also the migration of user data from Infusionsoft. Based on the information found through the Discovery we offer an all-inclusive Project Cost of $825 (11 hours at $75/hour) for the setup and implementation of the plugin as stated in Steps 1, 2, and 3. For Step 4, we offer an all-inclusive Project Cost of $900 (12 hours at $75/hour) for the migration of users.\r\n\r\nPayment processing: Accept payments anywhere | Authorize.net\r\nAuthorize.net supports payment processing by helping small businesses accept credit card and eCheck payments online, in person, via mobile devices, and more.\r\nWooCommerce\r\nAuthorize.Net\r\nAuthorize.Net gateway with support for pre-orders and subscriptions.\r\nWooCommerce\r\nWooCommerce Subscriptions\r\nLet customers subscribe to your products or services and pay on a weekly, monthly or annual basis.\r\nWooCommerce\r\nMigrating Subscribers to WooCommerce Subscriptions\r\nIf you have an existing store using another eCommerce platform and selling subscription products, you may wish to migrate your customers from this system into WooCommerce and Subscriptions. Because a subscription is linked to a product, customer, payment gateway and potentially an order or orders, migrating a subscription can be very difficult. This guide will […]\r\n\r\nGitHub\r\nGitHub - woocommerce/woocommerce-subscriptions-importer-exporter: Import your subscribers to WooCommerce from a CSV. Or export your subscription data from WooCommerce to CSV.\r\nImport your subscribers to WooCommerce from a CSV. Or export your subscription data from WooCommerce to CSV. - GitHub - woocommerce/woocommerce-subscriptions-importer-exporter: Import your subscrib...','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1600887774846107649','NA',7,'United States','Savannah',1725.000,'fixed',1725.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:23:44',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
(3956,'Graphic Artist needed for rework/redesign of promotional brochure',2,'I am looking for someone to rework an educational flyer that will be used on our website as well as by handouts through our sales force. Need creative person to make this more appealing and catch people\'s attention. It is an existing piece that needs to be refreshed. I will need someone to start on this right away with little turnaround time. Attached is the existing document that we will need update/add some creativity to it.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~018b9f604449b5c01e','no',7,'United States','Santa Clara',200.000,'fixed',200.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'Fixed budget',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:25:37',NULL,6,3,NULL,133),
(3957,'Looking for an expert web designer with UI/UX knowledge',3,'Thank you for taking the time to consider our job posting!\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a web design expert who has extensive experience building, designing, and redesigning websites, as well as other online assets such as social media graphics, article graphics, banner ads, mini infographics, etc.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for an expert, or senior-level designer, who can act as a \"Creative Director\" and who doesn\'t need assistance to create publish-ready deliverables. We are looking to compensate an expert-level designer accordingly. We are only interested in independent contractors, not agencies.\r\n\r\nWe have an in-house web development team, so coding/development experience is not required (but please mention if you have this experience as it can be helpful).\r\n\r\nWe are specifically looking for someone who can take our design requests and come back with high-quality deliverables that require minimal revisions -- in other words, we want someone who doesn\'t need us to tell them which font sizes, layouts, formatting, etc, are \"best\" from a design perspective. This is not our area of expertise and we want to be able to rely on you for this!\r\n\r\nOur immediate need is to hire someone who can help us redesign several web pages for one of our online properties. However, we are most interested in someone who is interested in a long-term relationship, as we manage multiple web properties, all of which need consistent design and redesign work. If you are interested in long-term part-time or full-time work, please mention this in your application.\r\n\r\nIn your application, please include 2-3 examples of live websites that you designed yourself, as well as a selection of your best 5-10 graphics -- you can pick which graphics you want to include, as long as you consider them to be the best representation of your skills. You are welcome to include a full portfolio as well, but if you do, please be sure to specifically include or link to the samples requested above.\r\n\r\nPlease also include your level of experience on a scale of 1 to 10 with the following (experience with these is not required, it\'s just to give us an idea of which projects we could bring you on to):\r\n- Online magazines\r\n- Nutrition websites\r\n- Lawyer websites\r\n- Dental websites\r\n- Display ads\r\n- Infographics\r\n- Social media graphics\r\n- Mini Infographics\r\n- Animated graphics/gifs\r\n- Videos/motion graphics\r\n\r\nThank you for taking the time to consider our application. We look forward to hearing from you!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1600892122304278529','NA',7,'United States','Tempe',90.000,'Open this select menu',90.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:37:54',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
(3958,'Hype Video to Kick of Annual Sales Meeting',2,'A Video is needed to for BakeMark’s North America Sales Meeting (NASM) in\r\nJanuary 2023. The theme is “Undisputed Champtions, built to win, driven to lead” and it centers on basketball and the crossover themes between basketball and business/sales such as training, dedication, teamwork, and execution.\r\n\r\nThe Video will be shown at the beginning of our meeting to kick it off. Attendees should feel that 2023 NASM is about basketball and being the undisputed champions of our industry.\r\n\r\nMandatory Aspects of the Video\r\nName of meeting: “Undisputed Champions”\r\n○ Meeting tagline: “built to win, driven to lead.”\r\n○ Footage/clips of basketball moments (training, huddles, 3-pt shots, Slam Dunks, buzzer beater shots etc), clips should be of memorable moments.\r\n○ Meeting messaging: Planning, Training, Determination, Teamwork, Execution,\r\nPassion, Winning Spirit, Victory/Champions\r\n○ High-energy music','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~013c84041f68ad436d','no',7,'United States','Pico Rivera',2500.000,'fixed',2500.000,'2022-12-08',1,'2022-12-08',1,'Fixed budget',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-08 16:43:53',NULL,6,3,NULL,133),
