(4234,'Squarespace website customization',3,'Hello !\r\n\r\nI am working on developing a website for a new company that will launch next year.\r\n\r\nWe have a Squarespace template we are working from - but would like to explore some customization options and are looking for a great designer/developer who can help.\r\n\r\nWe have a few customization features already in mind to ask about difficulty / costs for, among them:\r\n\r\n1) Making a members area with extra services. If someone signs up and is logged in, we would like them to have access to a few extra services, like a gift wrapping for the products. How could this be added in an elegant way?\r\n\r\n2) Is it possible to change the checkout email signup to be for a members area rather than for newsletters?\r\n\r\nThank you!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1602417310393110529','NA',7,'United States','Paris',100.000,'perhour',100.000,'2022-12-12',1,'2022-12-12',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-12 21:38:17',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
(4235,'Mobile Web UI/UX Designer',6,'See the complete job description in the attached PDF file.\r\n\r\nMcMurray Hatchery (https://www.mcmurrayhatchery.com/index.html) is the premier chicken hatchery in the U.S. consumer market. We have been in business for 106 years, specializing in rare and Heritage chicken breeds. We are looking for a contract mobile web UI/UX designer to help transform our existing website into a modern, customer-friendly, mobile-first experience. While we are not looking for a rebrand of our website, we are open to a transformation incorporating best-in-class UI/UX design and content mechanisms.\r\n\r\nThe attached file is a collection of design ideas that we like. These are ideas only — not final designs that are to be implemented.\r\n\r\nFor this project we are seeking an experienced web UI/UX designer to create the design of our website in HTML, CSS and JavaScript. Once the entire design has been completed in HTML, our in-house programming staff will integrate that design into our custom web platform to create the finished product.\r\n\r\nThis will be a two-phase project. The project will begin with a trial, phase 1. Your initial bid for phase 1, outlined below, must include a portfolio showing a minimum of 5 previously designed websites and links to at least 2 sites that are currently active.\r\n\r\nPhase 1 is a fixed-price project where you will produce HTML designs for 2 of the most important pages in our website. These two pages are the primary templates for the bulk of the content on our website. Both of these pages will be used to dynamically generate most of our ecommerce content on the completed website. As such, the design must accommodate significant variations in content without any loss of functionality or degradation in visual appeal. See below for a list of content variations and other information.\r\n\r\nSingle Live Animal Product Page: https://www.mcmurrayhatchery.com/whiting_true_green.html\r\nVariations and Content Needed: product images and videos, descriptive text, pricing quantity breaks vary by product, design for sale pricing, quantity inputs for purchase as text entry or drop down varies by product, dynamic product stats/details under Quick Stats, dates available under Availability varies by product, Q&A entries, customer reviews, and other product recommendations. Eliminate ‘Add to Wish List’.\r\n\r\nGrid Category Shopping Page: https://www.mcmurrayhatchery.com/chicks.html\r\nVariations and Content Needed: pages fit dynamically to browser vs max width of current site, grid showing total number of products in each category, product name/title, product image (most are 1:1 ratio, square images, but allow for those that are not), filter categories on current website, pop-up window for Add to Cart option. You do not need to program the filtering logic for this page, but the Add to Cart pop-up must display properly on all devices. Include support for pages that have no filters/filter categories. Should include a mechanism for the customer to change the sort order — may be included on some pages and not on others.\r\n\r\nThere will be up to 4 rounds of revisions to your initial designs. We may hire more than one contractor for Phase 1. The initial designs from Phase 1 should be completed no more than 2 weeks from when the contract is awarded. Revision requests are to be completed within 2 days for each revision.\r\n\r\nThe most promising design from Phase 1 may be selected for Phase 2.\r\n\r\nSee attached PDF for deliverable specifications.\r\n\r\nImportant Design Notes\r\n- The red “Mega Menu” near the top of current site will be eliminated. See Reworked Nav/MMH-Redesign-TopNav.jpg in the attached file for a sample of navigation that we like better.\r\n-The site “branding” will remain the same - colors, fonts, logo, etc.\r\n- New CSS should be clean and new to this project while retaining existing branding. Do not base the new design on the existing site style sheets, although selected style items (fonts, colors, etc) should be copied from the current site.\r\n- The new design must easily accommodate being integrated into a template-based rendering system. Header, footer and any side navigation areas must be the same across all pages in the site. Conceptually this can be thought of as: each content page uses a server-side “include” to render the common elements and dynamically generates the main content of the page. All submitted designs must follow this pattern.\r\n- “Current page” styles must be controlled by CSS and the appropriate class must be assignable by client-side javascript or the server-side rendering component, or both.\r\n- All functionality from the current site must be supported by the new design\r\n- We respectfully ask that developer/designers do not bid on Phase 1 unless fully willing and able to accomplish Phase 2.\r\n- All designs, styles and images submitted will become the property of McMurray Hatchery.\r\n- Pop-ups and other positioning must be able to handle any state of any fixed and/or collapsible navigation items (header).','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1602418378036408321','NA',7,'United States','Princeton',2500.000,'fixed',2500.000,'2022-12-12',1,'2022-12-12',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-12 21:42:21',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
