(4349,'Graphic Designer for Mobile App',6,'Tenney110 is a leading Venture Build Studio with a multi-year track record of successfully launching and scaling innovative solutions to the world’s biggest problems. Now, we are building a new climate change EdTech venture with a mission to provide homeowners with useful, actionable, and easy to understand information about how, when and where climate change will affect their individual lives; and what they can do about it.\r\n\r\nOur new EdTech venture educates users without users feeling like they’re being educated; meeting users where they are at while providing them with fun and desirable experiences through gaming mediums.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for an experienced Graphics Designer to help us prototype a mobile-first city building game that revolves around climate change simulations based on peer-reviewed and award-winning climate models. While this is aimed to evolve into a full-time, leading role as the game(s) goes into development, the role is initially seeking part-time freelance candidates.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\r\n● Optimize scenes with rendering performance in mind\r\n● Work closely with the founders to translate the vision into actionable designs\r\n● Develop player experience ideas such as content, gameplay and progression systems\r\n● Evolve design decisions based on regular playtesting and audience feedback\r\n● Understanding of art fundamentals and design, including scene composition, lighting and post processing\r\n\r\nExpertise Required to Succeed\r\n● Comfortable working from sketch concepts and taking direction from reference and draw overs.\r\n● Expertised with tools and software for 2D illustration and 3D modeling\r\n● Working knowledge of the ideation and creation of UI design deliverables: Sitemaps, user flows, wireframes, lo-fi and hi-fi layouts, prototypes.\r\n● Experience creating rapid prototypes.\r\n\r\nBonus Points\r\n● Passion for climate change adaptation\r\n● Experience with builder games\r\n● Bachelor’s in Game Design.\r\n● Experience with EdTech gaming\r\n\r\nJob Details\r\n● Freelance.\r\n● Remote\r\n● Language: English\r\n\r\nThis is a remote contractor position which requires regular collaboration online during New York City-time work hours, attending relevant team meetings (e.g. daily scrum, retrospectives, sprint planning, and design meetings). Occasional calls during late evenings, nights, and early mornings should be expected for international meetings with outside contributors. The option to convert to full-time employee may be available to ideal candidates, depending on their location, skills, fit, project needs and schedule, and funding.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1602768301983625217','NA',7,'United States','Madison',100.000,'perhour',100.000,'2022-12-13',1,'2022-12-13',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2022-12-13 20:55:17',NULL,6,3,NULL,116),
