(5261,'Mobile Application Developer - Part Time, Less than 10 Hours Per Week',6,'We are looking for a part time mobile engineer to help us with our mobile application. The application is V1 complete but not yet launched. While we are working on store listings and video we are continuing to make improvements to the application prior to submission to the stores.\r\n\r\nHere are the technologies used:\r\n\r\n- NodeJs / React Native: We build and run our native iOS and Android applications using NodeJs and React Native\r\n- PHP / Laravel: We write our backend applications in PHP using the Laravel PHP framework\r\n- MySQL: We store all of our relational data in MySQL via AWS RDS\r\n- Redis: We store our application cache in Redis via AWS ElastiCache\r\n- Apache: We use apache to run our web servers to serve content\r\n- Docker: We build all applications as Docker images\r\n- Docker Compose: Our local environment uses docker compose to spin up the Swatched stack\r\n- Fire Cloud Messaging, We send push notifications through FCM\r\n- Twilio, We provide login via SMS auth verification using Twilio\'s SMS auth\r\n- AWS: We deploy our entire Stack for Development and Production using Amazon Web Services\r\n- CDK: We deploy our entire Stack infrastructure as code using the AWS CDK Python framework\r\n- ECS: We run our application services using Amazon\'s container management service\r\n- ECR: We store our application images in Amazon\'s container registry service\r\n- RDS: We create our MySQL database in Amazon\'s managed relational database service\r\n- VPC: We isolate our environments using Amazon\'s virtual network, including\r\n- Subnets- public and private, Route Tables, Internet Gateways, Security Groups, Network ACLs\r\n- EC2: We manage scaling our capacity and safety of our application using Amazon\'s virtual servers, including\r\n- Instances, Security Groups, Key Pairs, Auto Scaling Groups, Load Balancers\r\n- ElastiCache: We create our Redis cache in Amazon\'s managed caching service\r\n- Secrets Manager: We store our dynamically generated credentials using Amazon\'s secrets manager\r\n- EFS: We can dynamically scale our content storage system using Amazon\'s elastic file system\r\n- S3: We store content from EFS drives as backup storage on Amazon\'s simple storage service\r\n- Jira for Task Management.\r\n\r\nWe\'re looking for someone with experience that is just looking to grab a few hours a month in extra work. There may be weeks where there are no tasks, other weeks where there are 2 hours, other weeks where there are 5 hours. As we are pre-launch we\'re making real-time decisions on what changes and features to invest in and so the workload is dynamic.\r\n\r\nNon Technical Skills\r\nCommunication is critical. Frequent updates, verbose summaries. We\'re all remote and we generally work via Jira and email to we need clear written communication.\r\n\r\nAttention to detail is a must have. Setting Jira tickets to the right status, assigning them to the right person, including links and details, writing system documentation. Detail matters.\r\n\r\nFinally, timeliness. We\'re looking to reach out on a Monday and get a response on Tuesday which would include, barring questions about the task, an eta on number of hours and completion of the task. Related to this we want someone that can estimate effectively. We\'re much more interested in having the task done on estimated schedule rather than having the task done fast and getting a estimated completion date that is missed or number of hours that is too low.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested please include some information on your prior experience with these technologies for mobile applications and if you are comfortable with the Non Technical Skills expectations noted above.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1612847112115834880','-',7,'United States','West Henrietta',70.000,'perhour',63.000,'2023-01-10',1,'2023-01-10',0,'normal bid',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-10 16:25:46',NULL,12,3,NULL,151),
