(5343,'Email template design',20,'Hello,\r\n\r\nWe\'re a consulting company that helps recurring revenue businesses scale efficiently. I\'m seeking someone who\'s an expert in designing email templates in Hubspot that will be received/viewed properly on any platform.\r\n\r\nWhat I need your help with is creating four versions of an email template that will be used to send out monthly emails about our training course schedule for the following month. We\'ll get the first version right and do the other three immediately after.\r\n\r\nSee the following deck for an example of the current email template: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/15VZBimD8VJJItSIJIG4c2aO5DYpIZRoGZyTnkZrUQUA/edit?usp=sharing)\r\n- Slide 1 is the original design of our current email template.\r\n- Slide 2 is the actual current output when sent in email.\r\n\r\nHere is an example of our current newsletter template. It\'s more minimal and more aligns with our brand aesthetic which could be called a \"academic and modern\" style.\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1Qoaghq6ZuOva9E7mYjoerlTr3ojxnNGQ/view?usp=share_link\r\n\r\nThis is what our research papers look like, as another example of academic and modern:\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1hSe487YdbwHApT4ltly8BHiQADiwHTRg/view?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nOnto the template. There are details in the actual output that are lost, which make the template a bit messy.\r\n\r\nThese are the things that need to be streamlined based on the current actual email output:\r\n1) Hierarchy feels off. The header feels the same as each course. The blurb in the header should probably be moved to whitespace under the header to make it less busy.\r\n2) The rest of the email is not full width but for some reason the header is.\r\n3) The featured course needs to be more obviously different from the rest of the courses\r\n4) The badges don\'t look right in their current spot (they looked better in the original design but not sure if that\'s workable. I\'m open to ideas.)\r\n\r\nPlease design a few options, with at least one that is an iteration of the current design, and at least one that is completely redone.\r\n\r\nWe need to be able to easily edit and change the amount of courses that are displayed. Designs should be clean, minimal, academic, modern.\r\n\r\nThis is our brand guide where you can find hex codes for color, how to use our logo, etc.\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1OpSB1qnSdj7aR9iB5X4pAjuZHhA4LBUyGGx87Q5c2NA/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nSlides 3 and 6 below you can find our logo and course badge files:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1J86FBeKOqsOe8M1h-X1CpCVOSoUKdm9fVpUDqyNglFU/edit#slide=id.g13c2030e7c1_0_136\r\n\r\nThanks','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/job/~01ba27aa37f6e587b1/apply/','-',7,'United States','Menlo Park',200.000,'perhour',60.000,'2023-01-10',1,'2023-01-10',1,'Hourly',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-10 21:37:01',NULL,6,3,NULL,120),
