(5351,'SEM/SEO Coach',5,'I used to own a sizable company in which we used SEM and SEO in a big way (www.epicsysinc.com). At one time, I considered myself knowledgeable in these areas. Time has passed and Google/Digital Marketing has changed in some big ways.\r\n\r\nI have started another small company (www.accublend-inline.com). We manufacture inline liquid blending systems for food & beverage, consumer products and industrial chemical companies.\r\n\r\nMy knowledge of SEM and SEO is now rather dated. I am very capable to do most of the work in the areas outlined below, providing I have a for-hire coach that will help me accomplish that. I am looking for someone at the expert level with an hourly rate that matches those credentials. I am more than willing to pay good money for great direction and advice. I would be respectful of your time and schedule and would like to schedule brief \"direction-setting\" sessions on a regular basis at your T&M rate.\r\n\r\nI have a functional website (www.accublend-inline.com) and a Google AdWords campaign set up. I have ads, ad groups and keyword phrases set up also. I am sure they are not optimized.\r\n\r\nExamples of some of the things that I need help with are as follows:\r\n- Set up header tags\r\n- Set up metatags\r\n- Review website and optimize for SEO / SEM\r\n- Review AdWords campaign set up and optimize\r\n- Review Ad Groups and optimize\r\n- Review ads and optimize\r\n- Review keyword phrases and optimize\r\n- Review daily spend limits\r\n- Create sitemap\r\n- Set up different types of ads where pictures and sub-menus\r\ncome up in search results\r\n- Decide on whether I should do display ads\r\n- Improve quality score\r\n- Develop back links\r\n- Do A-B testing on ads, keywords, etc.\r\n- Etc.\r\n\r\nYou would find me capable easy to work with. Every relationship in my life is based on WIN-WIN. It has to benefit both parties or it is not a good log term partnership.\r\n\r\nPlease reply if this situation will work for y