(5363,'Animator for training videos',8,'Scope\r\n22. To build on the work delivered in Phase 1, we are seeking to commission a supplier to develop and produce 10 explainer videos to help key personnel within local government to build knowledge within cyber security. The videos should help cyber security and risk become a whole workforce issue instead of it being viewed as an issue just for IT services.\r\n23. To build on the work delivered in Phase 1, we are seeking to commission a supplier to develop and produce 10 explainer videos to help key personnel within local government to build knowledge within cyber security. The videos should help cyber security and risk become a whole workforce issue instead of it being viewed as an issue just for IT services.\r\n24. The objectives of Phase 2 are:\r\na. to provide local government chief executives, councillors, and senior directors with a better understanding of technical computer science concepts to aid with more informed decision-making when it comes to cyber risk\r\nb. to support the improvement of communication between technical and non-technical people working in local government in order to encourage more open conversations around cyber risk at senior levels within councils.\r\nc. To enhance understanding of cyber risks relating to local government through clear and engaging graphic videos, aligning to established guidance and principles, that is accessible to lay audiences.\r\n\r\n25. By aligning with and signposting to NCSC guidance, the videos will provide an engaging way to learn about complex technical cyber security processes, and help councils respond effectively to the challenge that cyber security poses to organisational resilience.\r\n\r\n26. By providing council staff with the information and tools to understand cyber security, we can help councils to:\r\n• understand the nature of the threat and the potential impact of a cyber incident, to ensure that the right governance arrangements are in place to manage risk.\r\n• understand current levels of cultural awareness, put in place steps to improve this.\r\n• drive cyber security up the agenda, promoting leadership, to ensure that plans to tackle cyber security are consistent, resilient, tested and understood.\r\n• Managing cyber risk is about having the right controls in place to prevent compromise, but also ensuring that organisations are prepared, so that in the event of an incident councils can continue to deliver essential services and impact is reduced. Part of this preparation needs to involve in-depth business continuity planning for each department/team in the event of a cyber incident.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1613181256728260609?success','-',7,'United States','Saffron Walden',50.000,'perhour',50.000,'2023-01-11',1,'2023-01-11',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-11 14:32:11',NULL,10,3,NULL,119),
