(5672,'Climate Campaign Brand Design & Development',2,'ACE RFP for CAMPAIGN BRANDING\r\nJanuary 2023\r\n\r\nJOB SCOPE + DESCRIPTION\r\nACE is looking for bids on brand development and design, including specific social examples, for two overarching, multi-year campaigns we are running - 1. stopping new fossil fuel infrastructure and 2. advancing bold climate policies. Launch date for the first campaign is March 3 (this is a hard deadline), and launch date for the second campaign is still to be determined.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone with experience in branding, including logos, iconography, typography, color schemes, unifying thematic elements, photo treatments, social media, and has a style that is fresh, snappy, trendy, and appealing to Gen Z.\r\n\r\nWe have an existing organizational brand kit with which we want to remain in alignment. The kit can provide inspiration and/or guidance. Each campaign brand should be both unique and fit within the look and feel of the larger ACE brand.\r\n\r\nWe may also request feedback on naming for the new campaigns. ACE takes responsibility for generating and picking top potential names, and may solicit input on what names are most winning.\r\n\r\nPriority project deliverables are logo, brand guide, graphics and specific social examples (how visuals could be used over social platforms or in other creative ways (see pages 33 onward in the kit). We will be using these digitally first and foremost, but will also use them on printed materials like posters, banners, signage, tshirts, stickers on a more limited basis.\r\n\r\nWe want to get started with someone ASAP in order to meet that hard deadline. The start date could vary so long as initial drafts, edits, and final approved product are ready to go public by or before March 3.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1613923320961118209?success','-',7,'United States','Boulder',60.000,'perhour',60.000,'2023-01-13',1,'2023-01-13',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-13 15:39:43',NULL,6,3,NULL,123),
