(6289,'Medical Content Needed Weekly with Bariatric Focus',37,'I am looking for writers knowledgeable about medical weight loss surgery. Topics range from dietary needs, mental health, general bariatric needs, pre-op needs, post-op needs, etc. Weight loss surgery patients need high-quality, evidence-based content, and we strive to give it to them in a non-clinical way.\r\n\r\nExperience in bariatrics is preferred (dietitian, nurse, bariatric patient, etc.) but optional if you are willing to research before writing the article.\r\n\r\nI am looking for 1000-1200 words per article and will provide topics, keywords, and general outlines for each. There is room for creative elaboration and the use of your expertise to deliver value to each article.\r\n\r\nStrong external links to published research are preferred when applicable. Some articles will be more conversational, with no links needed.\r\n\r\nBudget:\r\n$50 per article','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1616134565274361857','-',7,'United States','Washington',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-01-19',1,'2023-01-19',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-19 18:05:53',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(6290,'Explainer Video',8,'Below is the script for my explainer/screen-demo video. You will use some of my existing footage and make your own. I need a fixed price... the website is http://www.joinlistenup.com\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat is ListenUp?\r\n\r\nIt’s the first audio app that tells you stories about where you are… wherever you are. It’s completely free and can speak 22 languages.\r\n\r\nAs you walk, drive or bike around, the app narrates to you through headphones or Bluetooth. All you have to do is download the app, install it, give it the necessary permissions, connect your speakers [headphone, AirPod, Bluetooth in car] and press play. Then put your phone someplace safe [into pocket] and enjoy the stories [Listening while walking, biking, driving].\r\n\r\nThe app works with the usual controls of your device, to change volume, skip backwards and forwards through the tracks or to pause the audio. You can even press on your airpod touch control once to pause audio, twice to skip forward or three times to skip back. But pausing the audio in ListenUp does not prevent the next audio file from playing. Inside the app, you need to press pause once, then immediately a second time to stop the audio from automatically playing. If you don\'t it may just continue talking forever.\r\n\r\nListenUp needs many permissions to work well. It will ask for access to your activity, Bluetooth connectivity, and several other permissions, but most important is that it ALWAYS has your precise location to accurately direct your attention. But once you are done listening, you can simply swipe up twice to close the app.\r\n\r\nListenUp is the only app that also allows you to become part of the story by allowing you to share your suggestions and feedback. If you want to improve an existing story, you can do that through the speech-bubble icon, and then select from a list of common issues... type in text feedback, or record your voice comments using your microphone... You can scroll down to see or hear your comment and the comments others users have made.\r\n\r\nBut the best part of our community is that you can add your own stories! Just download the tour record app from within ListenUp or the app stores. It\'s another app we’ve developed to make storytelling even easier.\r\n\r\nOur community is constantly improving the app, so we welcome your feedback. Don\'t forget that ListenUp is multilingual. You can select your language when you install the app, and change your language later using the setting icon. So, if you are helping someone and the language barrier is a problem, just suggest that they get ListenUp to help them get the information they need.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1616135345974063105','-',7,'United States','Chicago',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-01-19',1,'2023-01-19',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-19 18:09:07',NULL,10,3,NULL,119),
