(6365,'Philosophy Cartoon Artwork - Gift Art',2,'Hi, Cristian! The budget is about $300-350, but could be more depending on how many faculty decide to chip in. To start with, I\'m paying for this myself. If people chip in and the budget exceeds that, I\'m happy to forward some extra money your way.This can be digital, but for the final printed piece, it should be done at a high enough resolution it can be perfectly printed and reproduced at 8.5 x 11. So for an image, this would include the teacher in question, Dr. John Gallam, and his black cat Charlene (a gag from his classes). Dr. Gallam would be at the center of the picture, with the philosophers Plato and St. Thomas Aquinas next to him, perhaps patting him on the back and smiling, or welcoming him. One of these philosophers can even be petting the cat! The rest of the gathering can include the philosophers Aristotle, Leibniz, Emmanuel Kant, and Rene Descartes. You\'ll need to grab images of these philosophers from Google - so I figured $300 for the cartoon + $50 for the hour or so you\'ll need to grab images from Google of these great thinkers.In the background, a festive sign should read \"Hall of Great Philosophers, Past and Present\" and another sign should say \"Welcome Dr. John Gallam!\" or as an alternative \"Our newest inductee: Dr. John Gallam\". Let me know what you think and if you\'re still interested, and if so, how we can get started and when a rough sketch/draft would be possible.Thanks again!','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2004860','-',7,'United States','-',350.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-01-19',1,'2023-01-19',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-19 22:33:35',NULL,3,1,NULL,136),
