(6717,'Woocommerce TAX rates',15,'We have two tax rates, 5% and 19% that are applied to different products.\r\n\r\n\r\nCase 1:\r\n\r\n\r\nIn the woo product settings, for product A tax is 5%. If it is bought by end customer tax should be 5%. If it is bought by company the tax should be 19%\r\n\r\n\r\nCase 2:\r\n\r\n\r\nIn the woo product settings, for product B tax is 19%. It doesn\'t matter who is buying the product (end customer or company, the tax should be 19%)\r\n\r\n\r\nFor both cases, the tax should be calculated at checkout and should be based on a dropdown menu (end customer or company). If we have both products added to cart we should have:\r\n\r\n\r\n1. If the user selects end customer, the tax for product A should be 5% and the tax for product B should be 19%\r\n\r\n\r\n2. If the user selects company, the tax for product A should be 19% and the tax fox product B should be 19%\r\n\r\n\r\nThe dropdown menu comes from an invoicing plugin that is already installed and working.\r\n\r\n\r\nFor all scenarios the shipping tax should be 19%.\r\n\r\n\r\nShoptimizer theme installed.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2007760','-',7,'United States','-',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-01-23',1,'2023-01-23',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-23 23:08:48',NULL,3,1,NULL,136),
