(6885,'Certificate border art design',2,'I would like to have a border made for a certificate I am creating. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe certificate is for a longevity award. In Freemasonry, when you reach your 25th, 50th, 55th, 60th, 65th, 70th, and 75th year you are recognized for your service to the craft and given an achievement award. This certificate will be given to the member along with his award when they reach the given milestone listed above.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nWhat I am looking for:\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n1. The file “1A.jpg” is the type of certificate border I would like to have created, but using Masonic symbols instead of ocean stuff. The work should be professional and not look cartooneish.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2. The certificate should be colorful, landscaped, and should fit on a regular size piece of paper that can be framed.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3. The bottom of the certificate frame should be something like you see in the bottom section seen in file 3A.jpg. Please add color to the design. On the left and right sides of the frame, I would like the pillar design shown in file “3A.jpg” the color of the pillars can be changed. It’s the design of the pillars that’s important not the color. Each pillar has a unique design at the top one is a map of the earth and the other a map of the stars. Just like the pillars are wrapped in flags in the example given in file “3E.jpg.” The left pillar should be wrapped in the American flag and the right pillar wrapped in the Arizona State flag (see 3F.png).\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n4. In place of the ship, the certificate should have the Masonic Square and Compass (see File 4A.jpg for an example, again the color doesn’t matter) with a ribbon draped across the top that goes from one side of the page to the other like the flag seen at the top of file “4B.jpg”. The ribbon itself should be dark blue and have the name of my lodge “Huachuca Lodge No. 53 F  AM.” Hanging off the ribbon should be a golden circle like the one seen in file “4C.png.” This circle is where I plan to put the years of service, so at the bottom of the golden circle, there should be the word “Years” like it is seen in the file “4D.jpg” with enough space for me to add the year above it (25, 50, etc..).  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5. The inside of the certificate should be blank; I will add in the words once I get the certificate border created.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n6. Our next award to be given out is on March 1, 2023. I hope to have the certificate completed by then.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n7. The design should not be given or sold to anyone else. This certificate should only be used by my masonic lodge.   \r\n\r\n\r\nI had a company design a certificate for me back in 2021 for 150 and was was not impressed with the work. I ended up redesigning the entire thing myself, using parts of their design. I am hoping to find a better designer here.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2002354','Certificate Border Design (Brian|Guru-TR)',7,'United States','abc',0.000,'fixed',0.000,'2023-01-14',1,'2023-01-24',1,'NA',1,NULL,NULL,1,'2023-01-24 22:47:56','2023-01-26 20:37:12',4,1,NULL,152),
