(6959,'Senior Graphic Designer',2,'The Senior Graphic Designer will play a pivotal role in driving the visual direction of the Smith Co. Distributing’s family of brands. This is an exciting opportunity for a seasoned designer who’s looking to take their creative career to the next level.\r\n\r\nYou will be the creative lead on fast paced large-scale brand initiatives across a diverse product line including but not limited to knives, canabis, tecnology, sunglasses, flags, koozies, coffee, and stickers.  This position will work deep in the details of producing creative deliverables (Art, packaging, catalogs, marketing materials, etc...) while also overseeing junior design staff and cross-departmental oversight of brand applications. This is a full time, remote, and salaried position, earning between $750-$1100 monthly depending on experience.  This position reports to the Marketing / Creative Director and Production Director.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Conceptualize and develop graphic solutions from concept to delivery to support product development, marketing and brand needs\r\n• Develops and maintains graphic guidelines..\r\n• Creates custom logos, graphics, layouts and other design solutions optimized for digital and print channels.\r\n• Provides written, verbal, and visual input for Development, Retail, and Brand teams\r\n• Ability to manage multiple projects at once\r\n• Provide critique and mentorship to help develop junior staff\r\n• Responsible for creating custom logos, graphics, and layouts\r\n• Verbally present graphic concepts in small team settings\r\n• Ensure proper delivery of works to all departments\r\n\r\nSkills and Qualifications:\r\n• 4+ years of professional design experience required\r\n• Advanced knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite\r\n• Strong portfolio showcasing expertise of branding, typography, layout, and illustration skills across digital and print.\r\n• Expert knowledge of digital and print design requirements.\r\n• Ability to perform at a high level while juggling multiple projects\r\n• Ability to lead junior Design staff.\r\n• Must be highly Self Driven / Motivated.\r\n• Strong understanding of American pop culture, trends, etc...\r\n• Photography, video, animation, copywriting, 3d rendering and other multi-media experience is a nice bonus.\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout Smith Co. Distributing:\r\nSmith Co. Distributing and our family of brands pride ourselves in ensuring an effortless ordering process, guaranteed peace of mind with your purchase decision, personable customer service, timely delivery, quick sell-through, high margins, and less than 1% rate of return.  \r\n\r\nFounded in 2011 from what started as a few vans and a 2 car garage exclusively servicing Northwest Ohio, has grown into a dedicated global staff, working from our ever-growing warehouse in Northwest Ohio, timely delivering millions of products annually with the help of our trusted distribution partners.   \r\n\r\nSmith C. Distributing is the United States #1 source for high-quality tech accessories and impulse merchandise.  We manufacture, import and distribute travel accessories, cell phone chargers, 10-foot charging cables, bluetooth earphones, bluetooth speakers, stickers, socks, knives, sunglasses, metal signs and more.\r\n\r\nTimeline:\r\nAccepting Applications: Jan 25 - Feb 10\r\nReviewing Applications & Interviewing: Feb 13 - 28\r\nProjected Start Date: March 1, 2023','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0191282015def4a7d5','-',7,'United States','Liberty Center',45.000,'perhour',45.000,'2023-01-25',1,'2023-01-25',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-25 17:06:03',NULL,8,3,NULL,146),
(6960,'Webflow development 7/8 pages',3,'We are a digital agency based in France.\r\nWe are looking for a talented Webflow developer to work with on this project (and hopefully many more).\r\n\r\nThe project:\r\nThe Figma prototype of the project is very detailed, the mobile version is already designed as well. Inside the Figma is: (the complete style guide, the desktop and mobile version, the components and the visual elements.) The objective is to create all the pages present on the Figma, so 8 page without counting the legal notice and privacy policy. Many sections are reused on different pages, so it is a plus in terms of dev time.\r\n\r\nOur responsive expectations & effects:\r\n- Apparition effect of éléments in the navigation of the website (opacity effect & move in)\r\n- The website must absolutely respect the design of the models on desktop and mobile.\r\n- Some floating effect on graphic elements but nothing complicated.\r\n- Two CMS sections : 1 review section & 1 press section.\r\n\r\nSelection criteria:\r\n- Location = If you are based in Asia 5 to 8h after CEST it\'s a plus to allow us to work asynchronously\r\n- Please provide 3-5 examples of Webflow projects and explain quickly which method you use to name your classes. (We have a preference for websites coded in Em using the wizardry method but are open to hear about your specific process)\r\n\r\nMission: please keep in mind that we might have up to 3 revisions regarding small details of the dev.\r\n\r\nUpon request, I will send :\r\n- A quick screen recording explaining the project\r\n- the Figma file\r\n- The webflow template link\r\n-The access of client Webflow account ( IMPORTANT : Create new project and don’t touch to actual website in the dashboard !!!!)','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1618294378095321089?success','-',7,'United States','Paris',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-01-25',1,'2023-01-25',0,'Fix price project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-25 17:08:51',NULL,5,3,NULL,128),
