(6982,'eComm Optimized Design for Conversion, Speed, and Compatibility',4,'We are seeking an experienced designer to help us create an engaging yet simple and fluid design for our new Woocommerce site.\r\n\r\nYou can either edit a premium theme ,using elementor or create something completely unique\r\n\r\nThe topic is similar to grasscity.com,dankstop.com,cannabox.com\r\n\r\nWe want the design to be fast loading, cross-browser compatible, and optimized for conversions.\r\n\r\nIf you have the skills and enthusiasm to be part of an exciting project, then this could be for you!\r\n\r\nwe really mainly want to focus on the homepage and shop page design.\r\n\r\nhomepage needs to be engaging.\r\n\r\nshop/category page just need to be technically configured to provide category sorting and category page needs the same with highlights of the catgory included on the page\r\n\r\nso its designing homepage\r\nand configuring the category/shop pages.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1618329795588247553','-',7,'United States','El Paso',1000.000,'fixed',1000.000,'2023-01-25',1,'2023-01-25',1,'Fixed',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-25 19:35:10',NULL,5,3,NULL,132),
(6983,'Video editor needed to make animated explainer video',8,'The Behavioral Insights Team worked with a client to launch a large virtual event with participants from around the world. Participants met on a platform similar to Zoom and discussed complex issues, before ultimately voting on possible proposals to address the issues.\r\n\r\nWe are looking to rapidly produce two videos.\r\n- The first video will provide context for the event, using animation to bring a narrator’s voiceover to life.\r\n- The second video will bring to life what happened during the event, using animation, editing, and screen-recorded clips.\r\n\r\nThe videos are intended to be social-media friendly, which is why we’re aiming to keep them short. Captions will need to be added for both videos.\r\n\r\nProject descriptions\r\nVideo 1\r\n- Timeframe: ASAP (Aiming for first draft by Feb 6; completed by Feb 17)\r\n- Length: 1.25–2.5 minutes long (still clarifying with client, but might be two 1-minute videos)\r\n- Contents: This video is focused on the context behind why this event occurred.\r\nWe will provide a script for the video and the recorded voiceover. We are looking for someone who can bring the words to life through simple animation, music, and other editing techniques. If the video length allows for it, we may also ask for some clips from the event to be interspersed throughout the video. We will provide any such clips.\r\n\r\nHere’s an example of the quality of animation we’re looking for:\r\nhttps://www.powtoon.com/video-template/5-tips-for-better-work-life-balance\r\n- Audience and media format: The audience is firstly the client, and then second the general public (once the client approves the video). The client would like to be able to share this via social media platforms (e.g., instagram reels), though we would also like to embed it within blog posts.\r\n- Iterations & Review: We anticipate needing 3-4 iterations before the video is finalized. We will be the point of contact providing you with feedback, both from our team and from our client who is the final judge over whether the video is ready.\r\n\r\n\r\nVideo 2\r\n- Timeframe: TBD; Goal is to have something final by the end of March\r\n- Length: 1–1.5 minutes long\r\n- Contents: This video will focus on what happened during the event.\r\nThe primary piece of content for this video will be screen-recorded clips from the event itself. We want to attempt to capture diversity of perspectives that were voiced during the event, and the global scale of the event, through our use of clips. We need someone who can stitch together clips with smooth transitions, add captions, music, and editing, and produce a video that conveys the significance of the event.\r\n\r\nWe will provide our preferred clips, but the video editor will need to choose among them, cut them down to length, and order them appropriately. Our video will include non-English speakers. We can provide the translated text for these speakers.\r\n\r\nHere’s an example of a video that uses clips similar to what we will provide you with, and highlights the substance of the conversations among lay participants. Ours should be shorter than this:\r\nAmerica in One Room: Deliberative Poll : https://youtu.be/RkchIiA-t0M\r\n- Audience: This audience is the same as for video 1.\r\n- Iterations & Review: We anticipate needing 3-4 iterations before the video is finalized. We will be the point of contact providing you with feedback, both from our team and from our client who is the final judge over whether the video is ready.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1618331335370350593?success','-',7,'United States','Brooklyn',5000.000,'fixed',6000.000,'2023-01-25',1,'2023-01-25',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-25 19:36:02',NULL,6,3,NULL,123),
