(7299,'30 second demo/comparison of pool filter',2,'Our filter is made of a new technology vs traditional pool filtration. It filters smaller/finer particles than traditional pleated water filters. I\'d like to show a short features/benefits/comparison video of: \r\n\r\n    particles being trapped in the new filter media (old media stops particles as small as 10-15 microns, new media stops particles as small as 3-5 microns), leaving cleaner, clearer water. I also have a magnified image of the new media under the microscope... could demonstrate this way showing particles getting trapped. \r\n    Old filters must be washed monthly (with a water hose); new filters = no washing\r\n    Made in USA\r\n    Company logo\r\n    100% recyclable (icon, and/or showing the filter being tossed in recycle bin)\r\n\r\nIn the attachments found here, the blue filter is the new technology (\"meltblown\" fibers) and the pleated filters are traditional technology (on the market for 50+ years).\r\nAttachments','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2010197','-',7,'United States','abc',0.000,'fixed',0.000,'2023-01-27',1,'2023-01-27',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-27 20:20:15',NULL,4,1,NULL,152),
