(7363,'Turn Logo Into Short Style Guide',2,'Hi,\r\nWe\'re a small agency trying to get through a little design pileup and are looking for someone with strong visual identity and style guide experience to flesh out a short (roughly 3 to 5 page) style guide from an existing logo.\r\n\r\nThis needs to proceed quickly because we\'ve got three projects piled up behind it, including website, video, and pitch deck - all of which are coming due. To do it, you will work directly with the company\'s CEO and Creative Director, but we are hoping for a strong first draft.\r\n\r\nSections at this point include\r\n\r\n- Logo - Brand & Wordmark (this is done, but it will be included) including treatment and usage\r\n\r\n- Color Palate (This is actually already decided, but we\'ll need proportions, primary/secondary/tertiary, et al.\r\n\r\n- Font Stack (Again, already have the primary characters, but will need some expansion).\r\n\r\n- Illustrative Style - This one is a little tricky because we\'ll need to develop some style guidelines for illustration around device. May need some infographic style examples as well.\r\n\r\n- Patterns - Need some basic patters to help convey the devices general style and can be used to fill in the gaps on pitch decks, website, etc.\r\n\r\n- Image Selection & Treatment - Just need to ads some example images that show the type of photography, lighting, etc we use.\r\n\r\n- Video Treatment - About the same as video. Don\'t want to go too deep into this for right now, but some basic guidelines will be helpful.\r\n\r\nWe have a brand brief, but here\'s a short synopsis: The product is an integrated AI/Robotics platform meant for SMBs. The design needs to be business-facing. It shouldn\'t be austere, maintaining some friendliness, but will need to convey a cutting edge piece of machinery, not a children\'s toy. It should feel technology based, but not kitschy. It needs to feel professional, yet accessible.\r\n\r\nEmphasis, we don\'t have the bandwidth to hold someone\'s hand through this process and you will need to offer your own creative ideas. Please only apply if you strong experience in creating style guides and brand books and developing full guides from minimal input. Business illustration experience would also be hugely helpful.\r\n\r\nWe have plenty of style guides/brand books we can point to as examples of our work to give you a sense of our process.\r\n\r\nFinally, we work pretty exclusively in Figma (It\'s just the easiest, collaboratively speaking). Please only apply if you are an ace using the platform, have your own subscription.\r\n\r\nThanks so much and we look forward to working with you!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01a774fbfc5b6c7793','-',7,'United States','Seattle',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-01-30',1,'2023-01-30',1,'Fixed',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-30 15:04:24',NULL,5,3,NULL,133),
