(7586,'Looking for an illustrator with an eye for dark comedy to create 4 posters',2,'I\'m looking to create 4 posters to illustrate 4 scenarios a rogue landlord might deliberately manipulate to take advantage of an unsuspecting tenant.\r\n\r\nI would quite like each poster to be stylistically different to illustrate how this is a global reality. 1 could be japanese in style, another pop art, another a simple line drawing... etc I am not wedded to this idea. It depends on who comes forward.\r\n\r\nThese are business scenarios. The best characters to illustrate this would be rich landlord and desperate shopkeeper.\r\n\r\nThe characters can be hugely exaggerated to highlight the unfairness of the situation i.e. an angry, horned, greedy landlord sitting on piles of money and a weak, childlike, naive shopkeeper using his last buck to try and build a small business.\r\n\r\nI can support with rough sketches showing how these might be laid out, or we can discuss via email / zoom.\r\n\r\nHere we go...\r\n\r\nOpening Scenario and Poster 1\r\n\r\nBackground: Landlord has convinced a new tenant to spend money on a shop business and has promised a 5 year lease in return.\r\n\r\nPoster: The tenant keeps spending money and working on the business and the landlord keeps providing leases which are unsignable (no detail / back of a fag packet and literally nowhere to sign).\r\n\r\n**a good way to look at this might be an over powering landlord figure holding a fag packet or scrappy piece of paper aggressively out toward the tenant with \'sign here\' falling off the bottom while the tenant works away in the corner or hands money back to the landlord regardless of the scrappy nature of the lease document - in hope**\r\n\r\nConnected Scenario and Poster 2\r\n\r\nBackground: During this period the landlord fails to provide tenant with invoices for services (electricity, water etc) in spite of the tenant asking for them.\r\n\r\nPoster: After i.e. 6 months the landlord threatens to evict the tenant for non-payment of invoices even though the tenant couldn\'t possibly have paid them because they haven\'t been supplied.\r\n\r\n**a good way to look at this might be an over powering landlord figure hiding invoices behind his back demanding payment for them and threatening eviction - he could be wearing a t-shirt with a landlord / bailiff motif illustrating the control he has asserted. It would be important for the tenant to be seen to be visibly asking to see the invoices so they can be paid - tricky to show this well, i think**\r\n\r\nConnected Scenario and Poster 3\r\n\r\nBackground: The tenant tries to renegotiate the terms of the lease (yet to be supplied)  due to the increased uncertainty over the landlords intentions.\r\n\r\nPoster: The landlord kicks the tenant out of the shop premises for reneging on the deal AND non payment of invoices. The landlord has gas-lighted the tenant because it was the landlord who reneged on the original deal (offering a 5 year lease in return for the tenant\'s investment in the shop) and the landlord who withheld the invoices.\r\n\r\n**very tricky to illustrate but the first two scenarios might supply clues on how to proceed**\r\n\r\nConnected Scenario and Poster 4\r\n\r\nBackground: The tenant is now out of the way and the landlord has a business to build on.\r\n\r\nPoster: The landlord has taken over the shop business, shouting about how awful the tenant has been. And profits accordingly.\r\n\r\n**this is probably easiest to illustrate, tenant peering through window at a greedy landlord sat behind a shop counter**\r\n\r\nI am considering one illustrator to create them all. As well as one artist per poster.\r\n\r\nI will use these as standalone posters (a3 in size please) and I would also then create a quadriptych (all 4 on a3) in house to bring the whole story together.\r\n\r\nThe aim is to illustrate effectively the dangers of the power imbalance between landlord and tenant in a business and some common pitfalls to proceeding in anything without a signed contract.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01aadb54fa1d505c81','-',7,'United States','hope',50.000,'perhour',45.000,'2023-01-31',1,'2023-01-31',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-31 15:07:45',NULL,6,3,NULL,125),
