(7660,'Fiction Book Cover Design',2,'Title:\r\n\r\nThe Greater Good\r\nVolume One\r\n\r\nDescription:\r\n\r\nThe United States of America no longer exists as one country. Due to a series of dramatic events, including political unrest and violence, on July 4, 2026, exactly 250 years after the Declaration of Independence was published, the country splits in two. Differentiating it from the Civil War of the 1860’s, the split was negotiated and amicable among both sides.\r\n\r\nPolitical parties and power shifted from Democrats and Republicans and people aligned themselves under new banners of Red and Blue. The Blues created a new socialist economy in the North, the Reds maintaining the existing economy in the South.\r\n\r\nBoth countries, while having intentions to serve the greater good, find themselves creating the totalitarian hells that their opposition always warned of, where individual liberty is crushed; the people of the North unable to see their own slavery and the people of the South recognizing it all-too-well, each having their own limitations as to why they’re unable to do anything about their situations.\r\n\r\nThe protagonist of the story, Thomas, a very intelligent and highly educated man in his mid-20’s was born after the countries split and socialism was all he ever knew. After a run-in with the police which lands him in the Northern version of jail, he has a life-altering experience in which he finds himself with a group of people who tell him the real history of the downfall of America. The one that very few people know. Thomas proceeds to learn the truth about all the things going on behind the scenes in both countries, which horrify him, but he has a very hard time believing them and, when he leaves the company of the group, remains unsure of the groups intentions and the validity of their stories.\r\n\r\nWhat he does believe, though, is that war is imminent. The two countries can no longer peaceably exist on the same continent and Thomas must make a decision if, using his new knowledge, he should try and do anything about it or, do as he always did; trust the State to make the right decision for him and others.\r\n\r\nThe rest of the story occurs in Volume 2.\r\n\r\nDesign elements:\r\n\r\nI definitely want to incorporate the colors red and blue. Outside of that, I’m open to ideas. Front, back, and spine and I’d like the front to double as an ebook cover.\r\n\r\nLicensing:\r\n\r\nI want to own the artwork and want the source files.\r\n\r\nFee and turnaround time:\r\n\r\nI prefer a flat-rate, so please quote that. I’d like the turnaround time to be no more than 2-3 weeks.\r\n\r\nFinally:\r\n\r\nI want to hire whoever has the best idea. In your proposal, please include some of your work as well as a quick-pitch. You don’t have to give away much. Just enough so that I understand whether or not you “get” what I need and what would be ideal for the cover.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1620502991357493249?success','-',7,'United States','Athens',100.000,'perhour',100.000,'2023-01-31',1,'2023-01-31',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-01-31 19:29:34',NULL,9,3,NULL,140),
