(8357,'Many Lottie Animation for Child Health Mobile App',8,'This project is for a medical device/ support startup that offers a mobile application solution to children who experience seizures. This project includes a strict NDA agreement (for me), so without disrupting specific details about the app, a child uses the app so their doctor can better understand how to prescribe and reference an approach to their unique situation.\r\n\r\nThe app’s experience is designed for quick, simple usage. While the patient is prepping for a response within the app, we showcase a character to help soften and guide the child through the process. When the human participates in exercises needed to produce a response, they are presented with a video/ animation of the character going on a bike stroll through many different backgrounds. Our project starts here; we are responsible for bringing the static items to life.\r\n\r\nAll assets and designs are centered around one particular illustration collection that we will need to continue to use as we design all of the motion elements required for this outcome. Due to the nature of the application’s usage, we will need to keep the secondary motion items to a minimum. The client has specifically requested that we try to incorporate background motion items, like a cloud or animal moving along the path while the main character continues on the trail. We also want to ensure that the character styles through facial expressions, as if they are coming to life during this part of the app’s process.\r\n\r\nAs you might have already assumed, the need to incorporate motion files into an app is a challenge. Therefore, we will need the final render within a Lottie file format. We will also need to ensure that the file size is on the lower end to avoid uploading issues.\r\n\r\nI have uploaded and outlined all parts of the video and each different background within the Figma file that I will share after selecting a hire. Still, screenshots of the character and a sample background are included below for your reference.\r\n\r\n***\r\nI started this project with another freelancer who was unwilling to support the continuation of the project. Therefore, I have one primary example that my client approved, which we will use to direct the following 3 animations we will complete together. In total, you will produce 4 animations, all consisting of the same art and design style and the same file format.\r\n***\r\n\r\nWe have roughly a 2 to 4-week timeline to complete and revise any parts of the animations before the developers must include the asset for the client’s alpha launch.\r\n\r\nThank you for taking the time to review my post! Please feel free to message me with any questions.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1622620111601958913','-',7,'United States','Raleigh',70.000,'perhour',70.000,'2023-02-06',1,'2023-02-06',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-06 15:37:18',NULL,10,3,NULL,119),
(8358,'Packaging graphic designer for long term cooperation',2,'We are looking for a creative packaging designer for our organic products range. We constantly launch new products and there is always something to work - creating new designs, modifying some text on some labels.\r\nOur products are organic certified foods and the packaging is doypacks, carton tubes, j …','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1622620863899734017?success','-',7,'United States','Oradea',40.000,'perhour',40.000,'2023-02-06',1,'2023-02-06',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-06 15:39:44',NULL,9,3,NULL,140),
(8359,'Children\'s Book Illustration',2,'Looking for an experienced children’s book illustrator to create the character and illustrations for this first book (32-page children’s picture book) in a series, The Amazing True Story of Bruce the Flying Doodle Dog. After reviewing your samples, I will likely want to have a sample treatment of the character, probably via the design of the cover to make sure we are a good fit before doing the whole book.\r\n\r\nI have attached a PDF (Illustrations Guide) with the story and descriptions of what I envision each page to be. I am open to alternatives and would love creative changes to what I have described, but wanted to have this down for scoping for estimate and give you what I am thinking in general.\r\n\r\nPlease provide info about your process, including what you create in. I would like to get the original layered build files (Illustrator, photoshop, etc.). I plan to create a website for marketing and will want to use elements from the book for that as well as potentially creating interactive animations.\r\n\r\nI am new to children’s book production, so would also love to have someone with experience to guide me a bit on creating the book. I am a graphic designer, animator and have had my own media production company, so I know my way around the Adobe creative suite and can layout the book, but guidance on the children’s book industry, including self-publishing options is a big plus.\r\n\r\nI look forward to seeing your portfolio!\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nBrian','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01dd31c5b6d1aba0da','-',7,'United States','Cincinnati',2500.000,'fixed',2500.000,'2023-02-06',1,'2023-02-06',1,'Fixed',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-06 15:39:54',NULL,7,3,NULL,133),
