(8416,'Rebrand / New Brand Identity',2,'Looking to have some help rebranding our logo and stuff into something cohesive and more professional.\r\n\r\nAttached are all the logos associated with our brand. Packible Tools is the company name and the Packible logo is our main brand logo. This logo has good recognition with our customers and so I want to preserve it in the sense that it it still recognizable, but redo it in such a way that it can be integrated into a more cohesive big picture branding strategy.\r\n\r\nAll the other logos attached are branding of individual product lines. As you can tell they have a theme. A theme we have become known for.\r\n\r\nOur space is the industrial, contractors, trades people and tools sort of space. Think major brands such as DeWalt Milwaukee Tool or Craftsman.\r\n\r\nI am open to rebranding some of those products in a totally different fashion if the opinion is those names logos or branding are not the way to go moving forward. But I have had good success with my branding thus far, its unique and stands out and many if not most of our customers know the product line brands by name and our name has become synonymous with entire product categories. Think Kleenex association with tissue. Many people call the item by its brand. Our Joey and Level Lizard items are examples of that same thing in our space.\r\n\r\nI would basically like to rebrand to something more simple/minimalist that maintains an element or captures the industrial and heavy duty nature of our product.\r\n\r\nI want to go with more simple colors. Possibly all black. Greys, black and blues... I am open on this and want professional advice on how to cohesively tie this all together while communicating to our customers better the heavy duty tool nature of the brand while making sure it is still recognizable after the makeover to not loose any business.\r\n\r\nOne other reason for this rebranding is to try and find ways to make our logo more recognizable on social media when put into those tiny little circles. The nature of our long rectangular logo does not lend itself well to alot of those modern social media branding challenges.\r\n\r\nEnd result of this i would like to have a brand kit with all the fonts, logos, colors, etc... Needed for future branding activities. The main logo, Packible, being the spot lite and then finding a way to cohesively tie together my other artwork for the product lines into that image.\r\n\r\nOne thought I had to that end was to turn all logos into black and white line work type versions of their current form to tie them more together. Although I do like having some color and pop to them. But they just are not 100% the profesional look I want to have going forward as the business matures.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1622656060672245761','-',7,'United States','na',40.000,'perhour',40.000,'2023-02-06',1,'2023-02-06',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-06 17:59:54',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
