(9460,'Creating a website',3,'I would like to create a website for my company which is in fintech. My firm is far from being operational though.\r\n\r\nI have a couple of questions, as I am new to this:\r\n\r\n1) How does the process typically work? I understand you are both skilled on the creative side, i.e., thinking about how a website should look, but also on the technological side, i.e., actually creating the website. I have some ideas about the content of the site, but a lot still needs to be figured out.\r\n\r\n2) Once the website is created, how difficult/easy will it be for me (or someone else) to make edits to it? I have done a bit of work myself using Wix, but I am really a beginner. The website will obviously need to evolve over time.\r\n\r\n3) Given that my firm is still far from operational (we need government approval first), I am wondering if it makes sense to create a \"simple\", or \"prototype\" version first, and then upgrade it to something more sophisticated later on. I would like the website to eventually look as nice as possible, as this is important for getting people interested in my firm. Or, would you say that it makes more sense financially to go straight to the sophisticated version, to avoid double work?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nGideon Magnus','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1625145981585850369','-',7,'United States','New York',40.000,'perhour',40.000,'2023-02-13',1,'2023-02-13',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-13 14:53:48',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
