(9495,'Medical Billing Specialist',21,'So, what will you do as our AR Denial Specialist\r\nThis position is responsible for collecting insurance payer balances. The duties include but are not limited to timely follow-up on accounts, reviewing documentation, work denials and rejections, verify ERAs, post payer payments, manage recoups and refunds, work special projects as needed.\r\nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES:\r\n-Follow-up on open balances listed on monthly AR and Payer Follow-up reports\r\n-Review and update patient demographics and payer information as necessary for\r\ncompletion of claims payment\r\n-Responsible for transferring balances and submitting claims\r\n-Generate correspondence to payers such as appeals, reconsiderations and payments\r\n-Promptly identify any errors or other issues in claims processing\r\n-Effectively following up on any unpaid balances\r\n-Expeditiously bringing any remaining balance to resolution\r\n-Meet quality assurance and productivity standards by identifying and reconciling\r\ninsurance balance accounts\r\n-Review explanations of benefits details on denials. Documentation and notate\r\naccounts on collection activity to perform account resolution\r\n-Communicate with insurance payer representatives, patients, and other staff to ensure\r\ntimely and accurate resolution of account transactions.\r\n-Must be able to prioritize and work independently\r\n-Be able to understand the revenue cycle process and how it relates to payers and\r\npatients\r\n-Be able to review claims and understand the denial process and what is required to\r\nwork a denial to obtain payment for Better Health\r\n\r\nRegular and reliable attendance required working schedule open between 7a - 6p EST\r\nKPIs measured - work 35-50 claims daily.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1625164149502210049','-',7,'United States','-',8.000,'perhour',8.000,'2023-02-13',1,'2023-02-13',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-13 16:06:46',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(9496,'Develop & Write a Business Proposal',11,'Develop a comprehensive business proposal for presentation to a foreign corporate client. The proposal would build on our corporate and network capacity to concept, design, plan, engineer, and execute construction, commissioning, and operations of a modular refinery project.\r\nThe proposal would incorporate our corporate and network partners experience, real time market factors that impact the availability of qualified persons and timetables. More details will be discussed upon short listing and interviewing candidate to ensure that the candidate is up to the task after learning more details about the available content and the work scope objective.\r\nThe first task would be preparation of the Business Plan’s table of content following the interview to ensure that there is a mutual agreement on the completeness of content that is required for a compelling proposal.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~014e5c9aaf678ae2e0','-',7,'United States','Stone Mountain',150.000,'perhour',40.000,'2023-02-13',1,'2023-02-13',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-13 16:10:29',NULL,8,3,NULL,146),
(9497,'PowerPoint expert needed for branded internal document.',2,'I work for an insurance brand that have 3 Presentations (PPTX) documents that need to be combined, re-designed, and made easy to edit across a variety of teams and team members. The teams need templates which help them drop data into but, where needed, there’s visual cues or narrative written to direct the conversation. We need templates of different ways for information to be presented which gives us options that are easy to populate when we are creating the packs.\r\n\r\nThe combined document must include:\r\n• Standard approach to agendas, action tracking and minutes (I’ve designed some templates which I hope would then be easy to copy and paste into the presentation packs as required. They give the detail I’m looking for some of the logs to collect and display in meetings e.g. actions also remind committee members of the rationale behind them)\r\n• Gantt charts\r\n• Tables with data but clear RAG ratings, some where you can easily show the moving performance since last meeting and over a longer period of time\r\n• Project tracking slides\r\n• Ways of demonstrating workloads by department/topic against calendar month and giving a visual indication of level of workload it is\r\n\r\nI have the documents as they are, that need to be combined, along with their brand book for reference. The key is accessibility, so any team member can use the documents inputting data in a straightforward yet branded (well-designed/ visually pleasing) way.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1625165904289169409?success','-',7,'United States','Oxfordshire',300.000,'Open this select menu',300.000,'2023-02-13',1,'2023-02-13',1,'fix',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-13 16:13:40',NULL,10,3,NULL,139),
