(9609,'Build website',3,'We are wanting to build a web page on our domain setup on GoDaddy for the auction of our sailboat that was materially damaged by a yard in Grenada. This webpage we want to include the three survey reports we have (original, first damage report and second damage report). We also want to have the story of the boat and the story of what happened to our boat on this website with an auction set up for bids. Included on this website will be photos of the boat before and of it currently along with a list of systems and details of the vessel. We want to have the website to be user friendly, easy to navigate and have a place where serious buyers are required to register to bid on the boat. Along with this being an auction of our vessel we are wanting this to be a PR related website showing the negligence that the marina has caused, we have already discussed this with our attorney and she fully supports the decision to move forward in this direction to sell the vessel and to make the information public.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1625250891308466177','-',7,'United States','na',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-02-13',1,'2023-02-13',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-13 21:50:37',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
(9610,'Web design for in-person event site',3,'Hello - we are looking for a contractor to develop and implement a highly polished, limited-scope website for a professional event taking place in the late summer of 2023. Our organization can provide content, copy, and structure as needed, and we are looking to contractors to provide the design, development, and implementation required to bring this project into production by May 15, 2023.\r\n\r\nThe event in question is a high-profile professional event series attracting VIPs from several industries, and as such, we are prioritizing polish, attention to detail, intuitive design capabilities, and timeliness in selecting our contractor.\r\n\r\nThe site to be developed will consist of agendas for the event, bios of all speakers (including information on where/when during event they will be speaking), general information about the event and its hosting organization, and other information that will be helpful to attendees about the geographic area the event will be hosted.\r\n\r\nSites should be equally effective and usable on both mobile and desktop environments\r\n\r\nFor examples of sites with polish and similar objectives to what we are looking for, please see the below:\r\n\r\nhttps://conferences.wsj.com/\r\nhttps://techlive.wsj.com/\r\nhttps://www.nationalgeographic.com/events/?size=n_25_n&sort%5B0%5D%5Bfield%5D=start_date&sort%5B0%5D%5Bdirection%5D=asc&sort%5B1%5D%5Bfield%5D=title&sort%5B1%5D%5Bdirection%5D=asc\r\n\r\nWhen bidding, please include portfolio references of high-polish websites created by yourself (or the team you will be using, in the case of agencies) to demonstrate quality of look and feel you/your team is capable of. Agencies should not send portfolio references showing ANY work done by individuals who will not be working on this project, in whole or in part.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1625252807026634753','-',7,'United States','Arlington',60.000,'perhour',60.000,'2023-02-13',1,'2023-02-1