(10362,'UX/UI design project funding application',6,'We are seeking a UX/UI designer to create wireframes, visual designs, and UX and flow for a funding portal. The designer should aim to create an intuitive and user-friendly experience for potential grantees.\r\n\r\nThe project will involve creating wireframes and prototypes to test and refine the design of the portal. The designer should conduct user research to understand the needs and goals of potential grantees, and use this information to inform the design of the portal. The wireframes and prototypes should be used to solicit feedback from potential grantees and to iterate on the design as needed.\r\n\r\nThe designer should also create a visual design for the portal that is consistent with the branding and values of the organization. This includes designing a color scheme, typography, and other visual elements that create a cohesive and visually appealing experience.\r\n\r\nIn addition, the designer should create an information architecture that is easy to navigate and understand. This includes designing a clear and consistent navigation system, as well as organizing content in a logical and intuitive manner.\r\n\r\nOverall, the UX/UI designer is responsible for creating a user-centered design that meets the needs of potential grantees and helps them navigate the grant application process with ease. The designer should work closely with the development team to ensure that the design is implemented effectively and efficiently.\r\n\r\nThe project:\r\n\r\nThe funding portal will be designed with a variety of features to streamline the grant application process and enable effective communication between the organization and potential grantees.\r\n\r\nOne key feature will be a login system that allows applicants to create a secure account and access the various forms and resources available on the portal.\r\n\r\nAnother critical feature will be the various forms available to potential grantees. These will include a pre-application form, which will allow applicants to provide basic information about their project and receive feedback before submitting a full application. The full application form will be comprehensive, enabling applicants to provide detailed information about their project, budget, timeline, expected outcomes, and more. In addition, there will be an application form specifically for donations, allowing individuals and organizations to make contributions directly to supported projects. Finally, the portal will feature a transfer application form, enabling current grantees to request additional funding or make adjustments to their grant.\r\n\r\nThe funding portal will also feature robust file management capabilities. Applicants will be able to upload all necessary documents and materials through the portal, ensuring that the organization has all the information it needs to make informed decisions about grant applications. The portal will also allow for easy tracking and management of all grant-related documents, such as project proposals, budgets, and reporting materials.\r\n\r\nOverall, the funding portal will be an essential tool for ensuring effective communication and efficient grant management. By providing a streamlined process for submitting grant applications, managing files, and communicating with potential grantees, the portal will help the organization achieve its mission of making a positive impact in the community.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2024578','-',7,'United States','na',0.000,'fixed',0.000,'2023-02-20',1,'2023-02-20',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-20 13:23:56',NULL,9,3,NULL,116),
