(10893,'Administrative Support for Therapy Office',22,'I\'m the practice owner of Resolution Counseling Center, a 4-site psychotherapy service in northern New Jersey (right outside of NYC for a landmark) and we are looking to expand our administrative team. We have 50+ therapists on staff and plan to grow to 70 this year. Our therapists provide over 3500 therapy sessions a month to about 1200 active clients and we add about 35 new clients to the practice each week in busy seasons. That\'s where our admin team comes in--right now we have 1 full-time person and 3 part-time members of the team, and we\'re looking to add another person who would work up to working 40 hours/wk. Our admin team members wear many hats but your primary job would be to engage our clients over phone, text, and email-- helping prospective ones choose a therapist, answering questions, providing information, solving problems, and following our myriad processes along the way. The job involves a lot of detail-oriented work, a lot of writing and editing, a lot of communicating, following detailed step-by-step processes. You can feel good about the work you do because you\'re helping hundreds of clients who are strugglng with painful seasons in life get the help they need.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1628517679218716673','-',7,'United States','Jersey City',13.000,'perhour',13.000,'2023-02-22',1,'2023-02-22',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-22 22:11:58',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(10894,'Medical Billing Specialist',21,'At Adonis, we offer multiple solutions to assist medical providers in navigating the complexities of healthcare billing and receipt of payment for service. Billing and insurance related activities represent nearly $1 in every $7 collected by medical providers - and the high costs of collecting payments, as well as and other costs that stem from the administrative challenges within the space, unfortunately get passed down to the consumer. This is why healthcare costs continue to rise, with no end to that in sight. We’re set on helping to mitigate these challenges. While we are building a medical billing engine that automates billing workflows and improves reimbursement rates for medical providers, we at Adonis feel that there is always an aspect of healthcare billing that requires a human touch.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for medical billers with experience in multiple specialties, including but not limited to Mental Health, Dermatology, Orthopedics, and Primary Care. To perform the following functions for our clients:\r\n\r\nAnswer patient questions related to insurance claims.\r\nCollaborate with clients as related to billing needs.\r\nVerification of patient eligibility for services.\r\nSubmission of claims to insurance payors.\r\nResolution of claims that are rejected by the clearinghouse or the payor scrubber.\r\nResolution of claim denials.\r\nPayment posting of funds from paid claims\r\nThe ideal candidate for this role would have the following experience and background:\r\n\r\n2-4 years of healthcare billing experience\r\nCPC certification preferred but not required\r\nExperience billing while in a remote environment is required\r\nThe ideal candidate for this role possessed the following qualities:\r\n\r\nHas a technology first mindset and is committed to making processes more efficient and automated when possible.\r\nExcellent communication skills and the ability to practice proper phone and email etiquette, and is skilled in answering a telephone in a pleasant and helpful manner.\r\nAnswers questions from customers, clerical staff, and insurance companies.\r\nFamiliar with medical terminology and insurances HCPC/ICD-10 codes,\r\nDocuments activities in the Adonis system in an efficient, accurate, and timely manner.\r\nProvide feedback to the supervisor regarding issues regarding accounts.\r\nConducts routine tasks as directed; works under clearly defined guidelines to achieve clearly defined metrics..\r\nContributes to specific objectives and outcomes as','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1628519618531069953','-',7,'United States','-',26.000,'perhour',26.000,'2023-02-22',1,'2023-02-22',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-22 22:20:44',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
