(11097,'Experienced Psych/Medical Virtual Assistant and Medical Biller',21,'We are seeking 1-2 experienced Medical Virtual Assistant (Patient Care Coordinator) to help our rapidly growing outpatient Psychiatric Mental Health Practice located in California.\r\n\r\nThis position is Full-Time, Monday thru Friday, with working hours from 9:00 AM - 5 PM Pacific Standard Time (PST).\r\n\r\nOur ideal candidate is a Medical Virtual Assistant who has at least 1 year of experience working in a psychiatric, mental health, or therapy practice.\r\n\r\nTASKS:\r\nWhile our office is primarily hybrid (online and in-person), we need an experienced Registered Nurse or Medical Assistant to help to:\r\n\r\n1) communicate with prospective and current patients by text, email, fax and phone, as needed.\r\n2) assure new and follow up patients are entered into our Practice Fusion EHR system and that payment and paperwork is received for each appointment.\r\n3) perform limited medical billing duties within the EHR and other billing platforms, for cash and insurance claims processing. Will be entering CPT codes into EHR\r\n4) confirm insurance benefits eligibility electronically or by phone and collect any copays or deductibles due prior to appointment time.\r\n5) assure that patients are scheduling follow-up visits.\r\n6) complete and submit insurance Prior Authorization Forms for medication claims.\r\n7) retrieve EOB/ERA document from multiple insurance portals to retrieve information and match data on an excel file to each client visit and be able to organize excel to easily bring up the EOB/ERA when needed in case patient has billing questions\r\n8) will need experience multitasking between answering phones, data entry, completing requests from other staff members and attending to customer service tasks\r\n9) will need extensive experience with Microsoft products but especially Outlook, Excel, Word and Powerpoint\r\n10) will need to be detail oriented\r\n11) This position will also be in charge of handling customer billing questions and concerns, so you will need to have great customer service skills\r\n\r\n#1 requirement is RELIABILITY. We are a small team and depend on each other. Attendance is very important.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n-Must be a fluent English speaker and strong writer\r\n-Experience in working with Mental Health\r\n-Must own a laptop or PC\r\n-At least 20 mbps internet speed for primary ISP\r\n-Must have backup internet provider\r\n-Noise cancellation headset\r\n-Experience with practice fusion is preferred but willing to train.\r\n-Must be a outgoing, enthusiastic and willing to learn.\r\n-Nursing/Medical Background is A HUGE PLUS\r\n\r\nIf you are interested, please submit a resume and we will share the Practice details and arrange to speak.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to considering everyone qualified and hire immediately.\r\n\r\nOur record for hiring is excellent on Upwork and our long-term engagements speak to our commitment and ability to manage a virtual workforce.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1629131340282974209','-',7,'United States','Long Beach',7.000,'perhour',7.000,'2023-02-24',1,'2023-02-24',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-24 14:50:19',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
