(11385,'Credentialing Specialist',24,'*Performs accurate and timely provider credentialing, to include new applicant credentialing, re-credentialing and ongoing maintenance of provider credentials and reports as required by commercial, federal and state payer, hospitals and other regulatory or agency requirements.\r\nResponsible for accurate and timely collection and data entry of CAQH, DEA, licensure and other provider enrollment requirements.\r\n\r\n* Creates and facilitates completion of clinician applications for payer and facilities to ensure timely credentialing and enrollment.\r\n\r\n*Prepares application packet to send out to providers.\r\nAssists in maintenance of listing of “pending applications.”\r\n\r\n*Receives application from potential applicant; review application for completeness/accuracy and initiate processing, including but not limited to (1) Primary source verification (educational, employment, licensure, insurance carriers and hospital affiliations). (2) OIG query. (3) Criminal Background Check submission. (4) Third party payers, CAQH and other related credentialing applications.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1630301060358279169','-',7,'United States','Suffolk',10.000,'perhour',10.000,'2023-02-27',1,'2023-02-27',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-27 20:18:28',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(11386,'Branding Specialist.',2,'Our company is seeking a highly motivated and creative branding specialist to help our marketing team. We are looking for someone who has a passion for branding and a proven track record of creating successful brand strategies and compelling visual identities. As our branding specialist, you\'ll have the opportunity to create a complete company brand kit, including a visual identity that accurately reflects our brand\'s personality and a style guide to ensure consistency across all channels.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nDevelop and execute a comprehensive brand strategy that aligns with our company\'s mission and values\r\nConduct market research and competitive analysis to identify key differentiators and target audience\r\nCreate a visual identity that accurately reflects our brand\'s personality, including logo, color palette, typography, and graphic elements\r\nDesign templates for branded materials, including letterheads, email signatures, social media graphics, and other marketing collateral\r\nCreate a style guide for imagery to be used in applications on our website, social media, learning platforms, books, and merchandise\r\nCollaborate with internal teams, including marketing, product, and design, to ensure brand consistency and integration\r\nMonitor and measure the effectiveness of the brand strategy and make adjustments as needed\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\nProven experience as a branding specialist or similar role\r\nStrong understanding of branding principles and marketing best practices\r\nExcellent design skills with a proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite\r\nAbility to think creatively and strategically, with a keen eye for detail\r\nStrong project management and communication skills\r\nAbility to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment\r\n\r\nIf you\'re a passionate branding specialist who is committed to creating impactful brand strategies and driving business growth, we encourage you to apply. In this role, you\'ll have the opportunity to create a brand that resonates with our customers across multiple channels, including our website, social media, learning platforms, books, and merchandise. Please submit your resume, cover letter, and portfolio of your branding work for consideration.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1630301180718026753','-',7,'United States','Brooklyn',12.000,'perhour',12.000,'2023-02-27',1,'2023-02-27',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-27 20:18:52',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
