(11490,'Clue Style Game Board Design',2,'Need a game board illustrated. The game board style I\'m looking for visually is Clue--The top-down perspective. \r\n\r\n\r\nGame board is separated into four squares. Starting at the lower-right, here are the visual styles I want to see:\r\n\r\n\r\nThe bottom-right (Green) should resemble a low-income area with cracks in the concrete, potholes, trash scattered around and graffiti (maybe even on the spaces as well). The center grass should be mostly dirt and the leasing office should be a mobile home rather than a building. \r\n\r\n\r\nThe bottom-left (RED) should be a mid-town look. Mostly brick. Kind of middle-income level look. Not as much trash. Better roof condition. Grass around the leasing office is discolored with patches of brown. Leasing office can be a decent building. \r\n\r\n\r\nTop-Left (GOLD) should be upper-class. Should have home-style roofs. No trash. Nice grass with A small house as leasing office. \r\n\r\n\r\nTop-right (BLUE)  should be glass. Think Tesla. Landscaping. Very expensive. \r\n\r\n\r\nSee my rough example.\r\nAttachments','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2027772','-',7,'United States','-',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-02-28',1,'2023-02-28',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-28 15:31:02',NULL,3,1,NULL,136),
