(11543,'RCM Administrator',21,'nnovative Lab Solutions LLC is a boutique medical billing firm providing a full suite of specialized billing, consulting, staffing, and compliance services to meet the needs of independent and specialty laboratories. We are currently in search of a RCM (Revenue Cycle Management) Administrator.\r\n\r\nIn this role the RCM Administrator’s primary duties and responsibilities are to manage requests for payer portal access, payer enrollments (EDI, EFT, ERA), integration of new billing RCM systems to allow electronic claims submissions and payments. In this role, the RCM Administrator works with the IT department to ensure overall administration and compliance of RCM functions in all systems used by the organization.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities and Duties:\r\n• Updates and manages all requests for payer portal access by users.\r\n• Acts as liaison between ILS and outside vendors to ensure the complaint interface and set up for EDI, ERA, and EFT files.\r\n• Coordinates the set-up of users for access to Help Desk Tickets to record projects for turnaround time and resolution.\r\n• Reports monthly to Management on the status of all EDI/ERA/EFT applications and enrollments to ensure the ratio of electronic to manual claims and cash posting processes is within the targeted goals.\r\n• Works with the Denial Management team members to resolve issues for claims denied for provider access.\r\n• Coordinates with IT department the access and set up for all relevant billing systems and portal accesses for all new hires as well as remove access for those individuals no longer with ILS.\r\n• Other projects as assigned.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n• Bachelor’s degree preferred or other relevant revenue cycle experience.\r\n• Must have 3-5 years’ experience in health care organization in a revenue cycle department\r\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\r\n• Proficient with Excel\r\n• Insurance billing processes and website usage experience\r\n• Collaborator who can work cross functionally with different client accounts as well as work independently.\r\n• Excellent analytical and organizational skills\r\n• Professional team player who inspires trust\r\n\r\nJob Type: Full-time\r\nSchedule:\r\n• 8-hour shift\r\n• Monday to Friday\r\nExperience:\r\n• Payor Portal: 3 years (Preferred)\r\n• Revenue Cycle Management: 3 years (Required)\r\nWork Location: Remote','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1630625364034613249','-',7,'United States','Kings County',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-02-28',1,'2023-02-28',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-02-28 17:47:34',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
