(11758,'Medical Biller/AR Specialist',21,'A medical biller for a homecare agency is responsible for managing the billing process for services provided to patients in their homes. The primary duties of a medical biller for a homecare agency include:\r\n\r\nVerify patient insurance coverage: The medical biller must verify the patient\'s insurance coverage to ensure that the services provided are covered by the patient\'s insurance plan.\r\n\r\nGenerate invoices and submit claims: The medical biller must generate invoices for services provided and submit claims to insurance companies or government programs like Medicare and Medicaid.\r\n\r\nFollow up on outstanding payments: The medical biller must follow up on outstanding payments and denials from insurance companies, and resubmit claims as needed.\r\n\r\nManage patient accounts: The medical biller must manage patient accounts and ensure that all payments are accurately recorded.\r\n\r\nStay up-to-date on billing regulations: The medical biller must stay up-to-date on billing regulations and ensure that all billing practices comply with relevant laws and regulations.\r\n\r\nCommunicate with healthcare providers: The medical biller must communicate with healthcare providers to ensure that all necessary information is included on invoices and claims.\r\n\r\nMaintain accurate records: The medical biller must maintain accurate records of all billing activities and patient information.\r\n\r\nOverall, the medical biller plays a critical role in ensuring that the homecare agency is reimbursed for the services provided and that patients receive the care they need.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1630975998667730945','-',7,'United States','Brooklyn',12.000,'perhour',12.000,'2023-03-01',1,'2023-03-01',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-01 17:00:09',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
