(11912,'Logo design',10,'Looking for a logo design that can be used on a ID badge. Look at the purple Pensacon badge seen on this website for size and concept example. https://idshop.com/custom-id-card-badge-printing/custom-badges/\r\n\r\nThe design should have an image of Grand Central Terminal as a backdrop. you can use the one that is attached or your own ideas. The text should include\r\n\r\n1. The Journey - Grand Central Terminal\r\n2. 2023\r\n3. Special Access\r\n\r\nDeliverables include\r\n\r\n1. The design - it needs to fit on the attached SEJ-30 template (packaged Adobe InDesign folders and jpeg)\r\n2. A vector file of the text \"The Journey\" using the same font used in the logo\r\n3. A vector file of the text \"The Journey - Grand Central Terminal\" on 2 lines using the same font used in the logo\r\n4. A vector file of the text \"No underwear after Friday\" using the same font used in the logo','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1631313654010417153','-',7,'United States','New York',40.000,'Open this select menu',40.000,'2023-03-02',1,'2023-03-02',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-02 15:21:45',NULL,9,3,NULL,116),
(11913,'Brand Color & Packaging Redesign',2,'We are looking to update our brand colors and our packaging. Last year, we launched new patches, and strayed away from the brand guide. What worked for our original product was the two-color, three icon print on the front of the patches. We want to come up with a large array of icons that will work with the focus, stress and extra strength patches - as well as new patches we are working on. We would also like the colors to be updated in our brand guide. We are keeping the ZPatch colors as is, but want to rework all of the other colors. The goal is develop pouch packaging (vs cardboard) that looks good on the shelves of retailers - we really love the styling of The Good Patch and The Patch Brand. Our products all need to look good next to each other (they do not right now), and stand out/ catch the eye of the Target/ Whole Foods Shopper. Additionally, we love the icons in our current brand guide, and want to get back to that. The brand needs to be very unisex, and not just geared towards women or men. This job is to do three things: Create an updated color guide, with palates for each of the 4 patches - and 3 additional, select 3 icons for each patch - and come up with a new packaging style for a 7x9 pouch.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1631314698534707201?success','-',7,'United States','Santa Monica',1500.000,'fixed',1500.000,'2023-03-02',1,'2023-03-02',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-02 15:27:13',NULL,6,3,NULL,123),
