(12370,'Intake Coordinator for Psychologist in Private Practice',21,'This is a part-time virtual position responsible for the initial point of contact for all new patients. Initially you will be covering my current intake coordinators maternity leave. But it is likely this will become temp to perm.\r\n\r\nBusiness Values:\r\nPeople with psychosis have been short changed for too long. Traditionally in the US their treatment has been limited to hospital outpatient or community mental health clinics that are housed in well known to be stigmatizing to the community buildings, have noisy and sometimes unsafe waiting rooms, and give an all round “illness” attitude that many people with psychosis don’t agree with. Also traditionally treatment has been provided by early career clinicians, straight out of graduate school (or even still in graduate school on internships or externships), looking to gain clinical hours before moving up and out to something else. These clinicians are often not highly skilled or trained in evidence based therapies. I believe that people with psychosis deserve better!!! Psychosis can happen to anyone, regardless of who or where they are.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1632758976840445953','-',7,'United States','New York',35.000,'perhour',28.000,'2023-03-06',1,'2023-03-06',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-06 15:05:29',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
