(12668,'CODER for PEDIATRICS',30,'We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Medical Coder to join our Pediatrics department in Georgia. The ideal candidate will have a solid understanding of Georgia Medicaid guidelines and codes and a passion for delivering quality medical coding services.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nReview medical records to accurately identify and assign appropriate codes for diagnostic and procedural information.\r\nEnsure compliance with Georgia Medicaid coding guidelines and regulations.\r\nMaintain current knowledge of coding conventions and updates to codes and regulations.\r\nCollaborate with healthcare providers and office staff to ensure complete and accurate documentation.\r\nCommunicate coding issues and questions to the appropriate parties.\r\nConduct quality assurance audits to ensure coding accuracy.\r\nKeep updated records of coding activities and reports.\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nHigh school diploma or equivalent.\r\nA minimum of 2 years of experience in medical coding, with a focus on Pediatrics.\r\nKnowledge of ICD-10, CPT, HCPCS, and other coding systems.\r\nFamiliarity with Georgia Medicaid guidelines and regulations.\r\nAbility to work accurately and efficiently in a fast-paced environment.\r\nStrong attention to detail and excellent organizational skills.\r\nGood communication and interpersonal skills.\r\nMust be able to work independently or as part of a team.\r\nWe offer competitive compensation, benefits, and opportunities for professional growth. If you are an experienced Medical Coder looking to join a dynamic team, please submit your resume for consideration.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1633120515620331521','-',7,'United States','US',18.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-03-07',1,'2023-03-07',1,'Normal Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-07 15:47:51',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
