(12675,'UI / UX for a high growth running start up',4,'*About Us*\r\n\r\nCoopah is an early-stage startup, that’s developing a business that will revolutionise the world of health and fitness.\r\n\r\nWe are building the future of training.\r\n\r\nCurrently, 50% of people quit training within 60 days.\r\n\r\nWe are going to change that with a personalised, digital coach app.\r\n\r\nWe are based in London, but with a remote team across the globe that are integral to our development.\r\n\r\n*Our Achievements*\r\n\r\n✅ Secured an exclusive contract with the biggest running event in the country\r\n\r\n✅ Backed by Olympic medal-winning athletes\r\n\r\n✅ User base growing at a rate of 46% month on month\r\n\r\n✅ Over 100 5* rated reviews of the app\r\n\r\n*What We Are Looking For*\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a part time UI / UX designer to lead the deisgn and usability of our digital run coaching app. The role is a part time role (8 days per month) but we are looking for someone who would be looking to be a long term part of the business.\r\n\r\nYou will work collaboratively with our Co-Founder and Product Manager to develop and maintain the Coopah app UI. We have huge ambitions and we want to improve every element of our app to optimise the experience for users and retention with our training programs. We are looking for someone who lives and breaths design and can match their passion and understanding with the needs of our users.\r\n\r\n*The role will include but isn’t limited to:*\r\n\r\n- Creating wireframes for new product features to get sign-off from the product owner and lead developers\r\n- Designing UI’s for the Coopah mobile app based on new features, user feedback and analytics\r\n- Reviewing analytics to come up with new improvements to the existing UI / UX\r\n- On occasion, supporting the team on other design tasks such as social content, website design and event stands.\r\n\r\n*We’d expect the candidate to have the following skills:*\r\n\r\n- An amazing eye for the usability of consumer apps and experience designing wireframes to think through complex UX designs\r\n- Have developed a high-quality portfolio of UI/UX designs for mobile applications\r\n- You have a high level working knowledge of Figma and the ability to think up the right UI’s for the brand and solution\r\n- You have a good technical understanding of development processes and our product in order to build designs for developer handoff\r\n- You love running and understand the market for digital run coaches\r\n\r\n*Nice to have’s:*\r\n\r\n- You have experience with a sports application\r\n- You have experience working with Notion\r\n- You have experience working in your own business\r\n- You can design graphics and artwork for social media, websites and event stands when required\r\n\r\n*What’s In It For You*\r\n\r\n- £1,500 *per month for 8 days per month*\r\n- All Coopah benefits listed on Coopah Careers (https://www.notion.so/Coopah-Careers-dd6249b166594e4fa48b4e666aea385e)','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0191098c86eb089ee8','-',7,'United States','London',30.000,'perhour',30.000,'2023-03-07',1,'2023-03-07',1,'In process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-07 15:58:31',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
