(12807,'Bookkeeper',23,'We are a small company that manufactures very specialized packaging machinery. Actually, there are only 2 companies in the world that do this. We have a German subcontractor in Istanbul, Turkey where the majority of the machine components are manufactured and assembled by a small group of specially selected, and trained, mechanical and electrical engineers. We also have a full-time CAD design engineer in Istanbul, Jale, who has just finished up her last chemo treatment 5 days ago. Jale was diagnosed with breast cancer last year and thankfully she is finished with the chemo, which we hope will eradicate this insidious disease, and to which I am no stranger. I, myself, am a 3 time survivor of cancer. Cancer doesn\'t run in my family....it gallops, having lost one brother, David at 32 in 1975, as well as my Mom at 51, in 1976, almost 1 year later to the day.\r\n\r\nWe have a full-time employee, Ali, based in The Netherlands, who spends quite a bit of his time in Turkey as well as traveling for service and machine installations. Ali and I finished up a machine install in Ohio, where we spent 5 weeks together just before Christmas. Ali has worked for us for 20 years, and I have known him for almost 40 years. Our machinery is big. 60 ft long and weighs more than 20 tons, and can produce milk/juice cartons at more than 35 per second.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1633208346043985921','-',7,'United States','-',40.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-03-07',1,'2023-03-07',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-07 20:51:38',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
