(12983,'T Shirt Designs',2,'Design and create t shirt designs for the fastest growing brand within the vaping industry.\r\n\r\n1. Design a set of t-shirts for the brand Bar Juice 5000. https://barjuicevape.com/\r\n2. These t-shirts will be worn across exhibition events around the globe including London, Dubai and Germany.\r\n\r\nBrief:\r\n\r\n• After reviewing the website you will see that the brand specialises in the vaping industry manufacturing nicotine based e-liquid. This liquid comes in 20 different flavours.\r\n• We need a total of 10 different t-shirt designs for the 10 flavours. We would like to have each t-shirt represent one flavour. The flavours we want to translate into t-shirts are:\r\n\r\n1. Apple Peach\r\n2. Blue Razz Lemonade\r\n3. Blueberry Pomegranate\r\n4. Watermelon\r\n5. Gummy Bear\r\n6. Kiwi Passionfruit Guava\r\n7. Energy Ice\r\n8. Grape\r\n9. Pink Lemonade\r\n10. Strawberry Ice Cream\r\n\r\n• The branding for Bar Juice 5000 should be clearly visible on the t-shirt at the front and at the back.\r\n• Most importantly, we would need to have a graphic of each of the flavours on the back of the t-shirt. For example: if we are designing the flavour of Blueberry Pomegranate, the graphic for the back of the t-shirt would be a macro vector of blueberries and a pomegranate which looks tasty and juicy.\r\n• The t-shirt colour will correspond to the same colour as the bottle packaging as seen on the website.\r\n• We would like to use the same style of graphic as “macro vector” as attached. The graphics are SUPER IMPORTANT, they can’t look too realistic and not too animated. There needs to be a happy medium where the fruits and flavours look appetising!\r\n• Raw photoshop files for logo/fonts can be provided upon request.\r\n• The vibe of the t-shirts need to be professional yet quirky whilst being appealing to the eyes due to the graphics.\r\n• The placement of the logo should be at the front on the left side chest area and at the back on the neck line.\r\n• The name of the flavour should also be visible at the bottom of the graphic.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2033806','-',7,'United States','-',250.000,'fixed',650.000,'2023-03-08',1,'2023-03-08',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-08 17:33:20',NULL,3,1,NULL,136),
