(13476,'Medical Billing Charge Entry Specialist',21,'We are seeking a highly organized and detail-oriented Charge Entry Specialist with extensive knowledge of CPT codes, modifiers, and ICD codes. The Charge Entry Specialist will be responsible for ensuring accurate and timely charge entry for medical procedures and services rendered for pathology, hematology, and oncology. The ideal candidate will have excellent communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work efficiently and effectively in a fast-paced environment.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\nReview and analyze medical documentation to determine appropriate CPT codes, modifiers, and ICD codes for charge entry.\r\nAccurately enter charges into E Clinical Works and Advanced MD, ensuring that all required information is complete and accurate.\r\nIdentify and resolve any discrepancies or errors related to charge entry\r\nCommunicate with our Team to obtain missing or incomplete information\r\nMonitor and manage the charge entry process to ensure that all charges are entered in a timely and accurate manner\r\nMaintain up-to-date knowledge of coding guidelines, regulations, and compliance requirements\r\nAssist with coding audits and reviews as needed\r\nPerform other duties as assigned by management\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\nHigh school diploma or equivalent required; Associate degree or higher preferred\r\nMinimum of 2 years of experience in charge entry or medical billing, with a strong understanding of CPT codes, modifiers, and ICD codes\r\nKnowledge of medical terminology and anatomy\r\nMust be available to work 40 hours a week\r\nExcellent attention to detail and accuracy, with the ability to multitask and prioritize effectively\r\nStrong communication skills, both verbal and written\r\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team\r\nUnderstanding of healthcare regulations and compliance requirements, including HIPAA and Medicare/Medicaid guidelines','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635276431862157313','-',7,'United States','fresno',6.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-03-13',1,'2023-03-13',1,'Normal Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-13 14:17:13',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(13477,'Email Template Design',2,'Looking for a clean email template to be designed in Mailchimp. This designer should also be proficient in Canva as I would like to update the graphics on my own through Canva when I send it out monthly.\r\n\r\nThe email template is for real estate market stats that will include 6 different neighborhoods. I send out a more in-depth yearly market update, and I want this monthly update to be clean and simple so clients can review it over a few minutes. Each of the 6 neighborhoods will include Single Family, Condo, Townhome, and Vacant Land stats for the month prior. Stats to be included are Average sales price, Average price per sq. ft. sold, and number of sales for the month. Also wanted is the difference from the year prior to be added. The 6 neighborhood graphic templates should be created in Canva so I can update them.\r\n\r\nThe MailChimp email template should include Header, Footer, and Layout for the 6 neighborhoods, and design\r\n\r\nMy company already has logos, specific fonts and brand colors.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1633872579848581121','Leah Bishop || Leah Bishop || Crystal.',94,'United States','Winter Park',200.000,'Open this select menu',200.000,'2023-03-13',1,'2023-03-13',NULL,'Fix price project',1,NULL,NULL,1,'2023-03-13 14:17:13','2023-03-20 17:10:15',5,3,NULL,128),
