(13613,'Animated Video Creation',8,'We need an instructional animated video created on how to reconstitute and inject our peptide products that patients can refer to. I have step-by-step instructions, but would like the video to show those instructions. View the instructions below:\r\n\r\nHow To Reconstitute Your Peptide Vial(s)\r\n\r\nTo reconstitute your peptide vial(s), you will need:\r\nThe peptide vial you will be reconstituting\r\nA vial of bacteriostatic water\r\n1 alcohol wipe\r\n100 unit syringe\r\nTake the lids off of both the peptide vial and the bacteriostatic water\r\nUsing the alcohol wipe, clean the now exposed top of both the peptide vial and the bacteriostatic water\r\nRemove the plastic protectors from the 100 unit syringe\r\nPull the plunger of the syringe all the way back to bring air into the syringe\r\nPush the needle of the syringe into the bacteriostatic water vial\r\nOnce completely inserted into the bacteriostatic water vial, push the plunger of the syringe all the way down, injecting the collected air into the vial of water\r\nSlowly pull the plunger of the syringe back out, collecting the bacteriostatic water into the syringe\r\n**Use the provided table below to determine how much water you should pull into the 100 unit syringe depending on which peptide you are reconstituting.\r\nSlowly remove the syringe from the bacteriostatic water vial\r\nPush the needle of the syringe into the peptide vial\r\nOnce completely inserted into the peptide vial, push the plunger of the syringe all the way down, injecting the bacteriostatic water into the peptide vial\r\nRepeat steps 5-11 if needed, based on the amount of water needed to reconstitute the peptide vial, referring to the provided table\r\nOnce the recommended amount of water for the peptide vial has been inserted, gently swirl the water around within the peptide vial until mixed\r\nReplace the safety cap onto the 100 unit syringe and safely discard\r\nStore both the reconstituted peptide (up to 6 months) and bacteriostatic water (up to 6 weeks) in the refrigerator\r\nRepeat the process for all peptide vials, only reconstituting the vials that are needed immediately for dosing\r\nRefer to our “How to Inject Your Peptide” guide for step-by-step instructions on how to inject your peptide\r\n\r\nHow to Inject Your Peptide\r\n\r\nTo inject your peptide(s), you will need:\r\nThe reconstituted peptide vial\r\n1 alcohol wipe\r\n30 unit syringe\r\n**(Refer to our “How to Reconstitute Your Peptide Vial(s)” guide for step-by-step instructions on how to reconstitute your peptide, if you haven’t already done so\r\nUsing the alcohol wipe, clean the exposed top of both the peptide vial and injection area\r\n**You can inject into the skin at any location on the body – the most common sites are the back of the arm, the lower stomach, or the bottom\r\nRemove the plastic protectors from the 30 unit syringe\r\nPull the plunger of the syringe all the way back to bring air into the syringe\r\nPush the needle of the syringe into the peptide vial\r\nOnce completely inserted into the peptide vial, push the plunger of the syringe all the way down, injecting the collected air into the peptide vial\r\nSlowly pull the plunger of the syringe back out, collecting the peptide solution into the syringe\r\n**Use the provided table below to determine how much solution you should pull into the 30 unit syringe\r\nSoftly gather the skin, with a slight pinching motion, at your preferred injection site\r\nGently puncture the cleansed skin with the needle of the syringe and push it in completely, from a 45-90 degree angle\r\nPush the plunger of the syringe down, injecting the peptide solution into the skin\r\nReplace the safety cap onto the 30 unit syringe and safely discard\r\nStore the peptide vial in the refrigerator until the next use\r\n**Refer to the provided “For Best Results” card within your package for instructions on dosage timing','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635328821046411264','-',7,'United States','-',48.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-03-13',1,'2023-03-13',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-13 19:04:00',NULL,9,3,NULL,140),
(13614,'Pitch Deck for Software Startup',11,'Hello. We are an existing software startup founded and run by two brothers.\r\n\r\nWe\'ve had a difficult time getting users to adopt our current software, so in lieu of closing our doors we\'ve decided to attempt to \"pivot\" our software to cater to the dental industry. We need to create a 13 slide pitch deck of our idea and present it to some investors to hopefully raise money and fund the needed code change.\r\n\r\nI\'ve attached our previous pitch deck so you can have some idea of the design and feel we\'re looking for.\r\n\r\nWe\'re not looking for anything insanely complicated as this will only be seen by 6-7 people. We\'re expecting around 1-1.5 hours of work per slide.\r\n\r\nHere is our outline for the slides (we have all of the bullet points and data already, we just need someone with design skills to create our infographic slides for us.)\r\n\r\n1: Company logo/company slogan\r\n2: Our mission\r\n3: The problem\r\n4: The solution\r\n5: Our target audience:\r\n6: TAM (Total Addressable Market)\r\n7: Competitors. Competition appears to be contained to regions of the US.\r\n8: Technology Requirement for pivot:\r\n9: Proof of concept (industry quotes, testimonials)\r\n10: Business model:\r\n11: Current traction:\r\n12: Summary\r\n13: Ask from investors with forecast of deliverables','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635356271969718273?success','-',7,'United States','Millcreek',20.000,'perhour',50.000,'2023-03-13',1,'2023-03-13',1,'hourly',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-13 19:05:52',NULL,7,3,NULL,133),
