(13878,'Law Firm Needs A Website Re-design',3,'General: The client liked the sargentlawfirm.com page for reference. They also stated that they don’t like to brag about themselves too much. We have also attached a handful of other websites they like at the bottom of the brief.\r\n\r\nWe want the design to make the user feel comfortable reaching out to the firm. There should be an aggressive slant to the design, but not TOO aggressive.\r\n\r\nThe design should be well thought-out, with usability and professionalism highlighted throughout, with all styling being pretty consistent for the different sections.\r\n\r\nPlease review the project brief, as well as our attached guidelines and examples thoroughly, as we have done hundreds of hours of market research to maximize conversion on our websites.\r\n\r\nThis Client has an existing site: https://sevenishlaw1.wpengine.com/\r\nThey want to use the following colors:\r\n\r\nWhite: #ffffff\r\nBlack: #000000\r\nNavy Blue: #181B2D\r\nBlue: #092f68\r\nGray: #383838\r\n\r\nWe need you to choose a high contrast color for all call to action buttons - this color should only appear where we want the user to click/convert. \r\nFonts: Pick new fonts that align with our guidelines (which are attached.)\r\nTagline: “Fierce protectors of the injured”. The client wants this to be prominently used throughout the website, as they have trademarked the slogan.\r\n Ideal Audience: Injured individual in Indiana, seeking legal representation in a personal injury matter, who need reassurance that the attorney they are hiring is well qualified, respected, effective, professional, and fierce.\r\n\r\nPages Needed: We need Desktop AND Mobile designs for the following page types\r\n\r\nHomepage\r\nInterior Page\r\nAbout Us Page\r\nVideo Library Page\r\n\r\nThe sections for each page type are listed in order below, please design all sections in accordance with our guidelines and using your best design judgement\r\n\r\nHomepage: Needs to have the following\r\n\r\nHero Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nClient Reviews Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nIntro video of firm should be featured on homepage according to our guidelines which is attached (link to video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O4TX1FHcBl8)\r\nCase Results section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nPractice Area Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nCase Process Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nMultiple call to action sections - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nClient Testimonials section (comprised of videos)\r\nPeer Reviews section (comprised of videos)\r\nA contact us section\r\n\r\nInterior Page:\r\n\r\nHeading Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nClient Reviews Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nCase Results section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nPage Content Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nRelated Videos Section - This section should contain videos that correlate with that page on the bottom:\r\nFor example: Motorcycle accident interior page should have a Related Videos section that will show all the motorcycle videos, below the page content\r\nProminent Call-To-Action section (in accordance with our guidelines,)\r\nFooter\r\n\r\nAbout Us: Follow our guidelines which are attached for the below\r\n\r\nHero/Heading Section\r\nRandall Sevenish\r\nOther staff\r\nReviews\r\nResults\r\nClient Testimonials section (comprised of videos)\r\nPeer Reviews section (comprised of videos)\r\nFooter\r\n\r\nVideo Library: This should be formatted into an archive page where all videos are displayed, and the user can filter between the below options:\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions\r\nClient Testimonials\r\nPeer Reviews\r\nInformation Videos\r\nCommercial Videos\r\nOther Videos\r\nPersonal Injury\r\nCar Accidents\r\nMotorcycle Accidents\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNotes on Common Sections:\r\n\r\nFooter should contain the footer elements outlined in our guidelines, with 2 additional sections above it:\r\n\r\nA “Why Choose Us” type section, with the heading “Fierce Protectors of the Injured”\r\nAn awards section featuring all the award logos that appear on this page: https://sevenishlaw1.wpengine.com/peer-ratings-awards-memberships/\r\n\r\nMenu Bar:\r\n\r\nThe Menu Items should be same, however the header of the site should be redesigned according or our guidelines which are attached.\r\n\r\n\r\nReference Site(s):\r\n\r\nsargentlawfirm.com\r\nhttps://wattsguerra.com/\r\nhttps://justcallmoe.com/','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635731544166739969?success','-',7,'United States','Greenville',1800.000,'fixed',1800.000,'2023-03-14',1,'2023-03-14',1,'Fixed',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-14 19:56:56',NULL,7,3,NULL,133),
(13879,'Graphic Design',2,'We are looking for someone who can help us design the layout for an electronic newsletter that will focus on safety. All content will be produced by in-house writers. Our need is strictly with the design to make it pop! Our sector is transportation/infrastructure.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635731834790064129?success','-',7,'United States','ux',60.000,'Open this select menu',60.000,'2023-03-14',1,'2023-03-14',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-14 20:00:25',NULL,6,3,NULL,123),
(13880,'WebFlow Website Development',3,'Ad agency looking to contract WebFlow Designer(s).\r\n\r\nWe are looking to partner with a creative designer experienced in WebFlow. The number and type of projects will vary. The ideal candidate will establish themselves as the \"go-to\" designer for future projects.\r\n\r\nTypically, this designer will build a homepage and two internal pages (based on a website design brief submitted by clients). However, about 25% of the time we will need someone to build out an entire site, with various functionality, including e-commerce, animation, etc.\r\n\r\nWhile we expect this to change in the near future, the ideal designer will have their own WebFlow account with the ability to transfer their work to our workspace.\r\n\r\nProject revenues vary, so we don\'t know the pay range available for each project. We will scope the project together and provide a payscale to the designer for them to accept or reject.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635732427304894465','-',7,'United States','Edmond',40.000,'perhour',40.000,'2023-03-14',1,'2023-03-14',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-14 20:00:52',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
(13881,'Rebuild Company Website',3,'Hello,\r\n\r\nI am in need of someone to apply generic maintenance to my company website. The site as a whole requires extensive effort to update or change any media (we are a video production company) and we would like to streamline this process. As a whole we are open to a complete redesign if suitable. We simply are looking for a new sleek representation for the company.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635733703767609345','-',7,'United States','West Hollywood',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-03-14',1,'2023-03-14',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-14 20:05:34',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
(13882,'Web Designer',4,'The web designer will be responsible for the design & development of creative materials for nationally recognized auto service industry client, with the goal of bringing a sleek & modern feel to the brand.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities include, but are not limited to:\r\n\r\n• Provide design support and creative deliverables for nationally recognized auto service industry client\r\n• Provide direction on website UI – including, but not limited to:\r\no Service scheduling forms\r\no Location pages\r\no Header/footer design\r\no CTAs\r\n\r\nDeliverables will be used as:\r\no Marketing ad sets across several online platforms\r\no National Website\r\no Tech platform UI design\r\no Other','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1635735773981474817','-',7,'United States','San Diego',40.000,'perhour',40.000,'2023-03-14',1,'2023-03-14',1,'na',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-14 20:13:56',NULL,8,3,NULL,156),
