(14114,'Seeking Talented UI/UX Landing Page Designer / Figma expert for B2B SaaS startup',4,'About Secfix\r\n\r\nSecfix automates security compliance for SMBs in Europe. We help companies get and stay compliant with standards such as ISO 27001, GDPR, TISAX, and SOC 2 in weeks rather than months.\r\n\r\nAbout the role:\r\n\r\nAs a small team, we are all generalists and constantly picking up new challenges. Regarding design and code, we’re looking to work with experienced people who can pick a problem or idea, build and launch. We use Webflow and Figma and want to build out further our landing page so we can increase the reach and conversion on the pages. We don’t expect you to have a background in everything we use but expect very good eye for minimalistic and estetic landing page designs, strong web design fundamentals and a passion for visual design in Figma. Every landing page that is being ideated will be ideated, designed and user-tested by you.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- You are capable of creating beautiful, minimalistic and meaningful landing page designs in Figma by yourself in a quick iterations.\r\n- You have a strong portfolio demonstrating your passion for designing clean, elegant, and beautiful landing pages both designed by you from scratch in Figma, better if these designs are for tech brands like SaaS business.\r\n- You have 4 or more years designing pages within a cross-functional team environment in Figma and can lead Figma landing page and execute without external help. You can collaborate with senior management, and various departments in a concise but enthusiastic manner. You can collaborate in Figma Comments, Slack, Notion Docs and other tools.\r\n- You are creative but work with structure and are organised both in your work and Figma files\r\n- Strong leadership capabilities to advise on goal setting, vision, and resource planning and timely execution. You will follow-up till you get things done.\r\n- You are hacky. You don’t work on shaping a perfect idea for several weeks, instead you iterate on a simpler designs fast and get user feedback so you get the right things built fast.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n- You will do all of things below and learn fast if specific skills are missing.\r\n- You will be responsible for the visual design of our entire landing page. You will be the main landing page designer who can design pages fast\r\n- You will design and create low and high-fidelity Figma designs of new pages and iterate on existing ones with great taste and attention to detail. You will make sure the designs are modern, clean and user-friendly.\r\n- You will collaborate with the marketing, product, design and revenue teams on new pages, new designs, site optimization and improvements to website structure within webflow. Design consistent experiences across our web properties with reusable components. Design pages and prep briefing for Webflow developers. Come up with interesting animations.\r\n- Find areas of improvement and propose new and better solutions\r\n- An eye for detail. \"Pixel perfect\" Image optimization\r\n\r\nYou will stand out if you\r\n\r\n- Have SaaS/B2B design experience\r\n- You are up-to-date with the latest web trends, techniques, and technologies.\r\n- Have some experience in Webflow and designing pages in figma for webflow implementation\r\n\r\nProcess:\r\n- Small paid Figma & Webflow design trial project\r\n- If the trial project is successful, we will engage on a long-term basis','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0118a222e24269a0b1','-',7,'United States','UK',50.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-03-16',1,'2023-03-16',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-16 12:10:35',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
(14115,'Webflow Developer',4,'About the role:\r\n\r\nAs a small team, we are all generalists and constantly picking up new challenges. Regarding design and code, we’re looking to work with experienced people who can pick a problem or idea, build and launch. We use Webflow and Figma and want to build out further our landing page so we can increase the reach and conversion on the pages. We don’t expect you to have a background in everything we use but expect strong Web design and development fundamentals and a background working with Webflow and Figma. Every landing page that is being ideated will be ideated, user-tested, iterated, and developed by you. You\'ll get first-hand exposure to what it means to build and scale a remote software startup’s landing page.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n- You have deep knowledge and sound experience of at least 2 years developing user-friendly, responsive and animated Weblfow webpages with complex structure, fast. You can build a responsive, animated Webflow page within days, not weeks.\r\n- You have three or more years designing pages within a cross-functional team environment in Figma and can lead Figma landing page and execute without external help. You can collaborate with senior management, and various departments in a concise but enthusiastic manner. You can collaborate in Figma Comments, Slack, Notion Docs and other tools.\r\n- You have a portfolio demonstrating your passion for designing clean, elegant, and beautiful landing pages both designed by you from scratch in Figma and Webflow better if these designs are for tech brands like SaaS business.\r\n- Interview: You have experience in user research: you did user interviews and A/B tests before\r\n- Strong leadership capabilities to advise on goal setting, vision, and resource planning and timely execution. You will follow-up till you get things done.\r\n- You are hacky. You don’t work on shaping a perfect idea for several weeks, instead you iterate on a simpler designs fast and get user feedback so you get the right things built fast.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n- You will do all of things below and learn fast if specific skills are missing.\r\n- You will be responsible for our entire landing page. You will be both the main landing page designer and Webflow developer who can build a pages fast without destroying existing classes and backend.\r\n- You will design and create low and high-fidelity Figma designs of new pages and iterate on existing ones with a great taste and attention to detail. You will make sure the designs are modern, clean and user-friendly.\r\n- You will collaborate with the marketing, product, design and revenue teams on new pages, new desings, site optimization and improvements to website structure within webflow. Design and build consistent experiences across our web properties with reusable components. Design & build new pages within our Webflow instance. Create modern animations by leveraging Webflow’s capabilities.\r\n- You will do UX research including: A/B tests, Google Analytics, research experience using Hotjar/Fullstroy, and do user interviews early in the idea stage of Figma frames. You will support requests from other teams in updating the site’s content, building SEO, creating experiments. You know how to talk to users, do user tests and know YCombinator MVP lessons.\r\n- Optimize loading speeds and capacity, debug pages, and fix broken links or images. Ensure website consistency across all pages and other web properties.\r\n- Find areas of improvement and propose new and better solutions\r\n- An eye for detail. \"Pixel perfect\" Image optimization, Alt tags, SEO, social share images etc','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01d58f5c22b9cc58cf','-',7,'United States','UK',50.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-03-16',1,'2023-03-16',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-16 12:13:08',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
