(14136,'Design a product packaging for a payment ring',2,'Hey @all,\r\n\r\nwe have developed a payment ring and want to rebrand our product packaging. Currently we have a jewellry like packaging but want a more technical, apple like packaging for future. Therefore we need an expert in the fields of packagind design for a technical device. In a fresh modern way.\r\n\r\nThe packaging should be approx. the size of a smartphone packaging.\r\n\r\nWe are glad to see your past work and get in touch with you.\r\n\r\nBR','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01880194a7ca3374d2','-',7,'United States','Köln',50.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-03-16',1,'2023-03-16',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-16 14:45:27',NULL,8,3,NULL,146),
(14137,'WordPress Website for Annual Charity Event',15,'This will be awarded as a fixed-cost project. There will be plenty of opportunity for questions, clarification of requirements and review of the current site before you submit a final fixed-cost proposal.\r\n\r\nIn your response include a general price range based on the requirements listed below.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for an experienced WordPress developer to build a website for a charity sporting event that takes place over 1-2 days once or twice a year.\r\n\r\nThe event is used to raise money for charity whereby amateur competitors get sponsors to make financial donations.\r\n\r\nThe key components are:\r\n- the event (1-2 events per year)\r\n- Competitors (i.e. participants in the event)\r\n- Donors - people/companies that sponsor competitors\r\n- Donations - money paid by the donors\r\n\r\nThis is a re-build of an existing site. Much of the functionality noted below already exists on the current site, but the site was built without planning and now suffers from technical debt. The primary goal is to create a site that site admins can properly manage without requiring a developer for basic tasks. Rather than re-factoring the existing code, a new site with clear goals and planning seems more efficient and cost-effective.\r\n\r\nEvent: the event is created by the site admin several months before the event date. The event occurs on a specific date, over one or two days. The event will stay posted until the next event is created (a year later). Previous events are archived in their entirety and can be accessed in the event archive. The ability to create new events and archive events needs to be done by the site admin (currently can only be done by developer).\r\n\r\nParticipants: register online to compete in the event and complete a participant profile (name, address, photo, bio, etc.) and pay a registration fee (credit card). Every participant has a public profile page that displays the names of donors and the amount of their donation. Donors/donations update in realtime as new donations are made.\r\n\r\nDonors: donors can donate to specific participants or a general donation to the event. Donors are not required to register but donor information is stored for tax and reporting purposes. We should discuss a method for \"silently\" registering donors and provide a tool for site admins to merge duplicate donors.\r\n\r\nDonations: donations are made by credit card (Stripe) or check. For check payments the donation should have a pending state until the payment is received/posted by a site admin.\r\n\r\nAn Event consists of:\r\n- General information about the event. Location, date(s), announcements, FAQ, etc. This is essentially the event \"home page\". Event home page also includes the total of the donations received.\r\n- Competitor Archive page of all competitors with links to individual competitor profiles\r\n- Donations archive page with individual donations and donors\r\n- Basic page with Corporate Sponsor information (different from Donors, these are corporate sponsors with logos, links, etc.) This could be a custom post type created by an admin with different levels of Sponsors (Presenting Sponsor, General Sponsor, etc.)\r\n\r\nThe site includes (separate from Events):\r\n- News (blog posts)\r\n- About Us - general information about the organizer\r\n- Contact\r\n- Lifetime Donations (see below)\r\n- Social media links\r\n\r\nAdditional Details:\r\nThe individual events are archived every year - i.e. there is an archive page of previous events. Archived events store all the details about that event - competitors, donors, donations.\r\n\r\nWhen a new event is created the donations for the new event are set to zero, but the donations for previous events and competitors are preserved.\r\n\r\nCompetitors may compete over several years. The Competitor\'s profile page should include which previous events they participated, and the donations they received for previous events.\r\n\r\nA separate Donations archive should include links to donations received in previous events, and also a \"lifetime\" donations (i.e. the top 20 donors based on the sum of donations over the previous events).\r\n\r\nEvent winners - admins should be able to mark individual competitors as \'winners\' in specific categories. These winners will be automatically promoted on the Competitor Archive page.\r\n\r\nMust include the ability for site admins to export data to be used in external applications: Competitor Profiles with donors/donations, Donors.\r\n\r\nDesign!! The site must have a clean and professional design. This needs to be a site with a high quality design that is appealing to competitors, donors and corporate sponsors. Good mobile UX goes without saying....\r\n\r\nWe also need to discuss content migration to preserve previous events and past competitor profiles. This could be done manually by the client, or some other type of basic archive.\r\n\r\nWe do not want any type of page builder (e.g. Divi, Elementor, Beaver, etc.). In your response to this post, please indicate why you would or why you would not use the GeneratePress theme to build this site.\r\n\r\nMany thanks.\r\n\r\nDaniel','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1636378193043431425?success','-',7,'United States','Louisville',50.000,'perhour',50.000,'2023-03-16',1,'2023-03-16',1,'hourly',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-16 14:46:33',NULL,7,3,NULL,133),
