(14278,'WordPress Blog Creation',15,'*** Please reply with your total bid amount to complete this project. Prefer to work with freelancers with at least 10K+ in work completed on Upwork, not agencies ***\r\n\r\nHello Dev! We\'re looking to add a blog to our website and update our existing navigation. We currently have a blog that a freelancer worked on, but was not able to complete the project. Here\'s some details about our website:\r\n\r\n- WordPress using Beaver Builder theme and plugin\r\n\r\nWe\'re looking to add the following:\r\n- Blog homepage (a feed of recent blog), not the homepage for the site.\r\n- Category feed page\r\n- Blog post template\r\n- Update to our site navigation (detailed in PDF)\r\n\r\nPrefer to work with a dev or designer that has experience with Beaver Builder and can build with it.\r\n\r\nI\'ve attached a PDF that details the project design as well as all 3 templates to be updated. Work is expected to match the design and functionality 100%. Please do not respond if you\'re not able to meet this design.\r\n\r\nThanks!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01b9873619e72fd4f1','-',7,'United States','Boynton Beach',48.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-03-17',1,'2023-03-17',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-17 07:45:58',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
(14279,'Experienced Graphic Designer for Branding Project',2,'We are looking for an experienced graphic designer to help us create a strong and cohesive brand identity for our company, Neonflex. Neonflex is a design studio that creates personalized, high-quality neon lights that reflect our customers\' individuality and values. We are looking for a designer who can work with us to create a brand that reflects our mission, values, and style.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n* Collaborate to develop a strong brand identity that aligns with our mission and values\r\n* Design a logo and brand style guide that can be used across all marketing materials\r\n* Develop a color palette and typography that reflects the brand\'s energy and uniqueness\r\n* Create marketing materials such as business cards, social media graphics, and website designs (if possible) that reflect the brand\'s style and values\r\n* Provide guidance on the use of the brand across all marketing materials\r\n* Potentially work as a UX/UI designer to design our website \r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n* Strong portfolio of branding and graphic design work\r\n* Excellent communication skills to collaborate effectively with the Neonflex team\r\n* Experience creating brand style guides and designing marketing materials\r\n* Strong understanding of typography, color theory, and graphic design principles\r\n* Familiarity with Adobe Creative Suite and other design software\r\n* Availability to work on this project for a minimum of 20 hours per week\r\n* Potential availability and experience to work as a UX/UI designer to design our website \r\n\r\nIf you are a talented graphic designer who is passionate about creating unique and personalized brands, and potentially designing website UX/UI, we encourage you to apply for this position. Also if you read this all, please put Custom neon in the first sentence, so we can scale down the candidates. We are excited to work with someone who shares our values and can help us create a brand that truly reflects who we are as a company.\r\n\r\nBest,\r\n\r\nRoald','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0188c3640dfd393226','-',7,'United States','Alkmaar',1500.000,'fixed',1500.000,'2023-03-17',1,'2023-03-17',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-17 09:45:20',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
(14280,'Web Design: 10-15 Copy Wireframes for Enterprise-Facing Website',4,'I need to restructure, rewrite copy and redesign my website: www.learningfromnormalwork.com\r\n\r\nThe output:\r\nSTEP 1 - Proposal for a new website structure (10-15 pages), including homepage, resources, case studies, etc. -\r\nSTEP 2 - New copy for the identified pages\r\nSTEP 3 - FINAL DELIVERABLE - Copy wireframes for the identified pages with suggested layout\r\n\r\nNOT in scope:\r\n1. final graphics design\r\n2. logo design\r\n3. marketing report\r\n4. website coding or hosting\r\n5. brand guidelines\r\n\r\nYou will have:\r\n1. understanding of complex b2b sales cycles\r\n2. experience of developing website serving enterprise customers, (5,000 employees or more)\r\n3. understanding of the enterprise customer buying journey, including the needs of various stakeholders at various stages of the journey\r\n4. ability to create a copy addressing needs of these stakeholders\r\n5. understanding and experience with designing information architecture and UX\r\n6. familiarity with the \"Challenger Sales\" approach and ability to use it in copywriting to reframe customers\' problems\r\n7. familiarity with the customer\'s \"Sensemaking process\" (see Gartner\'s research) and ability to translate it into the information architecture and copy design\r\n\r\nI will provide:\r\n1. product descriptions\r\n2. marketing materials including value proposition, persona descriptions, competitor analysis, SWOT, the voice of the customer etc.\r\n3. Any other information you may need to set you up for success\r\n\r\nIn your application, please provide:\r\n1. at least one example of a website designed for the enterprise customer\r\n1a. explain how you designed the structure of the website\r\n1b. explain how you went about developing copy and what needs you addressed\r\n2. at least one example of copy wireframe that you designed\r\n\r\nTimeline: 14 days\r\n\r\nNOTE: I\'ve had some bad experiences in the past, when people tried to contact me outside UpWork through unsolicited personal email, skype, and other platforms. Please DO NOT do that. I welcome applications only through Upwork.\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and I very much look forward to learning about your work and hopefully working together.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01a14f60e21f1a6768','-',7,'United States','London',3000.000,'fixed',3000.000,'2023-03-17',1,'2023-03-17',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-17 10:05:56',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
