(14499,'Social Media Post Designer',2,'We are seeking a skilled and creative Social Media Post Designer to promote a new feature for our company. As a designer, you will be responsible for creating 4 eye-catching posts that adhere to our branding guidelines and showcase the new feature to our audience on LinkedIn, Instagram, and Twitter.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n-Develop and design 4 social media posts that effectively promote our new feature\r\n-Use images that directly showcase the new feature to potential customers\r\n-Ensure that all posts adhere to our company\'s branding guidelines\r\n-Tailor the posts to effectively market the new feature to our audience\r\n-Deliver posts in a format that can be easily posted on LinkedIn, Instagram, and Twitter\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n-Proven experience in social media post design, with a portfolio that showcases your work\r\n-Proficiency in design tools such as Adobe Creative Suite and Canva\r\n-Strong understanding of branding and design principles\r\n-Ability to tailor posts to different social media platforms and audiences\r\n-Excellent communication and collaboration skills\r\n-Ability to work independently and meet deadlines\r\n\r\nIf you are a talented and creative designer with a passion for social media and marketing, we encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01c3c8add258a5ed5b','-',7,'United States','Hielaah',50.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-03-20',1,'2023-03-20',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-20 15:42:34',NULL,9,3,NULL,126),
(14500,'Biller/Collector',21,'Medical Biller/Collector Job Description\r\nThe position will include reviewing all claims to determine all actions including but not limited to settlements, payments, communications, and documentations are made in accordance with company and legal regulations.\r\nEssential Functions:\r\n• Prepare technical reports by collection, analyzing and summarizing information and trends.\r\n• Identify and resolve problems and make time-sensitive decisions independently.\r\n• Collect information related to a patient’s overdue insurance or medical bill and then work with the patient in determining a repayment plan.\r\n• Review claims for eligibility to be reimbursed.\r\n• Follow all HIPAA regulations\r\n• Uncover, report, and organize details and information around claims.\r\n• Provide updates on any irregularities and discrepancies to find appropriate solutions.\r\n• Prepare technical reports by collection, analyzing and summarizing information and trends.\r\n• Identify and resolve problems and make time-sensitive decisions independently.\r\n• Investigate, evaluate, and settle insurance claims.\r\n• Analyze and review insurance claims for accuracy, completeness, and eligibility.\r\n\r\nCore Competencies:\r\n• Technological savvy with quick ability to learn new systems\r\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills\r\n• Exceptional phone skills\r\n• Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information (adhere to HIPAA)\r\n• Working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel and Outlook\r\n• Meticulously organized with strong attention to detail','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1637842115435630593','-',7,'United States','Kings County',8.000,'perhour',8.000,'2023-03-20',1,'2023-03-20',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-20 15:43:30',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
