(14515,'Pitch Deck / Slide Show / Adobe Illustrator / Draft',11,'I have narratives and bullets for TWO different pitch decks. One is 14 slides. The other is 23 slides. I have all the images identified, and many in ai files I can share. I have all the text for each slide.\r\n\r\nI need someone faster and better than I am at adobe illustrator to set up these 37 slides and format with the same fonts, good headers, and consistent colors.\r\n\r\nIt might take me a week and someone else who does this all day long would be much better.\r\n\r\nA few samples below: The full file after we discuss in detail.\r\n\r\nI need all the original dot ai files, art, fonts used (I will pick a common font) and any clip art base. So that I can tweak, modify, to change it totally later.\r\n\r\n--- Sample ---\r\n\r\nSlide 1: Introduction to Vertical Farming\r\n• Definition of vertical farming\r\n• Importance of sustainable agriculture in the 21st century\r\n• Overview of the presentation~\r\nSlide 2: The Need for Vertical Farming and Technologies\r\n• Growing global population and the need for increased food production\r\n• Urbanization and limited availability of arable land\r\n• Environmental concerns and resource scarcity\r\n• Hydroponics, aeroponics, and aquaponics as solutions~\r\nSlide 3: Aeroponics - The Superior Method\r\n• Introduction to aeroponics and its advantages\r\n• Increased oxygenation of plant roots\r\n• Faster growth rates and higher crop yields~\r\nSlide 4: The Science Behind Aeroponics\r\n• How aeroponic systems work\r\n• The role of nutrient mist and micro-droplets in delivering nutrients to plant roots\r\n• The importance of monitoring and maintaining optimal growing conditions~\r\n\r\nDesign -----\r\n\r\nSlide 1: A globe surrounded by various crops, illustrating the global impact of vertical farming.\r\nSlide 2: A bar chart showing the increasing global population, urbanization, and decreasing arable land over time.\r\nSlide 3: A pyramid with aeroponics at the top, showcasing its superiority over other methods.\r\nSlide 4: A diagram illustrating an aeroponic system with nutrient mist and micro-droplets being delivered to plant roots.\r\n\r\nDetails ---\r\n\r\nTitle: Vertical Farming: A Look into the Future of Agriculture with Aeroponics\r\n\r\nIntroduction\r\nAs the world population continues to grow, the need for sustainable and efficient food production has never been more pressing. Vertical farming, an innovative agricultural technique that utilizes vertical space to grow crops, has emerged as a promising solution to address this challenge. In this article, we will explore the basic technology behind vertical farming, focusing on aeroponics, and discuss the advantages and science that make it superior to other methods.\r\n\r\nVertical Farming Technologies\r\nThere are several technologies used in vertical farming, including hydroponics, aeroponics, and aquaponics. Hydroponics involves growing plants in nutrient-rich water without soil, while aquaponics combines hydroponics with aquaculture (raising fish) to create a symbiotic environment where the fish provide nutrients for the plants and the plants clean the water for the fish. Aeroponics, on the other hand, grows plants in air or mist environments without soil, allowing the roots to absorb nutrients directly from the nutrient-rich mist.\r\n\r\nAeroponics: A Superior Method\r\nAmong the three vertical farming technologies, aeroponics stands out as the most efficient and sustainable method. Aeroponic systems expose plant roots to a nutrient-rich mist, providing an optimal environment for oxygenation and nutrient absorption. This results in faster growth rates and higher crop yields compared to hydroponics and aquaponics. Additionally, aeroponic systems use significantly less water than traditional soil-based farming and even other vertical farming methods, making it an eco-friendly choice in water-scarce regions.\r\n\r\nThe Science Behind Aeroponics\r\nIn aeroponic systems, plants are suspended in air with their roots exposed to a nutrient-rich mist. This mist is composed of micro-droplets containing essential nutrients required for plant growth. The increased oxygenation of plant roots in aeroponic systems accelerates growth and enhances nutrient uptake, leading to improved crop yields. To maintain optimal growing conditions, factors such as temperature, humidity, and nutrient concentration must be closely monitored and adjusted as needed.\r\n\r\n\r\n--- Conclusion\r\n\r\nI have ALL this detail for ALL 37 slides (14/23) and just need someone to assemble it, make it standardized, and let me finish it.\r\n\r\nI am attaching my previous deck for a different project. I did this in a few weeks. I am not that skilled. It takes me way too long.\r\n\r\nI need these two to look and layout like this one.\r\n\r\nIgnore the slides in the sample attached which are company specific or financial. I will insert them later. This project is JUST the base slides.\r\n\r\nThanks','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1637848315427164161?success','-',7,'United States','Des Moines',1000.000,'fixed',1000.000,'2023-03-20',1,'2023-03-20',1,'Fixed',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-20 16:08:27',NULL,7,3,NULL,133),
