(14673,'Personal tax assistance: single member LLC + W2 + investment activity',23,'I\'m reaching out because I\'m looking fro someone to...\r\n\r\n1) Answer questions as it relates to my personal 2022 tax filing (and/or filing an extension and then completing it) and general tax advice\r\n2) File my personal tax return for 2022.\r\n3) Provide some (minimal) accounting assistance for my LLC.\r\n\r\n\r\nSome additional context—\r\n- My 2022 tax situation involves W2 income, single member LLC activity, and various investment transactions across online investment platforms (including cryptocurrency trades).\r\n- While I have all of my LLC income and expenses going through my LLC\'s bank account (not my personal account), we switched banks this year from Mercury to Found. Found handles accounting automatically (https://found.com/bookkeeping), but the fact that we switched from Mercury means that some expenses and income were not transferred over. This is the *only* accounting activity needed. We don\'t QBO or anything like that.\r\n- I\'ve prepared a Notion document outlining all the relevant details and a Google Drive folder containing (what I believe to be) all the necessary forms and income information that I would share access to you with so you wouldn\'t have to ask me to hunt them down.\r\n- The last several years I\'ve used Turbotax, but I felt like 2022 became a bit more complicated as I went full-time on my business and had slightly more investment-related activity.\r\n\r\nHere is an overview of my questions\r\n1. What can we do about the investment/trade losses? How much can we deduct and/or what do we carry over?\r\n2. Can we deduct losses associated with an investment platform going bankrupt (BlockFi)?\r\n3. I put almost all of my LLC\'s expenses on my LLC bank\'s debit cards. However, I imagine there are several things we can write off that were not transacted through my LLC bank account, such as personal healthcare-related costs, rent, internet/phone expenses, etc. What can we do about those?\r\n4. What\'s the process for converting to an S corp? Does it make senes for 2023?','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1638197228626239489','-',7,'United States','Carmel',70.000,'perhour',65.000,'2023-03-21',1,'2023-03-21',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-21 15:15:00',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
