(15217,'Experienced Logo Designer for Craig Coffee',10,'Job Description:\r\nWe are seeking an experienced logo designer to finalize a transformative and inspiring logo for Craig Coffee. Our brand is focused on inspiring and empowering young adults to take control of their lives and reach their full potential. We aim to overcome obstacles and unleash potential through our transformative life coaching.\r\n\r\nLogo Design: We have a first draft of the logo that was created using DALLE-2. The logo features an abstract image of a phoenix rising from the ashes. The phoenix is depicted in a bold and dynamic style, with vibrant colors that convey energy and ambition (Hex colors: #F05A28, #FFD700, #F7E319). We need a skilled graphic designer to refine the design, incorporate the brand name and tagline.\r\n\r\nFont: The brand name, \"Craig Coffee,\" should be displayed in a sleek and modern font. The font should be clean, easy to read, and emphasize the first letter of each word. Our top font suggestions are: Gotham, Open Sans, Raleway, and Bree Serif. The brand name should be positioned below the phoenix image.\r\n\r\nComposition: The logo should be balanced and symmetrical, with a clear focal point that draws the eye to the phoenix. The design should be simple and impactful, with a strong visual hierarchy that conveys the brand\'s message of transformation and success.\r\n\r\nTagline: The tagline for Craig Coffee is \"Unleashing potential, overcoming obstacles with Craig Coffee.\" It should be incorporated into the logo design in a way that complements the overall look and feel of the brand.\r\n\r\nDeliverables: The final deliverables should include the original source files (AI, PSD, etc.), vector files, and high-resolution PNG and JPG files in both color and black and white.\r\n\r\nTimeline: We are looking for a quick turnaround time, with the final deliverables due within 1-3 days of the project start date.\r\n\r\nTo Apply: If you are a skilled and experienced logo designer who is passionate about creating impactful and inspiring logos, we encourage you to apply for this project. Please include a portfolio of your previous work, along with a brief cover letter explaining why you are the ideal candidate for this project.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to working with you to bring the vision for Craig Coffee to life! As an added bonus, please include a creative message or joke related to phoenixes in your cover letter to let us know that you have read the entire job posting.','Job Description: We are seeking an experienced logo designer to finalize a transformative and inspir','-',7,'United States','Jacksonville',250.000,'fixed',250.000,'2023-03-24',1,'2023-03-24',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-24 16:44:12',NULL,5,3,NULL,129),
(15218,'Simple logo design',10,'logo design for a cleaning company located in a island in Massachusetts. perfer beach related ideas summer colors and simple. if you can mix and match beach and cleaning together will be great!\r\nname of the business is,\r\nMaid in Vineyard Co\r\n\r\nThank you!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01c0c685e59286318a','-',7,'United States','Framingham',120.000,'fixed',120.000,'2023-03-24',1,'2023-03-24',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-24 16:45:26',NULL,8,3,NULL,146),
(15219,'Senior Accounts Receivable Specialist',23,'Role Summary:\r\nReporting directly to the AR Supervisor, the Senior AR Specialist will be responsible for handling collections of a subset of key customers. Collections efforts will include but are not limited to hitting defined collection goals and KPIs, monthly reporting of customer portfolio, and cash application.\r\n\r\nJob Responsibilities:\r\nProcess high volume of collections calls on a daily basis to ensure customers are paying in a timely fashion, resolve and report on discrepancies as needed;\r\nCollaborate with customers directly to reconcile and resolve outstanding balances;\r\nReview invoice and payment status via customer portal\r\nTrack all disputed invoices for visibility and reporting purposes;\r\nUtilize resources at disposal to research and resolve customer disputes.\r\nMaintain communication in AR inbox and answer phone calls associated with customer questions;\r\nEnsure customers are paying in a timely fashion, resolve and report on discrepancies as needed.\r\nMaintain or exceed company DSO of 25 days\r\nPropose accounts that should be turned off or sent to collections based on payment history, claims status or disputed invoices;\r\nPrepare weekly AR Agings for sales to review;\r\nCustomer payment conversion from check to ACH\r\nMaintain files and documentation thoroughly and accurately, in accordance with company policy and accepted accounting practices;\r\nMentor and train new associates;\r\nAddress credit related issues that cause holds and payment delays;\r\nWork with cash application team to make sure all payments are posted;\r\nCollaborate with internal business partners (Sales, Billing, etc…) to address any and all issues that arise;\r\nProvide weekly aging progress report to the leadership team.\r\nCollaborate with internal business partners (Sales, Billing, etc…) to address any and all issues that arise.\r\nProvide support and take on additional tasks as needed.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1639306833618300929','-',7,'United States','Solana Beach',12.000,'perhour',12.000,'2023-03-24',1,'2023-03-24',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-24 16:46:01',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(15220,'Admin Support Needed for Provider Insurance Credentialing (long term, 4-12 hours/week)',24,'Compiles and maintains current and accurate data for all providers\r\nCompletes provider credentialing and recredentialing applications: monitors applications and follows-up as needed by phone and/or email.\r\nMaintains copies of current medical licenses, DEA certificates, malpractice coverage and any other required credentialing documents for all providers.\r\nMaintains provider files in Sharefile database.\r\nEnsures practice addresses are current with health plans, agencies, and other entities.\r\nProcesses applications for appointment and reappointment of privileges with hospitals-experience preferred\r\nAudits health plan directories for current and accurate provider information.\r\nOther reasonably related duties as assigned.\r\n\r\nROLE QUALIFICATIONS:\r\n\r\nPrefer credentialing experience within a clinic or physician practice is required (can be remote experience).\r\nPrefer working knowledge of insurance plans, including Medicare and Medicaid.\r\nProficiency in computer software use, including Microsoft Office and Excel\r\nEffective time management and the ability to prioritize work.\r\nExcellent communication skills and the ability to interact with all levels of management, staff, and physicians.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1639303604023795713','-',7,'United States','Katy',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-03-24',1,'2023-03-24',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-24 16:47:04',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
