(15310,'Medical Virtual Assistant',22,'Medical Office - Remote - Front office Back office, part-time.\r\n\r\nDUTIES:\r\nMust be able to multitask, work independently, and pay attention to details. Must have excellent reading and writing skills to respond to emails and texts. This is not a position for someone that is forgetful or has difficulty multitasking.\r\n\r\n1. Front and back office experience to assist with phone calls, scheduling, dealing with insurance questions, and answering emails, and texts. Look up eligibility, obtain authorizations, etc\r\n\r\n2. Be able to provide basic procedure, practice, and physician details to potential clients. Attention to detail is important.\r\n\r\n3. Marketing calls to potential referring physician\'s offices.\r\n\r\n5. Help with any administrative practice needs/improvement projects.\r\n\r\n6. Be able to check patient balance, and verify insurance and network status.\r\n\r\nPerfect candidate:\r\n\r\nExcellent writing skills to reply to emails and texts professionally.\r\nCan manage multiple responsibilities.\r\nExcellent organization skills.\r\nGreat attention to detail.\r\nFast learner.\r\nFriendly and compassionate.\r\nCan work independently.\r\nHard worker and efficient.\r\n\r\nTop applicants are friendly, outgoing, compassionate, full of ideas, and enjoy working as a team.\r\n\r\nWork Hours: Flexible time that includes one hour each weekday, Monday through Friday. We will provide you with a phone app that you can call out and receive calls. You will have hippa compliant email and EMR access.\r\n\r\nPosition Requirements:\r\n*Must provide your own computer, phone and headset.\r\n*Must have 6 months to 1 year prior front office/back office experience (preferred).\r\n*Must have experience in obtaining pre-authorization/insurance verification.\r\n*Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\r\n*Strong organizational and planning skills.\r\n*Answer phone calls, emails, online chat, online text\r\n*Assist in booking appointments\r\nPrior experience with EMR (preferred)\r\n*Marketing experience (preferred)\r\n\r\nDuties and Responsibilities:\r\n\r\n*Organize and schedule appointments.\r\n*Update and file medical records and insurance reports.\r\n*Produce and distribute correspondence memos, letters, faxes, and forms.\r\n*Providing information to patients relating to referrals, follow-up appointments, and test results.\r\n*Insurance Verification/Pre-authorization/Look up fee schedule','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~013575a86f9f4a2093','-',7,'United States','Saint Louis',15.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-03-26',1,'2023-03-26',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-26 18:47:33',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
