(16289,'Medical billing and AR specialist required.',21,'Assist with Claim filing -related inquiries. Medical terminology knowledge is a must including ICD10, modifier requirements, and CPT coding.\r\n\r\nStrong follow-up skills are essential, as applicants will need to follow up on rejected and denied claims and underpayments, using the Practices electronic health record and/or payers Explanation of Benefits forms.\r\n\r\nPrepare and submit billing data and medical claims to insurance companies.\r\nEnsure the patient’s payment is accurate and up to date.\r\nPrepare bills and invoices, and document amounts due to medical procedures and services.\r\n\r\nInvestigate and appeal denied claims.\r\n\r\nCharge is based on percentage of successful payments from all claims submitted -long term partnership desired based on experience','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1641832956153135105','-',7,'United States','San Francisco',5.000,'fixed',18.000,'2023-03-31',1,'2023-03-31',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-31 20:37:18',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(16290,'Pitch Deck Designer',11,'Description:\r\nWe are looking for an experienced pitch deck designer to work with us on a project starting immediately. The ideal candidate will have a strong portfolio of prior work in designing effective pitch decks that have helped businesses secure funding or partnerships. The project will involve creating a pitch deck for our company, which we will use to pitch to potential investors and partners.\r\nNEED TO START IMMEDIATELY\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Collaborate with us to understand our business, goals, and target audience\r\n• Create a visually appealing and engaging pitch deck that effectively communicates our value proposition, business model, market opportunity, and competitive advantage\r\n• Develop clear and concise messaging that highlights key points and addresses potential investor questions\r\n• Provide guidance and advice on best practices for presenting the deck in person or virtually\r\n• Work with us to refine and improve the deck based on feedback received from investors or partners\r\n\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n• Proven experience in designing successful pitch decks\r\n• Excellent communication and collaboration skills\r\n• Strong attention to detail and ability to deliver high-quality work within tight deadlines\r\n• Proficiency in using PowerPoint, Keynote, or other presentation software\r\n• Familiarity with startup and investment landscape\r\n\r\n\r\nTimeline and Deliverables:\r\n\r\nThe project will be divided into three stages: first pass, Second Pass and finalization\r\nThe first pass of the pitch deck should be completed within this week\r\n\r\nThe Second Pass  stage will involve filling in any gaps, and we will begin sourcing better images for the deck from our partners abroad,  and will address feedback received from us and potential investors or partners.\r\n\r\nThe finalization stage will involve polishing and refining the deck to ensure it is ready for presentation\r\n\r\nThe completed pitch deck should be delivered within three weeks from the start of the project\r\nIf you meet the above requirements and are interested in working with us on this project, please submit your application along with your portfolio of prior pitch deck work. Only candidates with a strong portfolio will be considered. We look forward to hearing from you!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01eb22fef0698e912e','-',7,'United States','Santa Monica',150.000,'perhour',80.000,'2023-03-31',1,'2023-03-31',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-31 20:37:49',NULL,19,3,NULL,129),
(16291,'US Medical Virtual Assistant/Medical scribe',22,'We are seeking a friendly and talented medical virtual assistant/Scribe to join our growing telemedicine practice. Possible someone with experience working with Mental/Behavioral Health providers. The ideal candidate will have a medical background (medicine, nursing, pharmacy, or similar) and relevant work experience as a virtual assistant. Your responsibilities will start with coordinating the intake/scheduling of patients and data entry into the EHR but can grow into other areas as we get experience working together. Experience working with EHRs (particularly Karo EHR) and an outpatient practice environment is ideal. We are seeking individuals with excellent customer service. More details can be provided to candidates after an initial screening.\r\nSkills required.\r\nCommunications: Fluent in English\r\nMedical Transcription/Scribes support\r\nHandling intake calls\r\nSchedule appointment\r\nScreening new clients\r\nReturning client calls promptly with a high degree of professionalism.\r\nCoordinating new client intake forms\r\nGenerating superbills for clients to submit to their insurance companies.\r\nBenefits and Eligibility insurance Verification\r\nProcessing Co-Pays and Self Pays\r\nPrecertification and pre-authorization\r\nClaims submission.\r\nFollow up on insurance companies for status of claims.\r\nResearch, correct and re-submit rejected or denied claims.\r\nPrepare appeals to denied claims and authorizations.\r\nAbility to read and interpret EOBs and post payments.\r\nCreate patient payment plan/agreements.\r\nManaging emails and voicemails\r\nUpdating client electronic health records\r\nSocial Media Management\r\nProofing and editing\r\nCREDENTIALING\r\n- Set up EDI/ERA/EFT enrollments.\r\n- Credentialing and Contracting with Commercial payers and government insurances','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1641833137355378689','-',7,'United States','Dacula',4.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-03-31',1,'2023-03-31',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-03-31 20:42:25',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
