(16305,'Credentialing Specialist ( Hospital Provileges, Insurances, Nursing Facilities, Surgery Centers)',24,'This position is responsible for the credentialing of physicians and allied health providers. Prior credentialing experience in licensing, hospital medical staff office (MSO), Physician Practice, or Healthcare background is required. Must be computer literate and possess exceptional oral and written communication and customer service skills.\r\nJob Duties\r\nCredentialing/ Re-credentialing (hospitals, surgery centers, SNF, ALF, insurance):\r\nPrepare individual files for each new physician/ mid-level with all their documentation\r\nAdd new/remove any physician/ mid-level to the malpractice insurance\r\nRequest pre-app/ application\r\nE-mail completed applications with required documents\r\nFollow-up to check status and submit anything that is missing\r\nUpdate all excel logs (Doctor’s info, Mid-level info, Expiration, Credentialing\r\nComplete any re-credentialing applications and submit required documents\r\nRenew any expiring licenses/ certificates\r\nAdd new physicians to insurances\r\nUpdate addresses on medical license, DEA, insurances, etc.…\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\nHigh School Diploma . Some college is preferred\r\nExperience in credentialing physicians for state licensing\r\nExperience in medical insurance credentialing\r\nCredentialing experience in a hospital medical staff office (MSO) ), Physician Practice, or Healthcare background.\r\nDemonstrated problem-solving and attention to detail skills\r\nExperience with Parallon is preferred\r\nExcellent oral and written communication as well as interpersonal skills with a focus on internal/external customer satisfaction\r\nAbility to work under pressure and be adaptable to change\r\nAttention to detail and accuracy','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1641901239015329793','-',7,'United States','-',18.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-03-31',1,'2023-03-31',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2