(16563,'New Website',19,'Hello,\r\n\r\n\r\n   I would like to create a website as a gift for a youtuber that I think is doing positive work. I want this to be a surprise. Please see below as a guide for the website\r\n\r\n\r\nYoutube channel: https://www.youtube.com/@juniorlifestyleoffishing\r\n\r\nKey Person: Junior\r\n\r\nHis Team: Shortman and D&G\r\n\r\n\r\nI would recommend you visit his page and view the videos. He mainly does fishing and then cooking afterwards. It should be a family friendly website.\r\n\r\n\r\nI would like to see a section on, About Lifestyle of Fishing, Videos, Cooking, Purchase, Donate, Discussion\r\n\r\n\r\nIn the about section he can add contents about him (junior), shortman, D&G and others\r\n\r\nin the videos section should be videos from youtube on the page\r\n\r\nIn the cooking page it can go over videos of him and his team cooking as well as recipes \r\n\r\nIn purchases it should offer merchandises connected to his paypal page so people can order cups, shirts, books, hats etc,\r\n\r\nIn the donate page it should go to his paypal donate page\r\n\r\nIn the discussion page it should have a discussion forum where people can leave comments and feedback etc\r\n\r\n\r\nI would like to see for the main page to have a banner containing Junior and his team with Junior being in the center of the banner\r\n\r\n\r\nPlease quote accordingly.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2049684','-',7,'United States','-',1500.000,'fixed',1500.000,'2023-04-03',1,'2023-04-03',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-03 19:34:26',NULL,16,1,NULL,136),
(16564,'Review and Advise on a Mobile App',6,'We built an App that judges will use on Apple iPads to judge/score contestants at a culinary event. We want someone who is an expert at building these types of Apps to review what we\'ve built and make sure it\'s as efficient as possible. After some initial testing, we are experiencing areas of the system that take 3-4 seconds to post/save. For example, after entering a score, it takes 3-4 seconds to move to the Comments field to write a comment.  Or, after taking a photo of the meal, it takes a few seconds to post the image. The client wanted things to save as they go so maybe how we wrote that aspect of the code could be done better? We\'ll want whoever is hired to get on Teams/Zoom meetings to work with our developer in real time. Thanks.','https://www.guru.com/work/detail/2049072','-',7,'United States','-',2000.000,'fixed',2000.000,'2023-04-03',1,'2023-04-03',1,'-',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-03 19:35:09',NULL,16,1,NULL,136),
