(16798,'Medical Assistant for Home Health and Hospice',22,'Selftone, LLC is seeking a qualified and dedicated medical assistant to join our administrative office supporting home health and hospice clients remotely. The ideal candidate would have a background in nursing and coding. In this position, you will be responsible for a variety of tasks requiring data analysis, in-depth evaluation, and sound judgment. As our medical assistant, your daily duties will include medical documentation review, care coordination, and supporting general medical administrative functions.\r\n\r\nTo succeed in this role, you must possess in-depth knowledge of Form 485 Plan of Care for home health agencies. The ideal candidate must also be able to demonstrate excellent written and verbal communication skills.\r\n\r\n\r\nJOB REQUIREMENTS:\r\n\r\nKnowledge of medical terminology and human anatomy is critical\r\n\r\nA strong work ethic your teammates can rely on\r\n\r\nStrong team spirit and “team-first” mentality\r\n\r\nA bright, problem-solving mindset + attention to detail\r\n\r\nPersonability (enjoy talking to people, and talking to patients in particular [note that this role\r\ninvolves primarily phone-based and virtual encounters])\r\n\r\nTech savvy\r\n\r\nMedical Assistant (MA) or Certified Nursing Assistant (CNA) qualification is an advantag','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1643238260732350465','-',7,'United States','-',6.000,'perhour',6.000,'2023-04-04',1,'2023-04-04',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-04 16:07:38',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
