(16974,'Medical Office Manager with billing and credentialing experience. Remote',29,'Qualifications/Experience\r\n\r\nMinimum High School diploma (Required)\r\n• Certified Medical Manager (CMM) or Certified Medical Practice Executive (CMPE), an advantage\r\n\r\n• Minimum of two (2) years of work in a medical office setting\r\n• Strong organizational and critical thinking skills\r\n• Demonstratable experience with reviewing, submitting, analyzing, and adhering to the billing revenue cycle\r\n• Experience with regulations related to Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial insurance\r\n. Should have credentialing experience.\r\n. Proficient in administrative duties, such as responding to emails, returning phone calls, and responding to patient inquiries.\r\n• Experience with HIPAA rules and regulations\r\n• Strong customer experience skills, computer literacy, and writing skills\r\n•Demonstrable skill in using EMR healthcare software, Athena health\r\n•Experience with continuous process improvement concepts\r\n\r\nResponsibilities\r\n\r\nThis role is pivotal in ensuring that the overall day-to-day business operations of the office are run smoothly and professionally. The overall responsibilities of the successful candidate will be to;\r\n\r\n• Oversee and support all administrative duties in the office and ensure that the office is operating smoothly.\r\n• Scheduling appointments for patients and providing intake documents, maintaining calendars, doing research, and creating reports.\r\n•Utilize knowledge of continuous quality improvement principles to analyze and execute improvements in office operations and quality of care\r\n•Work with prescribers to ensure accurate medication authorization and refills\r\n•Ensure patient records are current and accurate\r\n• Communicate with patients regarding inquiries and complaints.\r\n. Ensure all credentials are up to date\r\n•Create excellent customer experiences.\r\n•Oversee eligibility and insurance authorizations and discharges\r\n\r\n•Develop office policies and procedures and ensure appropriate implementation.\r\n•Utilize guidelines to ensure compliance with current healthcare regulations.\r\n\r\n• Designate work/office area that supports applicable privacy laws to conduct the day-to-day operations of the business\r\n• Attend virtual meetings and provide weekly updates and reports\r\n• Ensure regular status reports are due\r\n\r\nCompany Description\r\nA privately owned behavioral health practice that provides quality mental health services. Our mission is to engage, educate and empower all communities. We treat men, women, and children of all background with mental health issues. We therefore seek to improve the quality of life and wellbeing of individuals and families successfully.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1643598563529818113','-',7,'United States','Shelburne',20.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-05',1,'2023-04-05',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-05 13:26:34',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
