(17057,'Junior Web Designer & Developer (WordPress & Webflow)',15,'THIS JOB POSTING IS FOR A FULL TIME 40 HR PER WEEK POSITION. THIS IS NOT FOR AGENCY WORK.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a talented and experienced web designer and developer with expertise in WordPress and willingness to learn Webflow to join our team at [Name of Veterinary Marketing Agency]. As our Web Designer & Developer, you will be responsible for creating visually appealing and functional websites for our clients in the veterinary industry.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n- Design and develop WordPress websites from scratch\r\n- Develop custom WordPress themes and plugins\r\n- Develop websites using Webflow and other web design tools\r\n- Ensure websites are optimized for speed and SEO\r\n- Collaborate with clients and team members to create effective and visually appealing designs\r\n- Keep up-to-date with industry trends and technologies\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- 3+ years of experience in web design and development\r\n- Strong knowledge of WordPress, including custom theme and plugin development\r\n- Experience with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\r\n- Familiarity with Webflow or willingness to learn\r\n- Experience working in a marketing agency or with clients in the veterinary industry is a plus\r\n- Strong communication and collaboration skills\r\n\r\nBenefits:\r\n\r\n- Competitive salary\r\n- Quarterly Bonus\'\r\n- Paid time off and holidays\r\n- Opportunities for professional development and growth\r\n\r\nIf you are a talented web designer and developer with a passion for creating beautiful and functional websites, we want to hear from you. Please submit your resume, portfolio, and a cover letter explaining why you would be a good fit for this position. We look forward to hearing from you!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01450660a7b908631a','-',7,'United States','Pembroke Pines',1000.000,'fixed',1000.000,'2023-04-05',1,'2023-04-05',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-05 17:16:09',