(17098,'Wordpress Designer',3,'Job Summary:\r\nWe are seeking a talented WordPress UX Designer to join our team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for creating user-friendly and visually appealing WordPress designs that meet our clients\' needs. The UX Designer will work closely with our development team to ensure that the designs are integrated seamlessly into our clients\' websites.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n\r\nDevelop and maintain WordPress themes and plugins to create intuitive and user-friendly websites\r\nCollaborate with clients, stakeholders, and development team to identify design requirements and objectives\r\nDesign wireframes, prototypes, and visual designs that effectively communicate the desired user experience\r\nConduct user testing and gather feedback to refine designs\r\nWork with developers to ensure that designs are implemented accurately and efficiently\r\nStay up-to-date with emerging trends in WordPress design and UX/UI best practices','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1643699237605543937','-',7,'United States','Chardon',55.000,'Open this select menu',48.000,'2023-04-05',1,'2023-04-05',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-05 19:44:30',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
(17099,'Design PowerPoint Presentation',28,'Use Experian Health template for slides.\r\n\r\nSlide #1 Agenda\r\n\r\n-Industry Trends\r\n\r\n-Optimal Health System challenges\r\n\r\n-Experian technology solutions\r\n\r\n-Customer Success Stories\r\n\r\n-Why Experian\r\n\r\n-Next Steps\r\n\r\nSlide #2 State of Claims Survey- 200 Healthcare Executives( add graphics from page 5, Executive Summary attached)\r\n\r\nDenials are increasing, Better Technology is Needed, Everyone is looking to improve Processes.\r\n\r\nSlide #3 Optimal Healthcare System Challenges\r\n\r\n“The registration process is complicated, expectations on all sides stressed, too many tools, broken processes “…..Optum Health employee”\r\n\r\nRegistration errors leading to increase in denials, decreased collections, and revenue loss\r\n\r\nTeam members frustrated/overworked/short staffed\r\n\r\nTraining Difficult to manage, Tools not easy to utilize, 12 sign-ons\r\n\r\nLack of Visibility to pinpoint areas of improvement\r\n\r\nKPI’s difficult to measure/manage\r\n\r\nCustomer Satisfaction scores have declined\r\n\r\nSlide #4-5 Experian Solutions – We turn complicated into uncomplicated\r\n\r\nImagine if you could reduce your denials by 10% and your cash collections by 40%, all while improving employee and customer satisfaction…..what would your boss say….. how would your team feel?\r\n\r\nECare Next\r\n\r\nsingle sign on- training, learning, tools embedded- saving time, reducing friction, streamlining process\r\n\r\nPower Reporting\r\n\r\nProvides real time enterprise view and metrics\r\n\r\nIdentifies initial denials so that they can be corrected (lagging indicator)\r\n\r\nHelps identify bottlenecks in workflow (actions plans developed)\r\n\r\nProvides error data by team member and facility\r\n\r\nRewards and Recognizes team members\r\n\r\nKPI measurement in real time\r\n\r\nSlide #6 Customer Success Story’s\r\n\r\nExperian customers that utilize solutions have fewer denials, higher collections, better customer satisfaction and meet/exceed KPI’s\r\n\r\nBlessing Healthcare System\r\n\r\n“Experian Health provided our staff with a reliable, real-time registration error alerting process. Our overall registration accuracy rate has improved significantly since implementing eCare NEXT. We now have the tools we need to be successful in one, user friendly application.” —Jill Stroot, Director, Patient Access, Blessing Health System\r\n\r\nBanner Health\r\n\r\n“ Our partnership with Experian Health helps Banner Health\'s revenue cycle team deliver on its mission of “getting it right, at the right time, every time.” — Becky Peters, Executive Director of Patient Access Services, Banner.\r\n30M decrease in eligibility errors.\r\n\r\n\r\nSlide #7 ( use WHY section from attached brochure to make a slide)\r\n\r\n\r\nSlide # 8Next Steps (Bridge) to Success – add graphics of a bridge','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1643701203132289025','-',7,'United States','US',65.000,'perhour',30.000,'2023-04-05',1,'2023-04-05',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-05 19:46:50',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
