(17124,'Website Redesign',4,'General: The client liked the David Aylor (https://davidaylor.com) as well as the LA Century (https://lacenturylaw.com/) websites.\r\n\r\nYou will be provided the client website upon acceptance of the job.\r\n\r\nDesign:\r\nCrisp, Clean, Informative but not sterile, relaxed website. He doesn’t care to showcase himself but more of what he can do for his clients.\r\nColors: Dark Blue, Yellow\r\n\r\nThe design should be well thought-out, with all styling being pretty consistent for the different sections. Remember to keep in mind informative, relaxed. They want to make it clear that they want to focus on how they can help solve the clients problem, NOT the typical “look how good I am” lawyer website tone.\r\n\r\nPlease review the project brief, as well as our attached guidelines and examples thoroughly. WE NEED YOUR CREATIVITY ADDED TO THIS.\r\n\r\nThis Client has an existing site: This will be given once contract is approved\r\nFonts: No particular font but once again liked the David Aylor look\r\nTagline: Got Hurt? Get Gibbons?\r\nOn Their homepage they don’t like the hero section and how it just showcases the lawyer. They rather show a smaller picture of the lawyer but really showcase his google reviews and have information for his potential clients. Wants to focus on how he can solve your problem.\r\nWants the injured guy logo beside his name in the header\r\n\r\nIdeal Audience: Personal Injury victim in Philadelphia, PA, seeking legal representation in a personal injury matter, who need reassurance that the attorney they are hiring is well qualified, respected, effective, personable, and fierce. We want the client to understand they can trust and talk to their lawyer easily. No need for lawyer talk.\r\n\r\nPages Needed: We need Desktop AND Mobile designs for the following page types\r\n\r\nThe sections for each page type are listed in order below, please design all sections in accordance with our guidelines and using your best design judgement\r\n\r\nReviews and social proof are paramount to making this design.\r\n\r\nHomepage: Needs to have the following\r\n\r\nHero Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines.\r\nDoesn’t want the hero page to talk just about himself. Rather showcase his google reviews which he is proud of and for the Hero section to be informative.\r\nClient Reviews Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nWould like this to filter through his reviews automatically.\r\nCase Results section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nThey want the case results to follow the same order they have on the current website. He wants it to go from most difficult to less difficult.\r\nPractice Area Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines - however we’d like this to be called “How Can We Help?” How can we help section: They have this currently on their website but it needs to worked differently. Title saying: How did you get hurt? With the practice areas listed below and stating if you don’t see your specific area please contact us.\r\nPractice areas: Car Accidents, Motorcycle Accidents, Slip and Fall Accidents, SEPTA Accidents, Dog Bites and Attacks, Work Accidents, Medical Malpractice, Nursing Home Neglect and Abuse, DUI Defense, Criminal Record Expungement,\r\n\r\nCase Process- designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nMultiple call to action sections - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nClient Testimonials section (comprised of videos)\r\nMeet the Attorneys Section\r\nA contact us section\r\nWants access to his book to be on the homepage. Where they click on it and they are able to download it. The book is already on his current website homepage.\r\n\r\nInterior Page:\r\n\r\nHeading/Hero Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines - remember to prominently feature reviews. Make them the main focus at the top of this page.\r\nClient Reviews Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nCase Results section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nPage Content Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nRelated Videos Section - This section should contain videos that correlate with that page on the bottom:\r\nHe has short YouTube clips that we want to associate those with the specific practice areas. Add a button on the bottom that says “watch a 30 second video” once clicked YouTube video will pop up.\r\nProminent Call-To-Action section (in accordance with our guidelines,)\r\nFooter- designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\n\r\nAbout Us: Follow our guidelines which are attached for the below\r\n\r\nHero/Heading Section\r\n3 lawyers, 2 assistance\r\nReviews\r\nResults\r\nClient Testimonials section (comprised of videos)\r\nFooter\r\n\r\nNotes on Common Sections:\r\n\r\nFooter should contain the footer elements outlined in our guidelines\r\n\r\nMenu Bar:\r\n\r\nThe Menu Items should be same, however the header of the site should be redesigned according or our guidelines which are attached.\r\n\r\nAttach are our guidelines and the injured man logo\r\n\r\nThe logo that is attached all we need is the injured man nothing in black and white.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1643722766880813057','-',7,'United States','Greenville',1800.000,'Open this select menu',1800.000,'2023-04-05',1,'2023-04-05',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-05 21:11:26',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
(17125,'Virtual Assistant for Busy Solopreneur',22,'Busy solopreneur and mother seeking virtual assistant to help with various tasks in running a medical consulting company. Looking for someone that is a self starter and eager to learn with a sharp attention to detail. The ideal candidate will be personable and communicate quickly and efficiently. The ideal candidate will be familiar with:\r\n\r\n-Create and maintain virtual business card\r\n-Manage calendly account\r\n-Update and manage MTR website through Thinkific – create landing pages, upload recordings and manage sales\r\n-Update DSK website – GoDaddy – add a new page for speaking engagements\r\n-Create blog page – manage and update\r\n-Create the ability to book consultation sessions directly on my website with payment ability using Stripe\r\n-Post and manage social media accounts – through Hootesuite or other software\r\n-Invoice clients monthly – Harvest\r\n-Create and manage Coaching website – starting from scratch – also fold in Teachable for coaching options\r\n-Data entry\r\n-Research topics when requested\r\n-Research schedule travel etc\r\n-Mailchimp (to assist with monthly newsletter creation, sending and tracking statistics)\r\n-MS Office Suite (to assist in data entry, letter writing, PowerPoint presentation editing, email correspondence with clients)\r\n-Google Suite of Services\r\n-HIPAA certification is a plus\r\n-Podcast creation and management','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1643718896144814081','-',7,'United States','dallas',18.000,'Open this select menu',18.000,'2023-04-05',1,'2023-04-05',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-05 21:11:43',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
