(17256,'Publication Designer for DC Communications Firm',2,'Graphic Designer Job Description\r\n\r\nAffinity Media Consulting LLC is a full service communications firm located in Ward 7 of Washington, D.C. delivering quality communications and marketing services. With more than 25 years industry experience, we serve as brand partners to a wide variety of industries including: nonprofit organizations, education, healthcare, accounting/finance, retail and wholesale, technology, and government agencies. We are building a design team for Affinity Media Consulting. Our top priority is to find graphic designers who share our five core values:\r\nBe human.\r\nBe honest.\r\nBe proactive.\r\nBe strategic.\r\nBe accountable.\r\n\r\nPurpose: Significantly improve our clients ability to connect with target audiences through effective communication.\r\nOur Niche: Content development and production for government agencies, nonprofits, magazine publishers, and corporate businesses.\r\n\r\nDo you have rockstar skills at developing the overall layout and production design for various applications such as advertisements, brochures, magazines, corporate reports, and digital graphics? If so, keep reading.\r\n\r\nThe main responsibilities include:\r\nMeeting with the production or social media manager to understand their design requirements and objectives.\r\nDeveloping design concepts, graphics, and layouts for magazines, newspapers, reports, directories, logos, and infographics.\r\nCreating visual elements such as icons, logos, and illustrations.\r\nDesigning marketing materials, such as brochures, flyers, and newsletters.\r\nCreating layouts for print and digital publications, including magazines and newspapers.\r\nSelecting and preparing typography, images, and other design elements.\r\nCollaborating with other members of the creative team to ensure consistent branding and messaging.\r\nEnsuring that designs are visually appealing and meet established design standards and brand guidelines.\r\n\r\nREQUIREMENTS:\r\nmeet deadlines EVERY TIME\r\npay attention to details\r\ndesign with such detail that no more than two proofs are required to receive approval.\r\nuse InDesign, Photoshop and/or Illustrator CC 2023, Canva or Adobe Express\r\nstick to paragraph style sheets\r\nuse grep styles (optional)\r\ncommit to working with Affinity Media Consulting for at least 6 months\r\nopen to using new software to speed up production\r\nWork up to 25 hours per week (flexible)\r\n2 years experience or college degree required\r\n\r\nTo become a successful graphic designer, one needs to have a strong understanding of design principles, typography, color theory, and visual communication. Strong computer skills and proficiency in graphic design software, such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, and Canva or Adobe Express are also essential. Additionally, a degree in graphic design or a related field is often required, along with a strong portfolio showcasing one\'s design work.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644000414906257409?success','-',7,'United States','Washington',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-04-06',1,'2023-04-06',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-06 15:34:47',NULL,17,3,NULL,119),
