(17277,'Website Load Speed Expert - WordPress Elementor',3,'Looking for an expert to make these corrections to my WordPress Elementor website. I received the below issue suggestions.\r\n\r\n11 image(s) without explicit width and height tags.\r\n\r\nThese tags help your browser understand how big an image is going to be before it’s actually loaded, making sure that the page layout doesn’t shift around during loading.\r\n\r\nMost sites have some level of layout shift (often called “cumulative layout shift,” or CLS) before the page fully loads, but having too much can be a problem.\r\n\r\nIf a page partially loads and the user tries to click a link, they could click a completely different link if the page layout shifts enough.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644005813849108481','-',7,'United States','Phoenix',80.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-04-06',1,'2023-04-06',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-06 16:08:09',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
