(17404,'Administrative/virtual Assistant',22,'We are seeking an outgoing, detail-oriented, efficient person to join our psychotherapy practice. The ideal candidate will be adept at prioritizing, multi-tasking, and having a positive attitude. This candidate will also be willing to learn and grow with us! Currently, the position is 100% remote due to COVID. The position has flexibility in scheduling, though work must be during business hours. More hours and expanded responsibilities such as intake and/or billing tasks will be available for the right candidate.\r\n\r\n\r\nSchedule: Part-time; Design your own schedule: 5-15 hours per week, initially 8:00 AM - 6 PST\r\nPM Monday - Friday, Saturday from 9-1.\r\n\r\nThis role will report to the Clinic Director.\r\n\r\nTo succeed in this role …..\r\n\r\nYou will rock this role if you possess excellent communication skills and the ability to lead and promote the vision of the clinic. You must be able to stay extremely organized, think 10 steps ahead, and have the ability to see the big picture with an entrepreneurial mindset. You have a passion for helping others as you will be communicating with our clients.\r\n\r\nQualifications\r\n\r\n2-3 years of experience in Client Care and Customer Service (preferably in a medical office at the front desk)\r\nPsychology graduates are welcome!\r\nBasic computer skills\r\nBasic spreadsheet experience\r\nScheduling experience\r\nPrior experience with electronic medical records (EMR) software\r\nSome familiarity with how health insurance coverage works\r\nAbility to adjust communication style to relate authentically with individuals of diverse abilities, backgrounds, and interaction styles\r\nDesire to learn and become skilled in healthcare systems and processes\r\nResponsibilities\r\n\r\nSupporting therapists with client bookings, payments, administrating intake & consent forms, etc.\r\nClient support: answering/returning client calls and emails, processing payments, sending invoices\r\nMaintaining Quality Assurance (follow up to payments, securing payment information, uploading secure documents, managing the booking software including schedules and treatments offered)\r\nSkills & Attributes of our ideal candidate….\r\n\r\nDynamic, self-motivated individual with the ability to work independently, proactively, and well under pressure\r\nStrong communication skills, ability to communicate professionally and with compassion to clients with patience when dealing with challenging clients\r\nConfidence to share ideas and constructive criticism to help us grow\r\nJuggling multiple projects and to-do’s simultaneously is no problem for you — you work well under pressure, meet deadlines and keep promises\r\nTech savvy (we are mostly paper-less and everything is online)\r\nAn appetite for innovation and simplicity who is highly process oriented\r\nWorking autonomously comes easy to you but you also love collaborating\r\nConsiderable experience using the Microsoft Office Suite, Google Drive Suite, Gmail, Dropbox, Mac, Windows in a work environment\r\n\r\nAbout Us\r\n\r\nWe provide therapy services to children and families. Our goal is to help families heal from trauma and overcome challenges related to behavioral issues, school problems, attention-deficit disorders, anxiety, and depression. We place a strong emphasis on combining art and play-based therapies and other evidenced based techniques to teach the skills necessary to help children and families succeed.\r\n\r\nOur office is conveniently located on NW 23rd Ave in Portland, Oregon, and offers both in-person and tele-health appointments.\r\n\r\nOur Vision\r\n\r\nWe help children and families in our community heal from complex trauma and restore balance and connection through evidence-based practices.\r\n\r\nOur Core Values\r\n\r\nAuthenticity\r\n\r\nLearn and Be Curious\r\n\r\nDiversity and inclusion\r\n\r\nCommunity, Collaboration, Respect, and Empowerment\r\n\r\nBalance\r\n\r\nApplication Process:\r\n\r\nIn addition to submitting a resume and cover letter:\r\n\r\nPlease complete the Big 5 personality test (https://www.123test.com/personality-test/) and share your results during the hiring process.\r\nWe thank all applicants for their interests: Only those under consideration will be contacted.\r\n\r\nFor more info on our practice, check out our website: www.happyvalleycounseling.com\r\n\r\nJob Type: Part-time, potential for full time,\r\nFlexible schedule\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nExperience:\r\n\r\nCustomer service: 1 year (Preferred)\r\nLanguage: English, Spanish (Preferred, not required)\r\nWork Location: Remote','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644082107603582977','-',7,'United States','Happy Valley',10.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-06',1,'2023-04-06',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-06 21:00:40',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
