(17566,'Receptionist & Virtual Assistant with Medical knowledge',22,'A New York-based medical services company, 30 years established, is seeking a reliable and experienced Phone Receptionist to help in the process of receiving, preparing and reviewing radiology study information that assists in the production of X-ray study reports. Must be adept at grammar, and have a strong grasp of medical language and terms. Looking for an individual to work on a regular schedule, Monday through Friday from 11 AM - 5 PM EST, with the flexibility to also cover the occasional morning when needed. Must be willing to act as phone receptionist, including the answering of phone calls and managing the incoming caller’s request, when needed.\r\n\r\nDuties would include but not limited to :\r\n\r\nVerify accuracy of patient and study information such as name and identification number.\r\nVerify accuracy of transcription for correct punctuation, grammar, and spelling.\r\nProofread and edit written study reports, produced by our radiologists, into final study reports to be delivered to clients.\r\nFollow up with the Radiologist, when needed, to ensure the accuracy of the reports.\r\nCommunicate with supervisor or others as needed to yield intended reports.\r\nAbility to answer phones during agreed-to work hours, when needed.\r\nAnswer incoming telephone calls, determine the purpose of callers, and deal with as per company instructions.\r\nAssist BVR clients with requests regarding study reports and re-delivering reports when needed\r\n\r\nSkills/Qualifications:\r\n\r\n- Knowledge of medical terminology and preferably experience with radiology transcription.\r\n- Accurate proofreading skills with strong attention to details.\r\n- Knowledge base in Anatomy, and Medical Terminology.\r\n- You must have excellent US English grammar skills, oral and written.\r\n- Efficient typing skills; must be able to type 55+ WPM.\r\n- Clear communication skills, follow instructions, and must be consistently reliable.\r\n- Computer skills – proficient with Microsoft Office products and Google Suite.\r\n- Comfortable with computers and digital communication (Hangouts, email, remote desktop, etc.)\r\n- Ability to learn and work with our company’s internal transcription software.\r\n- Must have reliable internet, software, and hardware to work remotely.\r\n- Has knowledge of HIPPA and will maintain the confidentiality of patient information.\r\n\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nThe selected candidate will be required to:\r\n- Sign a Confidentiality Agreement and a Business Associate\'s Agreement.\r\n- Agree to work a regular schedule of days and hours.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644334935169765377','-',7,'United States','Queens',20.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-07',1,'2023-04-07',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-07 14:41:00',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(17567,'Logo design',10,'I need help with a logo design for my fitness and health website. The concept is just minimalist, clean, and have a \"flow\" which is the theme of my fitness classes.\r\n\r\nI have one started already but need help cleaning it up and maybe having a few other options. It\'s just in black and white but am open to colour as long as its a soothing more calm colour.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~017259cf355248c551','-',7,'United States','Burnaby',0.000,'perhour',30.000,'2023-04-07',1,'2023-04-07',1,'N/A',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-07 14:41:05',NULL,18,3,NULL,146),
(17568,'Content and Writing Manager-Regulatory Affairs Experience in Medical Devices Industry (EU MDR/IVDR)',37,'**Positions available:**\r\n\r\n- 40 hours a week - Up to $25/ hour\r\n\r\n**Job Summary:**\r\nWe are seeking a skilled LinkedIn Social Media Coordinator (Article Writer+ Linkedin Manager) to manage our social media presence on LinkedIn. The ideal candidate will be passionate about the medical device industry, specifically the MDR/IVDR regulations, and have experience in creating and managing engaging and effective social media content.\r\n\r\n**About the company:**\r\n\r\nCite Medical is a relatively new startup (5 years) that’s changing the way device manufacturers approach their Clinical Evaluation. Through a highly focused team and proprietary software platform, CiteMed can offer a depth of service that traditional ‘consulting firms’ can’t match.\r\n\r\nWorking with us will bring you into a high-paced and autonomous environment where creativity and initiative are valued, not stifled. The main services CiteMed Provides relate to:\r\n\r\n- Clinical Trials and evaluations\r\n- Post Market Surveillance\r\n- With other services being added\r\n- Device Development\r\n- Quality management\r\n- Med Comms\r\n\r\n**Responsibilities:**\r\n\r\n- Create and curate high-quality, engaging content (including posts, articles, images, and videos) that aligns with our brand and messaging.\r\n- Develop and implement a social media strategy for LinkedIn that supports our business objectives and targets our key audience in the medical device industry with the key objectives of\r\n- Driving impressions on linkedin\r\n- Increasing website traffic\r\n- Expanding our Emailing list\r\n- Defining the landscape of what can be improved within our content strategy\r\n- Monitor and respond to comments and messages on LinkedIn, fostering engagement and building relationships with our followers.\r\n- Use analytics and insights to track the effectiveness of our social media efforts and continually improve our strategy.\r\n- Collaborate with colleagues to align social media efforts with broader marketing and sales campaigns.\r\n- Stay up-to-date with the latest trends and best practices in social media marketing and the medical device industry.\r\n\r\n**Required Experience:**\r\n\r\n- Strong knowledge of the medical device industry and the MDR/IVDR regulations.\r\n- 2+ years of article writing experience with special emphasis on medical devices and MDR/ IVDR regulations\r\n- Proven experience managing social media accounts, specifically LinkedIn.\r\n- Fluent written and spoken English\r\n- Familiarity with social media analytics tools and ability to interpret data.\r\n- Ability to work independently and as part of a team.\r\n- Proven ability to solve problems creatively\r\n- You will fit this role well if:\r\n- You enjoy being given freedom in your work to make decisions to achieve targets for the business in the way you think is best.\r\n- You have had opinions or ideas that you would like to implement but haven’t been able to in other companies.\r\n\r\n**Desired Experience:**\r\n\r\n- Knowledge of SEO\r\n- Knowledge of Email marketing methods\r\n- Knowledge of General Social media marketing methodology','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644350005110657025','-',7,'United States','Chicago',30.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-07',1,'2023-04-07',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-07 14:44:08',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
