(17655,'Material UI Front-end Developer for React Application',6,'We are a fast-growing online casino startup looking for a talented front-end developer with experience in React and Material UI to join our team. As a Material UI Front-end Developer, you will be responsible for developing and implementing user interfaces for our online casino platform, ensuring our users have an engaging and seamless experience.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nCollaborate with the development team to implement new features and functionalities for the online casino platform using React and Material UI.\r\nBuild reusable components and libraries for future use across the platform.\r\nDevelop and maintain code standards and best practices for front-end development.\r\nOptimize application for maximum speed and scalability.\r\nEnsure cross-browser compatibility and responsiveness of the platform.\r\nContinuously improve user experience by implementing the latest design trends and best practices.\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nProven experience in front-end development using React and Material UI.\r\nStrong understanding of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Git.\r\nExperience in developing responsive and scalable user interfaces.\r\nKnowledge of Redux, Webpack (bonus), and Git.\r\nExperience working in Agile development methodologies.\r\nExcellent communication skills and ability to work in a team environment.\r\nPassion for learning new technologies and keeping up-to-date with industry trends.\r\nIf you are a highly motivated and skilled front-end developer with experience in React and Material UI, and you are excited to be a part of a fast-growing startup, then we want to hear from you! Please submit your resume and portfolio for consideration.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644399124039405569','-',7,'United States','Perth',30.000,'perhour',30.000,'2023-04-07',1,'2023-04-07',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-07 18:05:35',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
(17656,'UX/UI Expertise for New App Build',6,'Seeking UX/UI talent to work on small updates to current web-based app, plus new app build and a new website.\r\n\r\nThis is for an initial 15-20 hrs per month (flexible, remote) with the potential for a long-term assignment. Start date on April 18. Must be available April 21 between 11:00-5:00 pm PST for new build deep dive (video ok).\r\n\r\nHire will join our tech team, including a project manager, developer, and tech advisor.\r\n\r\nMust-have skills:\r\n• Information architecture\r\n• Content management systems\r\n• User & product research & testing\r\n• Knowledge of accessibility best practices\r\n• Understanding of SEO\r\n• Ability to interpret our brand mission & standards\r\n\r\nPreferred Skills:\r\n• Knowledge of Vue.js\r\n• Experience with both B2B & B2C markets','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1644400306152820737','-',7,'United States','San Francisco',50.000,'Open this select menu',48.000,'2023-04-07',1,'2023-04-07',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-07 18:12:10',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
