(17900,'AR Dispute Specialist',28,'Reporting directly to the Sr. AR Supervisor, the AR Dispute Specialist will review customer invoices and contracts for billing accuracy and apply logical judgment to make corrections as necessary. The AR Dispute Specialist will be responsible for research, analysis and resolution of high volume, complex customer accounts receivable, order entry exceptions and disputes involving contractual agreements and non-standard billing agreements for all customers.\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n● Investigate, research, and resolve outstanding disputed invoices.\r\n● Audits & correct disputed invoices submitted by internal and external customers\r\n● Provides final dispute resolution and revised invoice(s) directly to customers.\r\n● Identifies root cause of billing disputes, reports process deficiencies and recommends process improvements to create efficiencies and reduce errors\r\n● Analyzes invoices for billing accuracy, works with internal teams to ensure that revenue is applied correctly to invoices\r\n● Customer conference calls to discuss invoice disputes and solutions\r\n● Timely response to customer telephone and email inquiries\r\n● Prepares and submits requests in NetSuite\r\n● Reviews and interprets complex customer contracts and determines the applicable rule set for the invoicing\r\n● Acts as a representative for Flock to ensure that established Invoicing Policy is upheld during customer disputes\r\nRequired Qualifications:\r\n● 1-year experience in accounting, invoicing or freight audit, OTC, accounts receivable or accounts payable\r\n● Experience working in a high volume environment.\r\n● Ability to work with agility and minimal oversight\r\n● Excellent time management skills with a proven ability to meet deadlines\r\n● Critical thinking and problem-solving abilities\r\n● Clear and concise verbal and written communication skills; ability to communicate with customers, associates, and management in a professional manner\r\n● Bachelor\'s degree or equivalent related work or military experience\r\n● Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint) and other business applications\r\n● Ability to work independently and as a team with shared responsibilities\r\n● Demonstrated ability to follow up, multitask, and prioritize\r\n● Previous experience evaluating customer contract\r\n● Ability to prioritize work toward department and company goals','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645502454146093057','-',7,'United States','Solana Beach',10.000,'Open this select menu',18.000,'2023-04-10',1,'2023-04-10',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-10 20:22:22',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
