(17915,'Content writer for Major Health & Medical Publisher',37,'Looking for a strong technical writer to produce 1500-2000 word, originally-authored articles. Articles are to be posted on GlobalRPH.com which is a leading drug reference and clinical site in the healthcare category. Familiarity with WordPress and Yoast! SEO plugin, Copyscape, and/or on-page SEO best practices are plusses.\r\n\r\nArticles produced will be based on existing 3rd party journal articles. Current examples of articles we need would include:\r\nhttps://globalrph.com/2023/03/whats-the-difference-between-dental-inflammation-and-infection/\r\nhttps://globalrph.com/2022/12/carfilzomib-therapy-in-pediatric-acute-lymphoblastic-leukemia/\r\nhttps://globalrph.com/2022/12/golimumab-compliance-in-arthritis-treatment/\r\n\r\nThis is a long terms assignment. We are looking to pay on a standard per-word basis up to a maximum of $60 per article. English proficiency is required.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645513304634650625','-',7,'United States','Hawthorne',60.000,'fixed',60.000,'2023-04-10',1,'2023-04-10',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-10 21:00:18',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(17916,'Medical billing expertise in addiction medicine needed to conduct an internal audit',21,'We are seeking an experienced and knowledgeable medical billing and coding specialist to review our internal billing strategies and provide suggestions or recommendations on ways to optimize billing to maximize revenue while complying with insurance payor requirements.\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate will have a deep understanding of medical billing and coding practices for substance use disorder clinics, particularly in the state of Tennessee. They will possess the expertise necessary to analyze billing processes and identify areas of improvement, as well as the ability to communicate their findings and recommendations to clinic staff in a clear and concise manner.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nReview our current internal billing strategies and procedures, and identify areas for improvement to increase efficiency and maximize revenue.\r\n\r\nAnalyze patient records and ensure that billing codes accurately reflect the services provided, as well as any relevant insurance requirements.\r\n\r\nCommunicate findings and recommendations to clinic staff, including clinicians, administrative personnel, and insurance specialists.\r\n\r\nWork collaboratively with clinic staff to implement any recommended changes to billing practices, and ensure that these changes are sustainable and effective over the long term.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645505384557494273','-',7,'United States','-',125.000,'perhour',120.000,'2023-04-10',1,'2023-04-10',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-10 21:01:03',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(17917,'Senior Accounts Receivable Specialist',22,'Role Summary: Reporting directly to the AR Supervisor, the AR Specialist will be responsible for handling collections of a subset of key customers. Collections efforts will include but are not limited to hitting defined collection goals and KPIs, monthly reporting of customer portfolio, and cash application.\r\n\r\nJob Responsibilities:\r\n● Process high volume of collections calls on a daily basis to ensure customers are paying in a timely fashion, resolve and report on discrepancies as needed;\r\n● Collaborate with customers directly to reconcile and resolve outstanding balances;\r\n● Review invoice and payment status via customer portal\r\n● Track all disputed invoices for visibility and reporting purposes;\r\n● Utilize resources at disposal to research and resolve customer disputes.\r\n● Maintain communication in AR inbox and answer phone calls associated with customer questions;\r\n● Ensure customers are paying in a timely fashion, resolve and report on discrepancies as needed.\r\no Maintain or exceed company DSO of 25 days\r\n● Propose accounts that should be turned off or sent to collections based on payment history, claims status or disputed invoices;\r\n● Prepare weekly AR Agings for sales to review;\r\n● Customer payment conversion from check to ACH\r\n● Maintain files and documentation thoroughly and accurately, in accordance with company policy and accepted accounting practices;\r\n● Mentor and train new associates;\r\n● Address credit related issues that cause holds and payment delays;\r\n● Work with cash application team to make sure all payments are posted;\r\n● Collaborate with internal business partners (Sales, Billing, etc…) to address any and all issues that arise;\r\n● Provide weekly aging progress reports to the leadership team.\r\n● Collaborate with internal business partners (Sales, Billing, etc…) to address any and all issues that arise.\r\n● Provide support and take on additional tasks as needed.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645499918418198529','-',7,'United States','Solana Beach',10.000,'perhour',10.000,'2023-04-10',1,'2023-04-10',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-10 21:01:46',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
