(17984,'Small BIPOC-led Firm Needed for Re-branding Work',2,'**IF YOU CONTACT OUTSIDE OF UPWORK, YOUR PROPOSAL WILL BE DELETED**\r\n\r\nNow five years into the business, I have a much better understanding of what the business does and what the work is. Consequently, I want to rebrand the organization to align with this knowledge.\r\n\r\nI\'ve already undergone a branding discovery process with another consultant and can share that comprehensive doc that includes ideal clients, brand story, etc, after being hired. I\'m also totally open if the consultant wants to spend a little time revisiting this document before diving deeper into the work.\r\n\r\nWhat I\'m Looking For\r\n- A comprehensive portfolio of previous work.\r\n- Discussion on process and past experience\r\n\r\nExpectations:\r\n- In-depth consultation on elements like color, typography, graphics, and other stylistics\r\n- In-depth consultation on the name and renaming\r\n- Change the logo\r\n- Would also want to walk away able to change things like document headers and email signatures.\r\n- Payment would be milestones and in phases. Would want to do a (paid) introductory call. And, if that works well a phase one of reviewing the discovery and consultation to see if there is a fit. We could collectively work out the other phases.\r\n- Will also need to redo my website. We can discuss what scope that fits into.\r\n\r\nPreferences:\r\n- Small practice (1-20 people)\r\n- Owned or led by a BIPOC\r\n- Experience leading ideation on re-naming a business.\r\n- Graphic design expertise, with experience working with watercolors\r\n- Experience with color theory\r\n\r\n\r\nChallenges in the past:\r\n- I’m a solo practice, so I need someone conformable within circling back, checking in, and following up with me. Sometimes things get caught up in my email, or I get caught up in projects.\r\n- Also must be comfortable advocating for themselves. Let me know what may be unclear or require more instruction proactively.\r\n- Looking for someone to bring their expertise in.\r\n\r\n\r\nQuestions To Answer:\r\n- What is your larger process on branding projects?\r\n- What is your process when working with an organization to change its name?\r\n- What will specifically happen for the pricing proposed\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout Us:\r\n\r\nEMPLLC is an impact-focused company combining design, strategy, and law to translate ideas into life-changing projects. Specializing in impact, we work with a range of organizations and individuals on an affordable fixed-fee model to develop clarity, gain confidence, and connect the dots to meaningful products, services, programs, projects, and initiatives.\r\n\r\nIf you want to see current \"branding\" website is www.emcclartypllc.com','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01dd3f7c6baf5acdd8','-',7,'United States','Houston',4000.000,'fixed',4000.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 10:33:49',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
