(18076,'Need an expert in medical claim billing, coding and/or auditing',28,'I need someone with expertise in medical billing & coding, specifically regulations regarding proper billing of Regence Blueshield of WA for billing rotary airlift flights. I’m disputing an airlift bill where the company was paid a significant sum by my insurance company (over $40K) but are still billing me for a balance. As I was reviewing their bill, I noticed their air miles listed did not match the distance between the two points flown. A quick google search confirmed this. I’m trying to determine if they are supposed to bill the actual miles flown (my understanding) or the distance between two points (even better for me), or do they follow some other rules. I have copies of the bill and it shows line billing for fixed costs and then second line billing for 55 miles (whereas I think it was actually closer to 40 miles).\r\nThere was also some shenanigans with the billing, wherein the initial bill I received showed less owed, but then the insurance company paid more than they expected so they applied a large “negative” credit to the account, raising the total amount I had to pay due to increased copay.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I’m looking for a billing expert to review these bills, maybe assist me with getting copies of documents from Regence or the Airlift company, and provide a writen analysis of whether it’s all legitimate. If it is, I’m okay with that. But it sure seems fishy to me how they did the billing.\r\n\r\nI can switch to hourly billing if this project looks more involved (once you look over the documents), so no worries there.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645768843504664577','-',7,'United States','anchorage',200.000,'fixed',180.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 16:36:40',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
