(18099,'Product UI/UX Designer',6,'The Navigo Platform and Navigo Assistant mobile app for Android and iOS provide an on-demand suite of risk management, analysis and intelligence tools to help manage risk relevant to our users and the environment around them. Our systems continuously ingest massive amounts of intel from hundreds of sources, which we process and introspect to provide a near real-time risk profile anywhere in the world.\r\n\r\nAlthough we\'re based in Texas, United States, we work across many timezones as a multi-cultural team from many nationalities. As engineers we have a passion for producing a high-calibre product, in terms of its technical merit, design considerations and code quality, where testing is part of the development process, and documentation is a requirement.\r\n\r\nWe\'re searching for UI/UX talent to join our growing team, to help us continue our mission to build services that help people stay safe across the globe. You would join us to help with product design, and if successful, would be offered a permenant role in our team.\r\n\r\nRequirements\r\n\r\n- High proficiency in the English language, allowing for UI/UX discussion\r\n- At least 3 years experience with Figma\r\n- Working experience designing Web and mobile apps\r\n- Working experience with an API-driven product\r\n\r\nDesired Skills\r\n\r\n- Fundamental understanding of user experience design and knowledge of successful patterns\r\n- Ability to illustrate design ideas using storyboards, user flows, wireframes and design prototypes\r\n- Experience designing UI components for composable views (technically we use React)\r\n- Working experience with designing data visualizations\r\n- Working experience with designing for a map interface\r\n- Knowledge of HTML and CSS\r\n\r\nTarget Profile\r\n\r\n- Enjoy working on challenging and complicated design problems\r\n- Able to work autonomously with intiative and apply creative solutions\r\n- Understands the value of documentation, with some experience writing design guidelines\r\n- Capable of taking/giving constructive feedback and engaging in discussions\r\n- Good communication skills, with the ability clearly convey ideas','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645847280420405248','-',7,'United States','Dallas',45.000,'Open this select menu',45.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 17:56:34',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
