(18139,'Intake Coordinator for Psychologist in Private Practice',22,'This is a part-time remote position assisting a Psychologist who specializes in Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Psychosis (CBTp) and responsible for the initial point of contact for all new patients. This position will require 3-5 hours per week on average, no more than 20 hours per month. The ideal candidate for this position has empathy, patience and a willingness to guide patients and their families through the treatment services that we offer. Being able to stay calm and respectful in the face of conflict is a must as many individuals and family members are overwhelmed and frustrated as they search for care for themselves and their loved ones. An understanding of HIPAA and consent regulations to ensure the integrity of the practice is imperative.\r\n\r\nInitially you will be covering the current intake coordinators maternity leave. But it is likely this will become temp to perm.\r\n\r\nBusiness Values:\r\nPeople with psychosis have been short changed for too long. Traditionally in the US their treatment has been limited to hospital outpatient or community mental health clinics that are housed in well known to be stigmatizing to the community buildings, have noisy and sometimes unsafe waiting rooms, and give an all round “illness” attitude that many people with psychosis don’t agree with. Also traditionally treatment has been provided by early career clinicians, straight out of graduate school (or even still in graduate school on internships or externships), looking to gain clinical hours before moving up and out to something else. These clinicians are often not highly skilled or trained in evidence based therapies. I believe that people with psychosis deserve better!!! Psychosis can happen to anyone, regardless of who or where they are. As such people with psychosis deserve treatment the same as you or I: high level, gold standard, evidence based treatment, regardless of ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, sexual orientation, gender or socio-economic status; as well as choice in treatment location, which includes the option to attend in stigma reducing settings such as a beautifully furnished office in an unmarked building with a silent and safe waiting room.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645846455707680769','-',7,'United States','New York',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 20:15:54',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
