(18141,'Virtual Front Desk Support for Physical Therapy Clinic',22,'Looking for an energetic female virtual front desk success coordinator for Pin Point Physical Therapy, a women\'s health clinic in Charlotte, NC.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n- Calling new website and FB ad leads on a daily basis (M-F)\r\n- Responding to texts and emails from leads or clients needing to reschedule\r\n- Scheduling leads and patients via the phone\r\n- Posting content on our social media channels like IG and FB (experience with Canva would be great but not required)\r\n- Managing leads inside of our CRM (we use HighLevel) - knowledge of HighLevel not required but any experience is a bonus\r\n\r\nYou:\r\n- Detail oriented\r\n- Comfortable speaking with people on the phone\r\n- Polite, friendly, and considerate of others\r\n- Self starter (you like to innovate rather than just be told what to do)\r\n\r\nUs:\r\n- 1 person Physical Therapy practice that specializes in working with women dealing with pelvic floor issues\r\n- Based in Charlotte, NC (position is remote so not necessary to be in person)\r\n\r\nCan\'t wait to hear from you!','-','-',7,'United States','-',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 20:17:01',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(18142,'Need a medical biller for eligibility verification of medical records',21,'We are currently seeking a Medical Biller - Eligibility Verification Specialist to join our team. As an Eligibility Verification Specialist, you will be responsible for verifying patients\' insurance eligibility, obtaining necessary pre-authorizations, and ensuring that all billing information is accurate and up-to-date.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n\r\n- Verify patients\' insurance eligibility and obtain necessary pre-authorizations for medical procedures\r\n- Work with insurance companies to ensure proper payment of medical claims\r\n- Keep accurate records of patient billing information and insurance details\r\n- Follow up on denied claims and resubmit as necessary\r\n- Communicate effectively with patients, medical staff, and insurance companies to ensure timely and accurate billing\r\n- Maintain knowledge of current billing regulations and insurance policies\r\n- Collaborate with other medical billing staff to ensure efficient and effective billing practices\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Proven experience as a Medical Biller with emphasis on eligibility verification\r\n- Excellent knowledge of medical billing practices and insurance policies\r\n- Strong communication and organizational skills\r\n- Ability to work independently and as part of a team\r\n- Attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate records\r\n- Familiarity with medical coding and terminology\r\n- Proficiency in using medical billing software and Microsoft Office Suite\r\n\r\nEducation and Experience:\r\n\r\n- High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in healthcare management or related field preferred\r\n- At least 2 years of experience in medical billing, with a focus on eligibility verification and pre-authorizations\r\n- Certification in medical billing and coding preferred\r\n\r\nIf you have a proven track record of success in medical billing, possess strong communication and organizational skills, and have a passion for ensuring accurate billing practices, we encourage you to apply for this position.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645820260213411841','-',7,'United States','-',15.000,'perhour',15.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 20:17:51',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(18143,'Accounting & Tax Advisor with Delaware Experience',38,'I am seeking assistance with the following itesm\r\n\r\n1) Review of financial accounts: Our accounts have been prepared according to GAAP, but by a Dutch bookkeeper. They are relatively straightforward; we are a startup with no income. However I would like a practitioner, familiar with US tax treatment, to specifically review treatment of (a) an IP and asset purchase and subsequent amortisation, and (b) subsidiary accounts for a wholly owned Dutch company, also with no income.\r\n\r\n2) Assist with calculations required for franchise tax filings: We realise we will likely miss the 1 March deadline. We have a large authorised share base, and so we need to use the Assumed Par Value method for this filing, and would require assistance with the calculations required for this.\r\n\r\n3) View on whether any other extraordinary filings are required, i.e. do we need to file form 5472?','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645880929120075777','-',7,'United States','Wilmington',100.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 20:17:58',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
