(18145,'Experienced Medical Virtual Assistant',22,'• Answer phones in a professional manner\r\n• Obtain patient information and create their accounts in the EHR\r\n• Schedule patients in the EHR\r\n• Collect and apply virtual payments from clients\r\n• Return voice mail messages within 24 hours on business days\r\n• Check and respond to all emails within 24 hours on business days\r\n• Register patients for patient portal and online dispensary\r\n• Occasionally assist in training clients on the patient portal\r\n• Create/Update office forms as needed\r\n• Manage the schedules for all providers\r\n• Scheduling educational events sponsored by the company as needed\r\n• Order office supplies (as needed) for all staff members\r\n• Ability to be flexible and conduct other duties as needed for the office\r\n\r\nThe person applying for this position should possess the following qualifications:\r\n1. Associates degree or higher preferred with a concentration in Healthcare Administration, Healthcare Information Management or a similar field (a minimum of a High School Diploma or GED required)\r\n2. A minimum of two years of work experience with some transferrable skills\r\n3. Candidate must have strong computer skills in MS Office Suite and Adobe\r\n4. Knowledge of HIPAA and how to handle Protected Health Information (PHI) accordingly\r\n5. Must be detailed oriented and able to communicate effectively with patients, providers, and insurance companies\r\n6. Maintain a professional demeanor and cooperative attitude at all time\r\n\r\nWork Environment:\r\nThis job will be conducted from a private home office at the contractor\'s place of residence. This role routinely uses standard office equipment such as computers, phones, and printers.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645819034140852225','-',7,'United States','-',18.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-11',1,'2023-04-11',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-11 20:18:56',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
