(18396,'Yogurt Packaging - Modern, Organic, Minimalist Brand',2,'Thic Yogurt is a yogurt company that specializes in thick, high quality, homemade style yogurt, targeted towards a younger, health and wellness-minded crowd.\r\n\r\nI’m looking for a unique packaging design (individual serving) that will help the brand stand out in a bold yet subtle way.\r\n\r\nI want the packaging to be a minimalistic design. I came up with a very basic label design in Canva (attached) but I’m looking for a designer to help refine and improve it, and also render some 3D designs.\r\n\r\nThe branding and packaging should convey a few key values.\r\n\r\nOrganic and locally made - Thic Yogurt is a locally made product with no preservatives.\r\n\r\nHealth and wellness - Yogurt is naturally high in protein, making it ideal for people looking to get more protein in their diet. Our goal is to be higher in protein than most yogurts, so the protein content (in grams) will be prominently displayed on the front. Also, since yogurt is a fermented food with live active cultures, it’s beneficial to gut health (which is crucial to overall health as recent studies show). The ‘live active culture’ count may or may not be displayed on the label, I’m not sure yet, but please include it on the label design for now.\r\n\r\nMinimalism - As the name suggests, Thic Yogurt’s main differentiator is that it’s thicker than most other yogurts. I don’t want to try and convey too much other information in the design. Subtle details are better.\r\n\r\nAnother thing to convey is the tanginess of the product. Most consumers are used to less tangy yogurt. We need to convey that this yogurt is more tangy because it’s a more natural product with a higher live active culture count. A clever illustration combined with a little text should help explain this. Or it can be conveyed through the physical design of the packaging itself somehow. I don’t want to explain purely through text.\r\n\r\nAs I’ll need to add in some details later on, I’ll need the source files and some instructions on what tools to use to edit the design.\r\n\r\nThe design should also have a modern look and feel to it, to match the style of the logo and branding. I think a matte dark gray color (as shown in the image below) will help achieve this.\r\n\r\nIn terms of the physical design, something similar to this link should do, but open to other ideas: https://www.pacdora.com/mockup-detail/flexible-packaging-snack-jars-mockup-602700/.\r\n\r\nAlso, I will need the specifications that would be required to hand over to a printer/manufacturer. I don\'t know anything about this space so any input or guidance is appreciated.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646253737838133249?success','-',7,'United States','Los Angeles',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-04-12',1,'2023-04-12',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-12 20:49:42',NULL,19,3,NULL,123),
(18397,'Virtual Front Desk Assistant',22,'Looking for an energetic female virtual front desk success coordinator for Pin Point Physical Therapy, a women\'s health clinic in Charlotte, NC.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n- Calling new website and FB ad leads on a daily basis (M-F)\r\n- Responding to texts and emails from leads or clients needing to reschedule\r\n- Scheduling leads and patients via the phone\r\n- Posting content on our social media channels like IG and FB (experience with Canva would be great but not required)\r\n- Managing leads inside of our CRM (we use HighLevel) - knowledge of HighLevel not required but any experience is a bonus\r\n\r\nYou:\r\n- Detail oriented\r\n- Comfortable speaking with people on the phone\r\n- Polite, friendly, and considerate of others\r\n- Self starter (you like to innovate rather than just be told what to do)\r\n\r\nUs:\r\n- 1 person Physical Therapy practice that specializes in working with women dealing with pelvic floor issues\r\n- Based in Charlotte, NC (position is remote so not necessary to be in person)\r\n\r\nCan\'t wait to hear from you!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1645868695720742912','-',7,'United States','-',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-04-12',1,'2023-04-12',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-12 20:50:06',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
(18398,'Conversation with an Expert in Medical Claim Underpayment Appeals',21,'We are looking for US-based medical admins with experience in processing underpaid medical claims. Underpayment is defined as payer-only reimbursement and does not cover patient responsibility. You should have appealed at least several hundred claims and need to be currently professionally employed to work on submitting or processing medical claim appeals.\r\n\r\nWe will be conducting a 45-minute interview to understand what your work looks like on a daily basis. The aim of the call is to understand the process and tactics that result in a successful appeal. We will ask you for specific examples on both successful and unsuccessful appeals. You will be asked to discuss the strengths and weaknesses of medical billing software you have experience with. Additionally, we may ask other information about billing, payers, and software systems.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to meeting you.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646015060289458176','-',7,'United States','-',75.000,'perhour',75.000,'2023-04-12',1,'2023-04-12',1,'Regular Bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-12 20:51:41',NULL,12,3,NULL,150),
