(18402,'Durable Medical Equipment Specialist/DME Biller',21,'Job Title: Remote Durable Medical Equipment (DME) Authorizations Specialist (Ardent Medical Supply)\r\n\r\nArdent Medical Supply is currently hiring for the position of a Durable Medical Equipment (DME) Authorizations Specialist to work remotely. We are a leading provider of medical supplies, and we are seeking a qualified candidate with experience in prior authorization for motorized wheelchairs, manual wheelchairs, orthopedic braces, nebulizers, and breast pumps. Knowledge of medical billing procedures, HCPCS coding, and experience with New York City Managed Care Plans such as Health First, United Health Care, Fidelis Care, New York State Medicaid (DVS), Empire Health Plus, and Medicare is preferred. Experience with Integra Que and Cortex EDI is a huge plus.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Handle all authorizations in a timely manner, ensuring compliance with insurance requirements.\r\n• Perform routine clinical tasks to support patients\' needs, including verifying insurance coverage and obtaining necessary documentation.\r\n• Communicate with insurance companies for proper billing procedures, resolving any billing issues or denials.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n• Previous experience in healthcare DME is a must.\r\n• Familiarity with medical billing procedures, including HCPCS coding.\r\n• Strong organizational skills to manage and prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment.\r\n• Ability to thrive in a remote work setting with excellent communication skills.\r\n\r\nIf you have the required qualifications and experience in DME authorizations and medical billing, with a strong understanding of prior authorization for DME, we would love to hear from you. This is a remote position with flexible working hours. Please include your experience with Integra Que and Cortex EDI in your application.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646136401345560577','-',7,'United States','-',10.000,'perhour',10.000,'2023-04-12