(18523,'Quickbooks bookkeeper',39,'Part-time, Minimum 20 hours a week\r\n\r\nRemote work from home position\r\n\r\nFlexible hours between 9am to 5pm Pacific standard time\r\n\r\nResponsibilities\r\n\r\nEstablishing different accounts\r\nMaintaining records of financial transactions by posting and verifying\r\nDefining bookkeeping policies and procedures\r\nDeveloping systems to account for financial transactions by establishing a chart of accounts\r\nMaintaining subsidiary accounts by posting, verifying and allocating transactions\r\nReconciling entries to balance subsidiary accounts\r\nMaintaining a balanced general ledger\r\nPreparing a trial balance for the accountants\r\nPreparing financial reports by collecting, analyzing and summarizing accounting for information\r\nEnsuring compliance with federal, state and local legal requirements\r\nMonitoring for variances from the projected budget\r\nAdvising management on compliance needs\r\nAssisting in financial activities such as running payroll and generating invoices\r\nSkills and Qualifications\r\n\r\nBachelor’s degree in business, accounting, or related field\r\nGraduate in Accounting or Finance with bachelor’s degree or higher.\r\nMinimum 8 years’ experience in accounting and/or similar roles.\r\nCompetency with QuickBooks, virtual AP workflow solutions\r\nStrong Excel skills\r\nJob Type: Permanent','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646557623243055105','-',7,'United States','Montclair',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-13',1,'2023-04-13',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-13 16:58:05',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
(18524,'QuickBooks Online Accountant Bookkeeper',39,'Job Description:\r\n\r\nWe are seeking a skilled QuickBooks Online Accountant Bookkeeper to join our team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for uploading .csv files to QuickBooks and categorizing them correctly. Additionally, the candidate will be responsible for moving sales data from Etsy and Shopify to QuickBooks Online, performing bank reconciliations that may be overdue, and producing P&L reports.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nUpload and categorize .csv files into QuickBooks Online\r\nTransfer sales data from Etsy and Shopify to QuickBooks Online\r\nPerform bank reconciliations to ensure accuracy and completeness of financial records\r\nGenerate monthly P&L reports for management review\r\nAdvise on how to keep QuickBooks bookkeeping up to date\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nBachelor\'s degree in accounting or a related field\r\nAt least 2 years of relevant experience with QuickBooks Online and accounting/bookkeeping practices\r\nStrong knowledge of GAAP and accounting principles\r\nExperience with bank reconciliations, P&L reporting, and categorizing transactions\r\nExcellent organizational and time management skills\r\nAbility to work independently and within a team environment\r\nStrong written and verbal communication skills\r\nIf you meet the qualifications above and have a passion for bookkeeping and accounting practices, we encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity to work with our team.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646556461625163777','-',7,'United States','Palm Coast',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-13',1,'2023-04-13',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-13 16:59:20',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
(18525,'Bookkeeping, Finance Manager',39,'The Bookkeeping Finance Manager will be responsible for managing the day-to-day financial operations of the organization. The Finance Manager will report to the CEO and work closely with other members of the team.\r\n\r\nThe primary responsibilities include the following:\r\n\r\n1. Managing and maintaining accurate financial records\r\n2. Booking transactions in QuickBooks\r\n3. Managing accounts: ARs & APs\r\n4. Managing accounting email inbox\r\n5. Maintain and run payroll through Gusto\r\n6. Prepare financial reporting\r\n7. Manage cash flow, including cash receipts and disbursements, bank reconciliations, and cash forecasting\r\n8. Assist with all finance-related reporting for accountant and auditors\r\n\r\nTime:\r\nPart-time\r\nMonday - Friday 11am-1pm ET (email management, bookkeeping, ad-hoc projects)\r\nAnd ad-hoc meetings with Controller and team as needed\r\n\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Bachelor\'s degree in finance, accounting, or a related field\r\n\r\n- Minimum of 5 years of experience in bookkeeping and finance\r\n\r\n- Strong understanding of GAAP accounting principles\r\n\r\n- Experience with financial reporting and budgeting\r\n\r\n- Ability to work independently and as part of a team\r\n\r\n- Proficiency with accounting software Google Suite\r\n\r\nDon’t meet every single requirement?\r\n\r\nStudies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet every single qualification. At Food Connect we are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive and authentic workplace, so if you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646555133653303297','-',7,'United States','Philadelphia',55.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-13',1,'2023-04-13',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-13 17:00:51',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
(18526,'QuickBooks Online Bookkeeper and Trainer (Remote)',39,'We are seeking a certified QuickBooks Online bookkeeper and trainer to work remotely and provide training to the business owner on how to fix accounting problems such as the wrong category in the chart of accounts.\r\n\r\nThis is a part-time contract position, and the bookkeeper/trainer will work a total of 8 hours per week for 5 weeks.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nProvide remote training to the business owner on how to fix accounting issues in QuickBooks Online, such as the wrong category in the chart of accounts, duplicate transactions, and incorrect posting of transactions.\r\n\r\nSet up Match correctly and guide to help the business owner navigate QuickBooks Online and troubleshoot accounting problems.\r\n\r\nReview the business owner\'s QuickBooks Online account regularly to identify any issues or errors and provide guidance on how to resolve them.\r\n\r\nEnsure that the business owner\'s accounting records are accurate and up-to-date, and provide recommendations for improving their accounting processes.\r\n\r\nCollaborate with the business owner to create a customized training plan that meets their specific needs and goals.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nCertified QuickBooks Online ProAdvisor with a strong understanding of accounting principles and practices.\r\n\r\nDemonstrated experience in providing remote bookkeeping and training services to small businesses.\r\n\r\nAbility to communicate effectively and clearly with the business owner to provide guidance and support.\r\n\r\nStrong attention to detail and ability to identify and resolve accounting errors.\r\n\r\nProficient in using QuickBooks Online and other accounting software and tools.\r\n\r\nAbility to work independently and manage time effectively to meet project deadlines.\r\n\r\nThis is a great opportunity for a certified QuickBooks Online bookkeeper who enjoys working remotely and has a passion for helping small business owners improve their accounting processes.\r\n\r\nIf you meet the requirements and are interested in this position, please answer questions before applying','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646554065294188545','-',7,'United States','Georgetown',746.000,'fixed',746.000,'2023-04-13',1,'2023-04-13',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-13 17:01:57',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
