(18585,'Medical Event Planner for Startup Healthcare Organization',21,'Hello!\r\n\r\nWe\'re an industry-leading non-profit organization based in South Florida called The Foundation for Sickle Cell Disease Research. We host an Annual Symposium as well as Satellite Symposia that attract hundreds of unique individuals, who are leading researchers, physicians, clinicians, stakeholders, advocates, and social workers with the common goal of finding better treatment, and ultimately, a cure for sickle cell disease.\r\n\r\nOur attendees also originate from every corner of the world, with our highest numbers originating from the United States and U.S. Territories, the United Kingdom, Canada, Ghana, Sierra Leone, France, Italy, Switzerland, Brazil, Uruguay, Jamaica, Haiti, and India.\r\n\r\nWe have 3 satellite symposia a year, bringing this to 4 events total. The Big Annual Symposium is a hybrid event, the satellite symposia are only via Zoom. We also would like for you to travel to us in FL when we have our in-person meeting and be onsite for the week.\r\n\r\nWe are seeking a Medical Event Planner to perform as a professional administrative assistant who coordinates our Symposia, medical staff activities, performs secretarial and delegated executive job duties and acts as a liaison between the Planning Committee, Medical Staff, nursing staff and Administration within parameters established by the President/Chief Executive Officer and Chief Operating Officer. The Medical Event Planner helps to develop, organize, and execute our symposia, which are all CME Accredited, originating from the respective Symposium\'s Planning Committee, ensuring that strategic goals and objectives are met and expectations surpassed.\r\n\r\nHere is a link to our upcoming Symposium in June that we\'d appreciate help with: https://fscdr0623.eventscribe.net/\r\n\r\nWe request that you are available to come onsite and assist us in Fort Lauderdale, at the hotel, from June 15-18, 2023.\r\n\r\nDuties\r\n\r\nEstablishes and maintains positive professional communications with the Symposium Planning Committee, Medical Staff, Administration, nursing staff, all medical departments and related departments, as necessary;\r\n\r\nSet up Event Management Software for upcoming Symposium - we have one a quarter and need the same settings / documentation imported for each event.\r\n\r\nDrafting and sending speaker Letters of Invitation, sending follow up emails.\r\n\r\nThe Working Schedule on Google Sheets: importing a template (at start of event), adding in sessions and speakers as determined by planning committee, keeping speaker listing up to date and accurate with confirmations or rejections\r\n\r\nSpeaker management and logistics, examples: making sure Session Chairs know what their speakers are doing how session is going, confirming any special travel arrangements, Making sure speakers are completing their tasks\r\n\r\nAnswering inquiries as they come in, such as trying to login into one of the Cadmium products or confirming deadlines, for example.\r\n\r\nRun the planning committee meeting as needed, when the COO is unavailable. This includes following up on action items stated during the planning committees, such as asking speaker questions or sending invites.\r\n\r\nHandles all CE/CME planning and documentation requirements\r\n\r\nAssists in the registration process and follow up with attendees to ensure CE/CME credits are awarded as required.\r\n\r\nManages registration and RSVPs and all communications with registrants and attendees.\r\n\r\nWorks with the FSCDR Finance Director on back end regarding registration fees, credit cards, audit reports and reconciliations\r\nHelps to secure staff for the event as necessary\r\n\r\nEnsures adequate feedback post event through surveys, briefings, etc.\r\n\r\nExhibits a high degree of responsibility for confidential matters;\r\n\r\nPrepares for medical staff meetings, including scheduling, meeting reminders, agenda packets, and recording and processing of meeting minutes;\r\n\r\nAssures overall continuity of medical staff activities;\r\n\r\nSchedules medical staff meetings and Symposium Planning Committee meetings and maintains a master calendar for meeting types and the proper notification to medical / relevant departments of such meeting needs and activities;\r\n\r\n\r\nProvides other administrative support services and duties as may be requested;\r\n\r\nQualifications\r\n\r\n1. Two to four years of on the job experience in a healthcare setting utilizing medical terminology preferred. Knowledge of computer systems and software programs beneficial. Typing, spelling, grammar, and punctuation proficiency required. An active current knowledge of the healthcare environment helpful.\r\n\r\n2. Skilled professional communicator, including electronic and telephone communication.\r\n\r\n4. Ability to multi-task, prioritizes projects, and manages time efficiently and effectively.\r\n\r\n5. Knowledge of rules of spelling and grammar.\r\n\r\n6. Ability to maintain and organize files and records.\r\n\r\n7. Familiarity with medical terminology.\r\n\r\nWe are a woman-owned and black-owned organization and we are expanding! We have big plans in store!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1646611962180227073','-',7,'United States','Hollywood',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-04-13',1,'2023-04-13',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-13 20:38:51',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
