(18874,'Law Firm Website Redesign',3,'General: The client liked the https://attorneyharrell.com for reference. Also https://elrodpope.com/, They like the layout of this one. Want to keep their current color scheme that they have on their originally website.\r\n\r\nYou will be provided the client website upon acceptance of the job.\r\n\r\nThey want the design that isn’t playful something that is more serious. So when people come to their site they can see that these lawyers know what they are doing. They handle a lot of cases that end up being in the news. So a site that looks serious looking but also warm and inviting because of the type of cases they are taking on.\r\n\r\nThe design should be well thought-out, with all styling being pretty consistent for the different sections. Remember to keep in mind that they want a more serious looking page. The handle a lot of criminal cases and want people to know they will take things seriously but also someone they can trust. “Trust is everything” is there slogan. They look at things like, if you are our client you are our family. They want to do the right thing and help people who need it.\r\n\r\nPlease review the project brief, as well as our attached guidelines and examples thoroughly, as we have done hundreds of hours of market research to maximize conversion on our websites.\r\n\r\nKeep in mind the guidelines are just guidelines to make sure certain areas are included and features that we need. WE NEED YOUR CREATIVITY ADDED TO THIS.\r\n\r\nThis Client has an existing site: You will be provided the client website upon acceptance of the job.\r\nFonts: High-end font.\r\nTagline: \"Trust is Everything”\r\n\r\nOn Their homepage they do like the idea of their testimonials rotating through. Located in the middle bottom of the page. Then notable cases towards the top\r\n Ideal\r\n\r\nAudience: The firm hands Criminal, DUI, Personal Injury and Civil Rights cases. Their Ideal client is someone who is seeking a lawyer who will fight for them. Someone who needs to go the extra mile to show their case. The client is looking for some they can TRUST and are just not it for the money.\r\n\r\nPages Needed: We need Desktop AND Mobile designs for the following page types\r\n\r\nThe sections for each page type are listed in order below, please design all sections in accordance with our guidelines and using your best design judgement\r\n\r\nHomepage: Needs to have the following\r\n\r\nHero Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines.\r\nLikes the city background in the hero section of Trey Harrell website that was provided (attorneyharrell.com)\r\nNotable Case Results section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nPractice Area Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nClient/Testimonial Reviews Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines.\r\nRotating through. Located in the middle bottom of the page. Don’t include the phrase “what our clients are saying”.\r\nCase Process Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nMultiple call to action sections - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nMeet the Attorneys Section\r\nA contact us section\r\n\r\nInterior Page:\r\n\r\nHeading Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nClient Reviews Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nCase Results section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nPage Content Section - designed in accordance with our guidelines\r\nRelated Videos Section - This section should contain videos that correlate with that page on the bottom:\r\nFor example\r\nProminent Call-To-Action section (in accordance with our guidelines,)\r\nFooter\r\n\r\nAbout Us: Follow our guidelines which are attached for the below\r\n\r\nHero/Heading Section\r\n6 Attorneys (will provide once job is selected)\r\n4 Other staff (will provide once job is selected)\r\nReviews\r\nResults\r\nClient Testimonials section (comprised of videos)\r\nFooter\r\n\r\nVideo Library: This should be formatted into an archive page where all videos are displayed, and the user can filter between the below options:\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions\r\nClient Testimonials\r\nInformation Videos\r\nOther Videos\r\n\r\nSite Map:\r\nHomepage\r\nPractice area interior page\r\nAbout us\r\nContact Us\r\nAttorney BIO interior page\r\nResults Page\r\n\r\nNotes on Common Sections:\r\n\r\nFooter should contain the footer elements outlined in our guidelines\r\n\r\nMenu Bar:\r\n\r\nThe Menu Items should be same, however the header of the site should be redesigned according or our guidelines which are attached.\r\n\r\nMenu bar should be displayed under the header.\r\n\r\nReference Site(s):\r\nhttps://attorneyharrell.com\r\nhttps://elrodpope.com\r\n\r\nAttach are our guidelines and the logo\r\nThis Client has an existing site: You will be provided the client website upon acceptance of the job.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1648020497852334081','-',7,'United States','Greenville',1800.000,'fixed',1800.000,'2023-04-17',1,'2023-04-17',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-17 17:54:24',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
