(18883,'CPA wanted for filling 2022 taxes for US small biz',38,'Our current CPA has retired so we\'re looking for a new one.\r\nWe\'re late with our tax prep for 2022, so you\'ll help us catch up.\r\nWe use QuickBooks Online and we have a bookkeeper who has been attending our books. But some transactions need to be tidy up. For example some loans have been assigned to income, they need to be reassigned to the proper category.\r\n\r\nThe company is LLP based in Nevada, USA.\r\nPrimary income is food (we have a food truck). We also have some income from a side coaching business and online courses.\r\nWe need to file some 1099s, no payroll needed.\r\n\r\nYour job:\r\n. You will help us file for an extension on our company taxes as well as for our personal taxes. We didn\'t file an extension on time.\r\n. Your primary job is to prepare and file our company taxes and our personal taxes.\r\n. You need to be certified to file company and personal taxes in Nevada, USA.\r\n. You may help us sort out transactions in QuickBooks before filing taxes but we can also find someone else for that.\r\n\r\nYour profile\r\n. You need to be perfectly fluent in English so we can communicate easily\r\n. You need to be friendly and helpful, efficient, flexible and solution oriented.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1648020623308013569','-',7,'United States','Reno',200.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-17',1,'2023-04-17',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-17 18:42:18',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
(18884,'Senior UX/UI Designer',6,'Company Overview:\r\nWander is an interactive mapping company that provides travelers with a unique and personalized experience. Our mission is to create a platform that helps people discover the world around them and connect with their surroundings in meaningful ways. We are seeking a talented Senior UX Designer to join our team and help us create outstanding digital products that our users will love.\r\nJob Overview:\r\nAs a Senior UX Designer at Wander, you will be responsible for designing and creating exceptional user experiences across our platform. You will work closely with our product and engineering teams to develop and implement UX design solutions that align with our business goals and user needs.\r\nResponsibilities:\r\nCollaborate with product and engineering teams to identify user needs and develop UX design solutions that align with business goals.\r\nCreate low fidelity wireframes and prototypes in Figma to test and iterate on design concepts.\r\nDevelop high-fidelity visual designs that effectively communicate design concepts and solutions.\r\nConduct user research and usability testing to validate design decisions and identify areas for improvement.\r\nCollaborate with other designers and stakeholders to ensure consistency and alignment across the product.\r\nRequirements:\r\nBachelor\'s degree in Design, Human-Computer Interaction, or related field.\r\nAt least 5 years of experience in UX design, preferably at a mature UX organization.\r\nExpertise in low fidelity wireframing and prototyping in Figma.\r\nStrong visual design skills with a keen eye for detail and a solid understanding of design principles.\r\nExperience conducting user research and usability testing.\r\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\r\nA portfolio that demonstrates your UX design expertise.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1648034098492649473','-',7,'United States','Provo',50.000,'perhour',48.000,'2023-04-17',1,'2023-04-17',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-17 18:42:44',NULL,18,3,NULL,116),
