(19049,'Certified Public Accountant (CPA) for Reviewed Comparative Financial Statements (Last 2 Years)',38,'We are an education organization looking for a qualified and experienced Certified Public Accountant (CPA) to review our Comparative Financial Statements. The Company’s HQ is in Delaware.\r\n\r\nThe candidate must be authorized to prepare Reviewed Financial Statements (in Audited Financial Statements if required). If you have a strong background in accounting and have the required licenses, we would be excited to work with you!\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nAnalyze our Financial Statements which are ready and sent for tax filing and prepare Reviewed Comparative Financial Statements (for the last 2 financial years).\r\nEnsure financial statements are prepared in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). For GAAP compliant Reviewed Financial Statements, the following should be prepared or reviewed:\r\n• Engagement Letter\r\n• Management Representation Letter\r\n• Review Report\r\n• Balance Sheet\r\n• Income Statement\r\n• Statement of Cash Flows\r\n• Note Disclosures\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n• Must be a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) with an active license.\r\n• Minimum of 5 years of experience in accounting, financial analysis, or a similar role.\r\n• Strong knowledge of GAAP, IFRS, and other applicable accounting standards.\r\n• Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.\r\n• High attention to detail and accuracy.\r\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills.\r\n• Ability to work independently and meet tight deadlines.\r\n\r\nTo apply, please submit the following:\r\nYour resume, highlighting your relevant experience and education.\r\nA brief cover letter explaining why you are the perfect candidate for this role.\r\nTwo professional references who can speak to your accounting and financial analysis skills.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to reviewing your application and discussing the opportunity to work together! We can provide information about the Company (total asset size, total expenses, number of invoices etc.), if you are interested in this role.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1648377803425251329','-',7,'United States','Palo Alto',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-18',1,'2023-04-18',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-18 18:26:06',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
(19050,'Part-time Controller/Accountant/Bookkeeper needed for an advertising agency',39,'We are an advertising agency that is growing very fast and is in need of a part-time Controller. We need bookkeeping services right now and need our last few months reconciled ASAP.\r\n\r\nREQUIRED: extensive experience with spreadsheets and pulling numbers. MUST have experience using QuickBooks Online and fluent in English is a must.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n- Pulling numbers\r\n- Bookkeeping\r\n- Basic accounting\r\n- Spreadsheet management\r\n- Calculations and keeping track of revenue\r\n- Going into advertising platforms and pulling client spend (Facebook Ads, Google Ads, Snapchat Ads, etc.)\r\n\r\nCash bonuses will be paid for speedy, long-term, high-quality results.\r\nThe position will provide consistent work if this project is completed successfully.\r\n\r\nIf you are the right person to join our team then you will have taken the time to read this post carefully. This is very important to me so in your reply please tell me your favorite food in the subject of your reply. Also, mention which accounting platform you have experience with and if you have ever managed invoicing which platforms you managed for that.\r\n\r\nI look forward to working with you and building a solid ongoing relationship! :-)\r\n\r\nTalk soon,\r\n- Samir','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1648376399854047233','-',7,'United States','Boston',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-18',1,'2023-04-18',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-18 18:27:42',NULL,11,3,NULL,155),
