(19301,'Property Management Bookkeeping',39,'We are a vertically integrated real estate development and investment firm. Our fundamental purpose is to serve our community by providing homes and commercial spaces to the individuals living and working within these communities and we achieve this through the acquisition and thoughtful restoration of underutilized real estate.\r\n\r\nThe Bookkeeper is a critical member of our company because their work allows us to track the essential information to make critical decisions regarding finance, operations and investments.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities include: day-to-day responsibility for managing, implementing and controlling all financial-related activities in the property and construction management areas of our Firm.\r\n\r\nThis position will be responsible for all levels of g/l accounting -- including but not limited to data entry & oversight, A/P. A/R, Employee Onboarding (Tax Docs, Benefits, etc.), Collection of Lien Waivers, Construction Reimbursement Requests, etc.\r\n\r\nIf you enjoy entering & analyzing data and running all aspects of the company\'s bookkeeping functions and are looking for that opportunity to dive into a growing business and help drive success, then this may be the perfect role for you.\r\n\r\nQualifications\r\n\r\nBachelor\'s degree in Accounting, Finance or related field or equivalent experience\r\n\r\nExperience in real estate industry, including commercial property management\r\n\r\nSupervisory or equivalent experience\r\n\r\nProven working knowledge and experience with property management accounting systems, preferably Rent Manager Online, as well as Quickbooks Online\r\n\r\nHigh degree of personal drive and motivation to succeed\r\n\r\nExcellent communicator (written and verbal), with high quality report writing skills\r\n\r\nCommitted to achievement of assigned goals and targets\r\n\r\nAbility to maintain progress on multiple projects and processes\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe successful candidate must\r\n\r\nbe available to work during the Company\'s business hours and time zone (CST)\r\n\r\nbe dedicated to their contract with our company and provide a structured schedule during the Owner\'s workday. We do not want your work with us to compete with other contracts you are juggling\r\n\r\nhave a professional home office with fast internet, appropriate firewalls, multiple screens, etc.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1649044962236448769?success','-',7,'United States','Saint Louis',25.000,'Open this select menu',25.000,'2023-04-20',1,'2023-04-20',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-20 13:40:20',NULL,19,3,NULL,123),
