(19381,'Cryotherapy blog, psychology bias',37,'Hello,\r\n\r\nI\'m flexible with the budget but I needed to set a price so feel free to negotiate! I desire a blog post in the domain of practical psychology with the topic of cryotherapy as it affects mental health.\r\n\r\nMy wife is a psychotherapist who likes to add content that is congruent with her philosophies that is worth reading/linking that may benefit her existing and future clientele.\r\n\r\nWrite a blog describing how cryotherapy affects mental health and relieves anxiety purportedly quickly and holistically. I\'m less concerned with the physiological benefits at this time: the copy should just focus on mental health. I\'d prefer a brief medical-reviewed type copy complete with a citation list (think professional peer-reviewed research in the NLM/NIH, not Huffpost) of the background of cryotherapy, both full body submersion as well as the new trend of ice-pack therapy. It would be great to mimic or ghostwrite our current friendly, next-door therapist-style copy.\r\n\r\nThe post should be able to briefly describe the array of complex psycho-physiological processes of cryotherapy, the ANS, Vagus nerve relays, as well as the documented release of neurotransmitters such as dopamine, etc.\r\n\r\nIn pondering this topic, the question arrose. What is the proposed evolutionary response to cold water mechanisms when applied to the base of the brain stem (neck), or the act of the whole body ice-bath submersion; ie dive reflex? These all purportedly trigger an ANS response, but the question is why. Are they related? Is it the cold, or is it the water, or is it cold water? I don’t know. Describe how if so.\r\n\r\nAnother question is, is the act of performing cryotherapies psychosomatic, as in, are they behaviorally based grounding mechanisms? If so, explain with citations. In other words, does cryotherapy fall under the behavioral branch of psychology where the body is being conditioned to be calm when exposed to a cold water mechanism? I don’t know. Give a plausible explanation that it is a mental game and not an evolved physical response.\r\n\r\nNote, this isn’t a research paper! I feel there is something there that should be examined for edification, to ask the question, but to not answer it necessarily. There is a lot of research on cryotherapy. Please target your references to the scope of this blog only.\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n\r\nDescribe the psychological and physiological response to cryotherapy as it relates to mental well-being only.\r\n\r\nProvide a brief history of cryotherapy.\r\n\r\nDescribe the psychological benefits of cryotherapy.\r\n\r\nDescribe the overlapping applications of cryotherapy and compare and contrast at least the following three methods: 1) targeted ice-pack therapy, 2) fully body ice/cold water submersion, 3) splashing cold water on your face or dipping hands into cold water.\r\n\r\nArgue the evolutionary adaptations of the Dive Reflex, ANS, sympathetic & parasympathetic responses, role of the Vagus nerve, heart rarte variability (HRV), etc. Explore if innate responses are partially responsible for the allure of cryotherapy.\r\n\r\n**\r\n\r\nI prefer content that is 40% medical, 30% behavioral, and 30% segway to connect with the audience.\r\n\r\nOur style is to capture the audience with brevity quickly and directly correlate an everyday application of the idea. Then provide a brief detailed history, medical process explainer, describe a best case psycho application of the idea, and conclude with a whitty and convincing recap that provides a warm authority about the idea.\r\n\r\nRegarding behavior, argue in favor of the theory with clinical evidence.\r\n\r\nRegarding evolutionary adaptations, argue in favor of the theory without solid medical evidence, outside of the Dive Reflex and other documented physiological concepts.\r\n\r\nThe copy should be terse, propose questions, and attempt to answer the questions, but you’re not required to do so.\r\n\r\nExamples of past practical psychology blogs:\r\n\r\nhttps://www.samaraorr.com/blog/adhd-sensory-strategies\r\nhttps://www.samaraorr.com/blog/2021/5/18/box-breathing\r\n\r\nI look forward to working with you!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1649401668326895617','-',7,'United States','Forth Worth',250.000,'Open this select menu',200.000,'2023-04-21',1,'2023-04-21',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-21 14:25:38',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
