(19506,'Medical Biller Needed',21,'I am looking for Virtual medical biller, perfect for someone who wants to work home and have steady long term job security and great environment . LET ME MAKE THIS VERY CLEAR. Whoever I hire today should always be the same person working on my claims tomorrow, next week ,next month and next year. It should not be your friend, neighbor, husband, relatives or coworker. Someone with expertise in medical billing., submitting, correcting, posting claims and also good communication skills in English','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650880398051823617','-',7,'United States','Dartmouth',18.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:04:42',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(19507,'Medical Billing Coder Needed to Review Diagnosis and ICD-10 Codes for Healthcare Practice',21,'Introduction:\r\nWe seek a qualified medical billing coder to review our diagnosis and ICD-10 codes for accuracy and completeness. The goal of this project is to ensure that our billing process is in compliance with all relevant regulations and to maximize our revenue potential.\r\n\r\nScope of Work:\r\nThe medical billing coder will be responsible for the following tasks:\r\n\r\nReview all diagnosis codes and ICD-10 codes used in our medical billing system.\r\nVerify the accuracy and completeness of the codes.\r\nIdentify any coding errors, omissions, or discrepancies.\r\nRecommend corrections or updates to the codes as needed.\r\nEnsure all codes comply with relevant regulations and guidelines, including HIPAA and CMS rules.\r\nProvide guidance and support to our billing team on coding-related issues.\r\nWork collaboratively with our team to ensure timely and accurate billing.\r\n\r\nDeliverables:\r\nThe medical billing coder will deliver the following:\r\nA report detailing the findings of the code review, including any errors, omissions, or discrepancies identified.\r\nA set of recommended corrections or updates to the codes, if needed.\r\nDocumentation of compliance with relevant regulations and guidelines.\r\nOngoing support and guidance on coding-related issues as needed.\r\n\r\nTimeline:\r\nThe project is expected to take approximately 2 weeks to complete, with an estimated 20 hours of work. The exact timeline will be agreed upon with the selected candidate.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\nThe ideal candidate will have the following qualifications:\r\n\r\nA minimum of 3 years of experience as a medical billing coder.\r\nKnowledge of ICD-10 codes and medical billing regulations and guidelines.\r\nStrong attention to detail and accuracy.\r\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\r\nA commitment to quality and customer service.\r\n\r\nPayment:\r\nThe selected candidate will be paid a fixed fee for the project, to be negotiated based on experience and qualifications.\r\n\r\nConfidentiality:\r\nAll information and data provided to the medical billing coder will be treated as confidential and used solely for the purposes of this project. The medical billing coder will be required to sign a confidentiality agreement prior to starting work.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650880386947985409','-',7,'United States','US',2500.000,'fixed',2200.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:06:12',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(19508,'Medical Biller and Accounts Receivable',21,'Allara is looking for a Medical Biller to join the team and play a critical role in helping to fulfill our mission of building a better women’s healthcare experience. As a Medical Biller, you will supporting daily functions of clinical and financial operations, while interacting with patients to ensure timely collections.\r\n\r\nAs a Medical Billing Specialist you will:\r\nPlay a critical role in clinical and financial operations, as a team player\r\nManages patient billing and accounts receivable and provides superior customer support for patients with billing questions\r\nHandle patient refunds, subscription cancellations and invoicing requests\r\nInvoice and bill patients for outstanding balances, and trouble shoot as needed\r\nInterface with patients, as well as the following internal teams: Clinical, Concierge, Operations, Product\r\nAssists with external Health Plan correspondence related to nonstandard claim information requests\r\nThis includes, but is not limited to, investigation and routing of patient billing in a timely manner, providing an excellent support experience by meeting all applicable metrics and goals, and triaging customer requests while adhering to protocols and HIPAA guidelines\r\nCommunicates and contributes to ongoing medical billing assigned initiatives; uses sound judgment in assessing project health, identifying, mitigating, and resolving any project issues\r\n\r\nWe’re looking for:\r\nMinimum 1+ years of experience working within a Medical Billing-related field\r\nExceptional communication, both customer-facing and with internal teams\r\nWorks collaboratively and is solutions oriented\r\nRetains impeccable attention to detail and remains process-driven while operating with a sense of urgency\r\nProven ability to execute Medical Billing skillset effectively, as a way of combating visit revenue loss, and improving compliance\r\nExperience working with GSuite products, Stripe, electronic medical records (EMR) and clearinghouses preferred\r\nEmpathy for patients and commitment to work with discretion as you would be working with sensitive data\r\n\r\nAdditional details:\r\n100% remote and can be done anywhere (though the company is based in NYC)\r\nPart time to start but opportunity to join full time or longer term','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650880351170396161','-',7,'United States','New york',12.000,'Open this select menu',18.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:07:23',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(19509,'Experienced Medical Virtual Assistant and Medical Biller',22,'We are seeking 1-2 experienced Medical Virtual Assistant (Patient Care Coordinator) to help our rapidly growing outpatient Psychiatric Mental Health Practice located in California.\r\n\r\nThis position is Full-Time, Monday thru Friday, with working hours from 9:00 AM - 5 PM Pacific Standard Time (PST).\r\n\r\nOur ideal candidate is a Medical Virtual Assistant who has at least 1 year of experience working in a psychiatric, mental health, or therapy practice.\r\n\r\nTASKS:\r\nWhile our office is primarily hybrid (online and in-person), we need an experienced Registered Nurse or Medical Assistant to help to:\r\n\r\n1) communicate with prospective and current patients by text, email, fax and phone, as needed.\r\n2) assure new and follow up patients are entered into our Practice Fusion EHR system and that payment and paperwork is received for each appointment.\r\n3) perform limited medical billing duties within the EHR and other billing platforms, for cash and insurance claims processing. Will be entering CPT codes into EHR\r\n4) confirm insurance benefits eligibility electronically or by phone and collect any copays or deductibles due prior to appointment time.\r\n5) assure that patients are scheduling follow-up visits.\r\n6) complete and submit insurance Prior Authorization Forms for medication claims.\r\n7) retrieve EOB/ERA document from multiple insurance portals to retrieve information and match data on an excel file to each client visit and be able to organize excel to easily bring up the EOB/ERA when needed in case patient has billing questions\r\n8) will need experience multitasking between answering phones, data entry, completing requests from other staff members and attending to customer service tasks\r\n9) will need extensive experience with Microsoft products but especially Outlook, Excel, Word and Powerpoint\r\n10) will need to be detail oriented\r\n11) This position will also be in charge of handling customer billing questions and concerns, so you will need to have great customer service skills\r\n\r\n#1 requirement is RELIABILITY. We are a small team and depend on each other. Attendance is very important.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n-Must be a fluent English speaker and strong writer\r\n-Experience in working with Mental Health\r\n-Must own a laptop or PC\r\n-At least 20 mbps internet speed for primary ISP\r\n-Must have backup internet provider\r\n-Noise cancellation headset\r\n-Experience with practice fusion is preferred but willing to train.\r\n-Must be a outgoing, enthusiastic and willing to learn.\r\n-Nursing/Medical Background is A HUGE PLUS\r\n\r\nIf you are interested, please submit a resume and we will share the Practice details and arrange to speak.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to considering everyone qualified and hire immediately.\r\n\r\nOur record for hiring is excellent on Upwork and our long-term engagements speak to our commitment and ability to manage a virtual workforce.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650880337562021889','-',7,'United States','Long Beach US',7.000,'Open this select menu',18.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:11:52',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(19510,'Medicaid Billing Consultant',21,'I am seeking a person that has experience with Medicaid billing experience.\r\n\r\nI\'m in the process of acquiring a medical facility in the south and looking for someone with experience as a medical clinician or medical billing specialist. I\'m analyzing what services we can offer my patients immediately upon acquiring the business.\r\n\r\nI primarily need someone to advise me on what telehealth options I have.\r\n\r\nThis role will most likely entail:\r\n- Researching medical billing processes and rates in the southeast\r\n- 20-30-minute phone calls with me to discuss those findings\r\n\r\nI\'m looking forward to meeting you, and feel free to let me know if you have any questions.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650880303772307457','-',7,'United States','Newyork',30.000,'Open this select menu',50.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:13:56',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(19511,'Website Design',4,'# Outline\r\n\r\nThis site allows users to sell their cars by entering various information and ultimately receiving a quote in return which they can accept or decline.\r\n\r\n# General Notes\r\n\r\nThe site will be mostly for mobile users (expected ~80%). Although it needs to work for all resolutions and should scale appropriately on desktop, the concentration should be for mobiles.\r\n\r\n# Pages\r\n\r\n1. **Homepage**\r\n\r\n1. This should contain brief messaging to describe what the site is about, and call to actions to “get a quote”\r\n\r\n2. This should contain a general header and footer\r\n\r\n3. Header will need to include different logged in / logged out parts (so we can have options to logout and view quotes / profile info (generic)\r\n\r\n2. **Vehicle Details Form**\r\n\r\n1. This will contain a form / wizard to collect the users information about their car.\r\n\r\n2. Each step / form will have a title, subtitle (explanation), help tooltip and a field (i.e. dropdown, text input, etc.)\r\n\r\n3. Each step of the form will look very much the same but will be contained within a parent form / container (to enable turning it into a SPA / Vue.js component)\r\n\r\n4. The for should also contain a progress indicator i.e. how far through the user is in the process\r\n\r\n5. Final step must include a confirmation of terms, etc. with checkbox\r\n\r\n3. **Quote Page**\r\n\r\n1. Once the user has completed all of the necessary information, they will be presented with a quote\r\n\r\n2. This should be an eye catching page as this is the step we want the user to be encouraged to accept the quote\r\n\r\n4. # Vehicle Details Form (In-Depth)\r\n\r\nEach page/section of the form will contain a help tooltip and what is described in the above section. Below is the exact description of what is in each step of the form. Most “choice” forms will be options to choose from and not just basic dropdowns, so the user can easily see all of them on the page and will hopefully reduce users picking the wrong option.\r\n\r\n**************Forms/Steps**************\r\n\r\n1. Tell us about your car - Dropdowns for make, model and year in same form/group\r\n2. Zipcode (where is it getting picked up from?)\r\n3. Do you own the vehicle?\r\n1. Yes, it’s fully paid\r\n2. No, I am still paying it off\r\n3. My car is on a lease\r\n4. Condition\r\n1. Multi select / checkboxes or images to select\r\n2. Options are:\r\n1. One or more flat tires\r\n2. One or more missing tires\r\n3. Car won’t start\r\n4. Battery doesn’t work\r\n5. Key fob not working\r\n6. Car won’t drive\r\n7. Exterior damage ( few scratches)\r\n8. Missing or damaged doors\r\n9. Missing or broken mirrors\r\n10. One or more broken windows\r\n11. Damaged interior\r\n5. Does the vehicle have a clean title?\r\n1. Yes\r\n2. No\r\n3. Not sure, I don’t have it\r\n6. Mileage\r\n1. Enter mileage (numeric text input with range)\r\n7. Has your car ever been in a fire or a flood?\r\n1. No\r\n2. Yes\r\n8. Photos of your vehicle\r\n1. Upload both sides, front and back of vehicle\r\n9. Loading offer… (show loading, while we call the API)\r\n10. User registration\r\n1. (i.e. enter your email to continue, and save your quote)\r\n2. Only email and password\r\n11. Finally, enter your title details\r\n1. Full Name\r\n2. VIN (optional)\r\n3. Title issue state (US states)\r\n4. Color (basic color picker - normal car options, not like hex picker)\r\n12. Where will we be picking up your car from?\r\n1. Residence or business (choose one)\r\n2. Street address\r\n3. City\r\n4. State\r\n5. Zip\r\n6. Contact name\r\n7. Contact phone\r\n8. Update me via SMS - (checkbox - optional)\r\n13. Accept offer\r\n1. I.e. user is presented again with final offer and they need to take action to “accept” (which will trigger a pickup schedule call from us)\r\n14. Final info\r\n1. Last page which shows all the necessary details of the offer, pickup location, status, etc.\r\n2. Will need to include n option to cancel near the bottom also\r\n\r\n# Components\r\n\r\nBelow is a list of components that will be reused across the site.\r\n\r\n1. General overlay - i.e. for showing general information, with an image, title, subtitle and description text (e.g. “We can’t give you a quote without info [x]”, etc.\r\n2. Tooltip / help text (i.e. on each step of the form there may be extra info required so would use a general info icon / tooltip text\r\n\r\n# Design Inspiration\r\n\r\nI have included below, some similar sites for inspiration, and also some that we like the design style / layout of.\r\n\r\nhttps://peddle.com\r\n\r\nhttps://carbrain.com\r\n\r\nSome examples of multi-step forms for ideas: [https://www.growform.co/10-best-multi-step-form-examples-and-why-they-work-new-for-2022/](https://www.growform.co/10-best-multi-step-form-examples-and-why-they-work-new-for-2022/)','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650896310837030913?success','-',7,'United States','Miami',50.000,'perhour',45.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:17:45',NULL,17,3,NULL,119),
(19512,'Medical Writer',37,'Company: DME Web\r\nLocation: Remote (US)\r\nType: Full-time / Part-time\r\n\r\nDME Web is a growing American company dedicated to improving healthcare safety, quality, and reliability. We are seeking a Medical Writer to join our team and work on a medical IT project. This project focuses on developing a medical web platform with a focus on billing.\r\n\r\nAs a Medical Writer, you will be responsible for converting complex medical data into concise and comprehensible user surveys that comply with US medical regulations. You will contribute to ensuring the accuracy and reliability of our platform by updating our knowledge base, working with medical equipment descriptions, creating new medical quizzes for users, and editing existing quizzes to ensure they meet US legal requirements.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n• Regularly updating the knowledge base to comply with US healthcare regulations\r\n• Working with medical equipment descriptions on the web-portal DmeWeb\r\n• Creating new medical quizzes for users of the web portal\r\n• Editing already completed quizzes for medical grammar, punctuation, style, and internal consistency with US law\r\n• Working with relevant medical documentation\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n• Fluent in spoken and written English, with a solid understanding of medical terminology (C1 level or higher)\r\n• Prior experience as a Medical Writer or in a similar role is required\r\n• Experience using tools such as Zoom, Google Drive, etc.\r\n• Ability to adapt medical content for different target audiences\r\n• Ability to review and check the composed texts to ensure materials are scientifically and technically accurate\r\n\r\nNice-to-haves:\r\n• Higher education in a related field\r\n• Experience in supply/distribution management in the field of pharmaceutics and medicine\r\n• Profound understanding of the US medical system\r\n\r\nWe offer:\r\n• Remote work\r\n• Full-time/part-time employment\r\n• Competitive salary, which will be discussed during the interview\r\n• Personal bonuses\r\n\r\nWe are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from people with disabilities.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1650880281895219201','-',7,'United States','US',25.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-25',1,'2023-04-25',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-25 16:23:57',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
