(19624,'Finance Manager or Chief Financial Officer',39,'Job Overview:\r\nWe are seeking an experienced and highly motivated Finance Manager/Chief Financial Officer (CFO) to join our e-commerce team. The CFO will be responsible for managing the company\'s finances, including budgeting, forecasting, and financial reporting. This executive will also oversee the development and implementation of financial strategies to maximize profitability and support the company\'s growth. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in finance, accounting, and strategic financial planning in the e-commerce industry.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nOversee all aspects of the company\'s financial management, including financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting.\r\nDevelop and implement financial strategies to maximize profitability and support the company\'s growth objectives.\r\nManage cash flow, working capital, and capital expenditure to ensure financial stability and efficient resource allocation.\r\nPrepare timely and accurate financial reports, including income statements, balance sheets, and cash flow statements, in compliance with accounting standards and regulations.\r\nCollaborate with the leadership team to develop and monitor key performance indicators (KPIs) and financial metrics, providing insights and recommendations for improvement.\r\nEnsure compliance with all relevant financial regulations, tax laws, and industry standards, including timely filing of tax returns and financial statements.\r\nDevelop and maintain financial policies and procedures to ensure the integrity and efficiency of the company\'s financial operations.\r\nManage relationships with external partners, such as banks, investors, and auditors, ensuring transparent communication and timely reporting.\r\nOversee the company\'s payroll, accounts payable, and accounts receivable processes, ensuring accuracy and efficiency.\r\nStay current on industry trends, emerging technologies, and best practices in financial management to drive innovation and maintain a competitive edge in the market.\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\nBachelor\'s degree in Finance, Accounting, or a related field; Master\'s degree and/or CPA certification preferred.\r\nA minimum of 7 years of experience in finance, with at least 3 years in a leadership role.\r\nProven experience in financial management, specifically within the e-commerce industry.\r\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to develop and implement effective financial strategies.\r\nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to present complex financial information in a clear and concise manner.\r\nProficiency in financial software and tools, such as accounting systems, budgeting and forecasting tools, and financial analysis platforms.\r\nAdept at managing budgets, forecasting, and financial analysis.\r\nFamiliarity with financial regulations, tax laws, and industry standards.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651250671078920193?success','-',7,'United States','Smyrna',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-04-26',1,'2023-04-26',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-26 15:44:38',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
