(19674,'Accountant with Quickbooks experience',39,'Job brief\r\nWe are looking for an Accountant to manage all financial transactions, from fixed payments and variable expenses to bank deposits and budgets.\r\n\r\nAccountant responsibilities include auditing financial documents and procedures, reconciling bank statements, and calculating tax payments and returns. To be successful in this role, you should have previous experience with bookkeeping and a flair for spotting numerical mistakes.\r\n\r\nUltimately, you will provide us with accurate quantitative information on the financial position, liquidity, and cash flows of our business, while ensuring we’re compliant with all tax regulations.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities\r\n- Manage all accounting transactions\r\n- Prepare budget forecasts\r\n- Publish financial statements in time\r\n- Handle monthly, quarterly and annual closings\r\n- Reconcile accounts payable and receivable\r\n- Ensure timely bank payments\r\n- Compute taxes and prepare tax returns\r\n- Manage balance sheets and profit/loss statements\r\n- Report on the company’s financial health and liquidity\r\n- Audit financial transactions and documents\r\n- Reinforce financial data confidentiality and conduct database backups when necessary\r\n- Comply with financial policies and regulations\r\n\r\nRequirements and skills\r\n- Work experience as an Accountant\r\n- Excellent knowledge of accounting regulations and procedures, including the Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP)\r\n- Hands-on experience with accounting software like FreshBooks and QuickBooks\r\n- Advanced MS Excel skills\r\n\r\nThis position will start off as part time and eventually transition to full time. Candidate must be willing to work from 9am - 5pm EST.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651333795389476865?success','-',7,'United States','Lowell',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-26',1,'2023-04-26',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-26 21:14:55',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
(19675,'Insurance billing',28,'Seeking an insurance biller for a Durable Medical Equipment (DME) company who will be responsible for ensuring that the company receives timely and accurate payments for the medical equipment it provides to patients. The following is a typical job description for an insurance biller for a DME company:\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nReview patient medical records and prescriptions to ensure that equipment provided is accurately coded for billing purposes\r\nSubmit insurance claims to insurance providers, government agencies, and other third-party payers for reimbursement of DME equipment\r\nFollow up on outstanding claims and resolve any billing discrepancies or denials related to DME equipment\r\nMust have experience billing Medi-cal and managed plans in California\r\nCommunicate with patients, healthcare providers, and insurance companies to answer questions and resolve issues related to billing and insurance coverage for DME equipment\r\nMaintain up-to-date knowledge of medical billing codes, insurance regulations, and billing software systems related to DME equipment\r\nManage patient accounts and ensure that all payments for DME equipment are accurately recorded and applied to the correct account\r\nAssist with the preparation of financial reports and audits related to billing and reimbursement activities for DME equipment','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651214472413556737','-',7,'United States','FORT LAUDERDALE',25.000,'Open this select menu',18.000,'2023-04-26',1,'2023-04-26',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-26 21:31:51',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
