(19677,'Book cover design and manuscript formating',2,'**Please read all details before making offer**\r\n\r\nI am extremely excited about my new book! I am passionate about helping kids and teens find happiness and success! Because it is written for teens, the design elements, both on the cover, and inside, will be truly critical in order to hold their attention and get the reader interested. I need somebody who will be able to do following:\r\n\r\n1. Design the cover of the book, this will include front, cover, back, cover, and spine.\r\n2. Copyright page, title page, dedication page, any other ancillary pages, like author’s info, author’s comments, etc.\r\n3. Manuscript formatting-I will provide the manuscript, but there are different segments and highlights placed in each chapter. These need to be designed with color and organizational elements to make it interesting.\r\n4. Book needs to be formatted for kindle direct publishing (KDP) print AND ebook formats!\r\n\r\n* This book is for teenagers. It is written as to be a “roadmap” for important decisions in life.\r\n* It will give them tips and hints and counsel on making wise choices in their life so they can maximize their happiness and success.\r\n* Because it will act as a roadmap, all art and design elements, both on the cover, and in the manuscript should be done with a “map and direction” theme-utilizing roadside signs and symbols (will give more specific direction on this once the contract is granted and the Freelancer has seen the manuscript)','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651330848425750529?success','-',7,'United States','Surprise',600.000,'fixed',600.000,'2023-04-26',1,'2023-04-26',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-26 21:33:13',NULL,17,3,NULL,119),
(19678,'Need a Healthcare / Medical Virtual Assistant (HVA)',22,'Hi!\r\nWe are looking for one HVA to support the rest of our team. The hours are Monday-Friday 9am-11am PST (9:30pm-11:30pm IST, or 12am-2am PHT). This position could be anywhere from a minimum of 3-4 months, to many years if it\'s a good fit and you\'d like to continue.\r\nYou will primarily be helping us with medical documentation, note writing, scheduling, email communications, new patient contracts, billing, charging cards, payment reconciliation, auditing payments, prior authorizations, billing corrections, data entry, and general revenue cycle management.\r\nYou may also be asked to help with miscellaneous online research tasks and executive assistance for the medical director.\r\nThis job is ideal for RNs and MDs, who are looking for part-time work at scheduled hours (9am-11am PST 5 days a week). Must be HIPAA certified or willing to do the 1-hour certificate.\r\nThank you!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651214274498899969','-',7,'United States','Palo Alto',18.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-26',1,'2023-04-26',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-26 21:34:17',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
(19679,'Scheduling Manager',21,'Guada Psych and The Chicago Foundation for Mental Health (TCFMH) are outpatient mental health centers run by the same owner. Guada Psych is a for-profit company located in Schaumburg, IL and TCFMH is a nonprofit community mental health organization with locations in Auburn Gresham and Little Village. We are a group of mental health providers who are passionate about offering quality mental healthcare to all, especially those who live in areas that lack resources. We are in a period of expansion and are looking for a scheduling manager. The person must speak English and Spanish! People must have a quiet place to work without a noisy background; this is not a job for people who take care of young children in their homes.\r\n\r\n-Answer phone and schedule patients’ initial therapy sessions. This requires you to collect insurance information (we have a separate billing department who handle insurance verificantions).\r\n\r\n-Respond to all voicemails\r\n\r\n-Use our electronic medical record (EMR)\r\n\r\n-Maintain spreadsheet (excel or any preferred method) with weekly counts of therapist sessions\r\n\r\n-Communicate with staff regarding office needs at all locations, communicate information to supervisor.\r\n\r\n-Handle records requests, we currently receive an average of 3-6 per month. This entails requesting your supervisor to send you a clinical chart, you then ensure we have a release on file and fax the chart to the necessary party.\r\n\r\n-Send out emails, make phone calls to patients, community partners, colleagues, etc per supervisor\'s request\r\n\r\n-Schedule meetings in supervisor\'s calandar\r\n\r\n-Schedule reviews with staff (quarterly)\r\n\r\n\r\n-The person in this role will have different tasks they will be working on while they are not answering phone calls or doing any of the above listed duties. For example, working on making a list of the assessment test inventory we have along with a list of passwords. These tasks will not be time sensitive.\r\n\r\nIf you think you might be a good fit for this role and hold the skills for this job, please apply!\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who is a good fit for our organization, which is dedicated to providing accessible and affordable mental health services. We hope to meet you soon!','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651219113848410113?success','-',7,'United States','US',20.000,'perhour',18.000,'2023-04-26',1,'2023-04-26',1,'normal bidding',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-26 21:35:11',NULL,12,3,NULL,157),
