(19728,'Payroll Contractor',38,'Scope of Work\r\n\r\nWe are currently seeking an experienced remote, part-time Payroll Contractor to join our team. The ideal candidate will be trained and well-versed in payroll processing in the United States of America, with skills in dealing with government tax websites, customer support issues in tax and payroll, and experience with Quickbooks Online, TSheets (QBO Time), Gusto, Paychex, and other payroll software and their corresponding accounting integrations.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n-Implement, maintain, and review payroll processing systems to ensure timely and accurate processing of payroll transactions, including salaries, benefits, garnishments, taxes, and other deductions.\r\n-Ensure accurate and timely processing of payroll updates, including new hires, terminations, and changes to pay rates.\r\n-Prepare and maintain accurate records and reports of payroll transactions.\r\n-Ensure compliance with federal, state, and local payroll, wage, and hour laws and best practices.\r\n-Facilitate audits by providing records and documentation to auditors.\r\n-Identify and recommend updates to payroll processing software, systems, and procedures.\r\n-Perform other duties as assigned.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n-Extensive knowledge of the payroll function, including preparation, balancing, internal control, and payroll taxes.\r\n-Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail.\r\n-Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\r\n-Strong supervisory and leadership skills.\r\n-Proficient with payroll software and experience with various accounting software.\r\n-If you have a strong background in payroll management and are passionate about providing exceptional customer support, we encourage you to contact us regarding this exciting opportunity.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651601281635004417?success','-',7,'United States','Carlsbad',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-27',1,'2023-04-27',1,'Client may ask for meeti