(19764,'Experienced Bookkeeper / Accounting Assistant who knows Xero well Needed',39,'We are searching for an entry level Accounting Assistant / Bookkeeper who is comfortable with working in a fast-paced environment. The ideal candidate will be passionate about helping organizations find optimal methods to support business growth and career development.\r\n\r\nABOUT US: The Family Centred Practices Group (FCPG) designs and monitors comprehensive educational and behavioural intervention programs for families with young children who have been diagnosed with an autism spectrum disorder or related disability.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n• Manage client billing/invoicing\r\n• Manage month end and year-end accounting related / bookkeeping processes\r\n• Conduct all administrative work relating to ROE’s/accounting records\r\n• Process payments to vendors\r\n• Use Asana to manage daily, weekly and monthly tasks\r\n• Prepare and manage various spreadsheets related to accounting related matters\r\n• Provide excellent client service by resolving invoice exceptions\r\n• Ensure compliance with Federal and Provincial legislation with regards to deductions, remittances, and reporting requirements\r\n• Participate in other activities and projects as required\r\n\r\nOther Specific Duties:\r\n- Request bank and credit card statements\r\n- Verify bank and credit statement balances against Xero bank and credit card account balances to make sure balances all agree before doing any bank reconciliation\r\n- Use Dext to manage bills and receipts so anything submitted by you and your team will be published via Dext as expenses with backup receipts attached in Xero\r\n- Download monthly consultant invoices from Sync (our online file sharing system), attach and enter them in Xero\r\n- Perform bank accounts reconciliation\r\n- Download payroll reports from Sync and enter them in Xero while doing bank reconciliation\r\n- Perform credit card accounts reconciliation\r\n- Generate and send query lists for any transactions that were missing receipts or need additional details, clarification for proper reconciliation. - Reconcile those transactions upon Tina’s responses\r\n- Record monthly office wages and salaries based on the detail provided by admin team\r\n- Record expenses paid\r\n- Accrue payroll for the month based on cut-off date\r\n- Review accounts payable details\r\n- Review fixed assets accounts and enter any new assets into fixed assets register\r\n- Run depreciation\r\n- Send out monthly income tax payment reminder\r\n- Calculate and record quarterly income tax (done quarterly)\r\nPrepare employer health tax return (done annually) (https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/taxes/employer-health-tax/employer-health-tax-overview/eht-file-pay)\r\n- File employer health tax return with etaxbc (done annually)\r\n- Calculate instalments for employer health tax (done annually) and inform Clinical Director of payment amount and due dates\r\n- Send out quarterly employer health tax payment reminders\r\n- Help with editing or fixing invoices, credit note upon request\r\n- Enter budget in Xero upon request\r\n- Write off bad debt upon request\r\n\r\nAdditional Responsibilities may include:\r\n• Policies and procedures manuals\r\n• Maintaining employee and client electronic and physical files\r\n• Support for Clinical Director; research and related tasks, including creating various spreadsheets and graphs / data analysis\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n• Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience in Bookkeeping and/or Accounting\r\n• Previous payroll experience with salary and hourly employees\r\n• Experience with accounting software, specifically Xero\r\n• Intermediate computer skills using Excel, Word and able to quickly learn new computer programs and database tools\r\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills and interpersonal skills\r\n• Ability to lead, work collaboratively and prioritize to meet all deadlines\r\n• Have a positive and friendly personality with a demonstrated strong work ethic\r\n• Ability to multi-task in a very fast paced environment\r\n• Able to handle challenging situations in a confidential and diplomatic manner\r\n• Ability to work 25 hours per week Monday to Friday from home (ideally between the office hours from 10 am to 6 pm PST but this is flexible)\r\n• Able to start training immediately','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651689318588420097?success','-',7,'United States','Canada',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-04-27',1,'2023-04-27',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-27 20:47:48',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
(19765,'US/International Accountant with IFRS and/or GAAP experience',39,'We are looking for a US/International Accountant to have a wide range of duties in performing and overseeing accounting functions for the company’s international fruit trading and distribution subsidiaries in Latin America, US. and Europe. Activities include G/L accounting, AP & AR functions, monthly close, account reconciliations, vendor payments, invoicing, intercompany accounting, and variance analysis.\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate must be proficient in GAAP, while also having a working understanding of IFRS. Responsible for the overall accuracy and timeliness of monthly financial accounting.\r\n\r\nThis role will serve important retail accounts like:\r\n\r\n- Walmart\r\n- Costco\r\n- and others...\r\n\r\n--\r\n\r\nResponsibilities\r\n\r\nJournal entries, account reconciliations, and variance analysis.\r\nCoordinate appropriate approval and coding of supplier/vendor invoices.\r\nMonitor outstanding AP and ensure timely payments to vendors/ suppliers.\r\nMonitor outstanding AR to ensure timely payments and reconciliation.\r\nReconcile inter-company balances between subsidiaries.\r\nRecord monthly payroll based on service provider reports.\r\nCollaborate with external auditors to ensure successful audit results and compliance.\r\nIdentify internal control and process gaps and develop and implement recommendations for resolution.\r\nParticipate in the ongoing development/establishment of accounting policies and procedures including the review and implementation of process and system changes.\r\nContinued focus on improving system efficiencies and business practices.\r\n\r\nExperience\r\n\r\nBS in Accounting.\r\n3-5 years of progressive experience in public or private accounting is required.\r\nCPA, Chartered Accountant, or equivalent professional accreditation is strongly preferred.\r\nInventory/ manufacturing experience is strongly preferred.\r\nIntercompany accounting expertise is strongly preferred.\r\nLast mile and high logistics cadence experience are strongly preferred.\r\nAdvanced Excel skills.\r\n1-2 years of supervisory experience managing a staff of professionals preferred.\r\nSpanish language skills are a plus, but not necessary.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651701995575160833?success','-',7,'United States','Alpharetta',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-27',1,'2023-04-27',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-27 21:37:51',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
(19766,'Small business taxes for US-based international services firm',38,'We are a small services firm based in the US whose sales are primarily outside the US.\r\n\r\nWe need a certified accountant who can file taxes on our behalf.\r\n\r\nAll our books are kept with Quickbooks. We have no property and everyone is paid as a contractor (no W2s).\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who can:\r\n- Help navigate sales tax\r\n- Tell us how to account for salary payments to owners\r\n- Guide filing with a foreign owner\r\n\r\nIf the project goes well then there are 3 additional projects you may be invited to work on including a business acquisition, business restructuring, and tax preparation for the following year for 2 businesses.\r\n\r\nUpon hiring, this will be updated with the agreed upon deliverables.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651703467083108353?success','-',7,'United States','United States',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-27',1,'2023-04-27',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-27 21:44:03',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
