(19779,'Brand Identity Specialist',2,'About Us:\r\nWe\'re a leading Branding SaaS company dedicated to empowering professional brand builders and progressive business leaders. We\'re passionate about creating cutting-edge tools and resources to help our clients build unforgettable brands.\r\n\r\nThe Opportunity:\r\nWe are currently seeking an experienced Brand Identity Designer to work on a one-off project. The ideal candidate will have a keen eye for modern design and a passion for SaaS projects. This is an exciting opportunity to work with a dynamic team and help shape the visual identity of a groundbreaking product.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\nDevelop a comprehensive brand identity, including logo, color palette, typography, and other visual elements\r\n\r\nCreate a style guide and identity guidelines to ensure consistent implementation across various touchpoints\r\n\r\nCollaborate with our team to incorporate design feedback and revisions\r\nDeliver high-quality original design files and identity guidelines within the 2-3 week timeframe\r\n\r\nMaintain clear and responsive communication with the team throughout the project\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\nProven experience in brand identity design, preferably in the SaaS industry\r\n\r\nProficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, specifically Illustrator, Photoshop, and InDesign\r\n\r\nStrong portfolio showcasing relevant design work\r\n\r\nHighly responsive and excellent communication skills\r\n\r\nAbility to work independently and collaboratively\r\n\r\n\r\nBonus:\r\nWhile this is a one-off project, there is a possibility for further UX/UI design projects for the right designer.\r\n\r\nTo apply, please submit your resume along with your design portfolio showcasing relevant work examples. We look forward to seeing your creativity in action!\r\n\r\nWe\'re excited to find the perfect designer to bring our brand to life. Good luck with your application!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01827ae5fce618a573','-',7,'United States','Cogee',50.000,'perhour',50.000,'2023-04-28',1,'2023-04-28',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-28 12:42:08',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
(19780,'Freelance Contractor Bookkeeper',39,'Company Overview:\r\nWe are a rapidly growing company in search of an experienced and detail-oriented Freelance Contractor Bookkeeper to join our dynamic team. The successful candidate will be responsible for maintaining accurate financial records, ensuring compliance with GAAP principles, and providing financial insights that contribute to our organization\'s success. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who is looking to work in a flexible and collaborative environment.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n\r\nMaintain accurate and up-to-date financial records using popular accounting software such as QuickBooks and Xero.\r\nReconcile bank statements, credit card statements, and other financial documents.\r\nManage accounts payable and accounts receivable, ensuring timely processing of invoices and payments.\r\nPrepare monthly, quarterly, and annual financial reports, including balance sheets, profit and loss statements, and cash flow statements.\r\nEnsure compliance with GAAP principles and assist in the preparation of financial statements for external auditors.\r\nAnalyze financial data to identify trends, discrepancies, and opportunities for improvement.\r\nCollaborate with other team members and departments to ensure smooth financial operations and accurate reporting.\r\nMaintain strict confidentiality and adhere to all applicable data protection regulations.\r\nRequired Qualifications:\r\n\r\nBachelor\'s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field.\r\nA minimum of 3 years of experience in bookkeeping or a similar role.\r\nThorough understanding of GAAP principles and financial reporting.\r\nProficiency in popular accounting software such as QuickBooks and Xero.\r\nAdvanced skills in Excel and other document management applications.\r\nStrong attention to detail and the ability to identify and resolve discrepancies in financial records.\r\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\r\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team, meeting deadlines and delivering high-quality work.\r\nStrong problem-solving and analytical skills.\r\nPreferred Qualifications:\r\n\r\nProfessional certifications such as CPA, CMA, or CB are a plus.\r\nExperience working in a remote environment','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1651938976533106689?success','-',7,'United States','Aventura',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-04-28',1,'2023-04-28',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-04-28 13:20:37',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
