(20104,'Real Estate Investment Analyst',39,'Real Estate Investment Analyst\r\n\r\nWith an Emphasis on Financial Modeling, Proformas, and Stress Testing. The Candidate will be responsible for:\r\n\r\nBuilding Financial Models:\r\n- Building, updating, or editing the financial models used to project property income and profits.\r\n- We are constantly updating our analysis of each project, considering changes to pricing, timing, costs, and strategy.\r\n- The qualified candidate will be able to discuss and quickly digest the necessary considerations, then build or alter the current analysis to consider the new information.\r\n\r\nMarket Data & Analysis: Find and analyze market data that is relevant to the project they are evaluating. For example, analysts may look at market rental rates, absorption figures, and vacancy.\r\n- Our portfolio properties include multifamily, hospitality, single-family residential, and senior living facilities.\r\n- The qualified candidate will understand the key factors affecting the investment in each category as well as the corresponding sources of quality data.\r\n- Data collection, analysis, interpretation, projection, & reporting skills are a requirement of the position.\r\n\r\nSensitivity Analysis: Analysts may run many different scenarios to account for unforeseen circumstances. For example, they may present “base case,” “best case,” and “worst case” property scenarios.\r\n- The qualified candidate will test a range of possibilities for each data input and identify the most impactful key metrics.\r\n- The successful candidate will identify the investment strategy most likely to produce a positive outcome, based on a robust sensitivity analysis.\r\n\r\nDebt Sizing & Equity Returns: Work with banks and lenders to determine the maximum amount of debt that a project can support based on projected cash flows and lending requirements.\r\n- The qualified candidate will have a complete understanding of commercial loan terms, fees, analysis, underwriting standards etc.\r\n- The successful candidate will analyze current commercial debt options and create a capital stack that is most advantageous for the investment type.\r\n- A complete capital stack analysis will identify the best available debt and equity combination to maximize investment returns for all parties in balance with an acceptable amount of risk.\r\n\r\nProvide Opinions: Analysts may be expected to provide their opinion about the attractiveness of a deal. Senior management may rely on this opinion when deciding whether or not to greenlight a deal.\r\n- The qualified candidate will create and implement a rapid analysis tool that is capable of rapidly qualifying a potential investment.\r\n- The candidate must accurately identify & recommend quality investments as well as disqualify offerings based on current market data.\r\n\r\nLikely Growth of the Role into the following areas of responsibility:\r\n- Document Review & Analysis: A review of important documents including: leases, historical financial statements, property tax records, and utility bills.\r\n- Records & File Maintenance: Management of files (electronic or paper) for each deal. For smaller firms, these files may be used for reference throughout the investment lifecycle. In larger, publicly traded firms, these files may be used in regulatory or internal risk reviews.\r\n- Prepare Underwriting Memo: Documentation of their analysis in a detailed underwriting memo that is presented to senior management and other stakeholders. The contents of the memo form the basis of the invest/don’t invest decision.\r\n- Stakeholder Meetings & Presentations: For each deal, the analyst is the expert on the finances of the deal. As such, they may be asked to give presentations to potential investors, lenders, or other stakeholders.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1653829427022241793?success','-',7,'United States','Greensboro',25.000,'Open this select menu',25.000,'2023-05-03',1,'2023-05-03',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-03 18:32:10',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
