(20109,'Estate and Tax Planner for Wyoming Estate',38,'We are seeking an experienced and qualified Estate and Tax Planner to provide guidance and advice on managing the estate of our client in Wyoming. The candidate must be knowledgeable in estate planning and tax laws, specifically in the state of Wyoming.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n-Assess the estate of the client and provide recommendations on how to manage and preserve assets\r\n-Develop and implement strategies for estate planning, tax minimization, and wealth transfer\r\n-Prepare and review legal documents such as wills, trusts, and powers of attorney\r\n-Advise on the proper titling and ownership of assets, including real estate, investments, and business interests\r\n-Stay up-to-date with changes in tax laws and regulations that may affect the client\'s estate\r\n-Communicate with the client\'s financial advisors, accountants, and attorneys to ensure a cohesive plan\r\n-Provide guidance and support during the probate process if necessary\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n\r\n-Bachelor\'s degree in finance, accounting, law, or related field\r\n-Minimum of 5 years of experience in estate planning and tax law\r\n-Strong knowledge of Wyoming state tax laws and regulations\r\n-Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills\r\n-Effective communication and interpersonal skills\r\n-Detail-oriented with strong organizational skills\r\n-Ability to work independently and meet deadlines\r\n\r\nIf you are an experienced Estate and Tax Planner who is interested in working on this project, please submit your proposal along with your resume and references.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1653835971326672897?','-',7,'United States','Tivoli',2500.000,'fixed',2500.000,'2023-05-03',1,'2023-05-03',1,'00',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-03 18:59:35',NULL,11,3,NULL,160),
