(20137,'Seeking Financial Analyst & Business Modeling Forecast',39,'We are startup skin care company and have begun our initial financial forecasting for the business. We are interested in working with a financial analyst to understand questions that we need to know and have answers for in our business plan. Some of the questions we would like to have answered are the following:\r\n\r\n• For free shipping over $50, what would be the best price point that would give us 25% profit margin?\r\n\r\n* How should we price products in relationship to our competitors and what would be the window for pricing that give us the best chance of success?\r\n\r\n• If we want to encourage people to subscribe and save money, what discount could we offer for 4-, 8- and 12-month packet subscriptions? Must include all applicable discounts and free shipping.\r\n\r\n• What bundle discount can we provide that include free shipping but maintaining at least 25% profit margin?\r\n\r\n• If we’re offering 60-day trial, what would be the best strategy to pay our suppliers and not run out of product.\r\n\r\n• Can you provide a 3-year financial forecast if we anticipate selling on average 50 bottles per day and 100 packets per day the first year, 200 bottles per day and 400 packets the second year and 500 bottles per day and 800 packets per day year three.\r\n\r\nWe have many more questions and would like to work with someone that can help us build excel sheets and give us financial planning guidance. We are open to working with international applicants whom are skilled in this area.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1653868237469204481?success','-',7,'United States','Claymont',25.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-05-03',1,'2023-05-03',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-03 21:05:48',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
