(20356,'Accounts Payable',39,'About Fairgrove Property Management:\r\n\r\nFairgrove Property Management provides industry-leading residential property management services to real estate investors and residents throughout Southern California. Founded in 1976, the Irvine, CA-based company makes owning investment properties profitable and effortless. Four decades of experience in the residential real estate sector empowers Fairgrove to deliver a combination of exceptional operational expertise and innovative technology to both owners and residents. The company’s management approach enables stress-free, passive investing for owners, and provides residents with quality housing where service is the highest priority. Fairgrove Property Management operates in four major Southern California markets and is rapidly expanding across the West.\r\n\r\n\r\nJob Summary\r\n\r\nThe Property Accountant, under supervision of the Director of Accounting, will be responsible for ensuring the proper and accurate entry and coding of accounting related transactions, invoices, expense reports and the timely submission of payments for owner and vendor transactions.\r\nMust work Pacific Standard Time for California business hours 8AM - 5PM\r\n\r\nEssential Job Functions – To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential function satisfactorily.\r\n\r\nProvide real estate accounting and clerical support\r\nPrepare bank deposits, general ledger postings and statements\r\nManage accounts payable transactions using accounting software\r\nCreate and update vendors and maintain communication\r\nResearch, track and restore accounting or documentation discrepancies\r\nWork with vendors and internal departments to ensure seamless onboarding of new vendors; gather contracts and resolve any payment issues\r\nReview expense reports and ensure all documentation is included\r\nEnsure all bills are coded accurately and approved for payment in a timely manner\r\nReview daily payment requests for accuracy and confirm no duplicates are processed\r\nReconcile bank accounts for all owner accounts\r\nRun reports and conduct analysis as needed\r\nSupport Accounting team with ad hoc reporting or special projects\r\nProvides professional and consistent customer service for both internal and external customers\r\nEnhance professional growth and development through participation in educational programs, current literature, and seminars\r\nPerform other duties as assigned.\r\nExperience in AppFolio a MUST','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1654543919659077633','-',7,'United States','Santa Ana',10.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-05-05',1,'2023-05-05',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-05 19:53:28',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
(20357,'Seeking collaborative bookkeeper for growing team!',39,'Specialized Office Support (SOS) is a unique group of remote workers providing professional fractional COO services for businesses and their owners. We are specialists who walk the talk in the remote business world and teach others how to do it effectively.\r\n\r\nIf you encapsulate the following traits, we\'d love to hear from you:\r\n\r\nCurious - Do you have a strong desire to understand complex problems and offer your ideas to help solve the problem?\r\n\r\nResourcefulness - Are you motivated and inspired by out-of-the-box thinking, generating new ideas to visualize solutions to problems?\r\n\r\nPerseverance - Are you focused to give continuous effort to tasks and projects despite difficulties?\r\n\r\nAs a remote working staff, we diligently follow the below critical actions daily and would expect the same of you:\r\n\r\n1. We say, \"How may I serve you?\" to our fellow remote workers as we understand it is imperative to collaborate to move all people and the work forward with our talents.\r\n\r\n2. We ask and answer questions of our fellow remote workers knowing questions improve the outcomes of our projects to the highest quality.\r\n\r\n3. Most importantly - we are accountable daily to the SOS Remote Project Management Processes assuring strong collaboration in meeting goals and deadlines as a team.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, SOS is looking to create a partnership with a bookkeeper/bookkeeping business as a B2B relationship assisting SOS in servicing our clients with monthly bookkeeping, catch-up bookkeeping, financial reporting, and other needs requested by SOS clients. You would report directly to SOS, who is a Quickbook Pro Advisor and would take direction on all accounts from SOS.\r\n\r\nTasks requested would include but are not limited to:\r\n\r\n-Monthly reconciliations\r\n\r\n-Updated monthly financial reporting\r\n\r\n-JE for payroll (if you don’t offer payroll services)\r\n\r\n-1099/1096 Preparation, mailing, and filing to include ongoing management of vendors in QBO throughout the tax year\r\n\r\n-Expense management\r\n\r\n-A/P and A/R management through QB, Melio, Stripe, or any other payment system the client may have set up directly through their bank or other applications\r\n\r\nPreferred initial skills:\r\n\r\n- Comfortable communicating via Slack and/or Zoom\r\n\r\n- Read and follow SOPs set up for every SOS client’s QBO file\r\n\r\n- Read and review transcripts from all appropriate client meetings when assigned\r\n\r\nIf you think you can fit our remote company culture with strong communication skills, we will look for a contractor to hire for these outlined projects and likely more in the future. If you are our person, SOS would love to be your preferred client.\r\n\r\nPlease include the word \"SOS\" in your proposal so we know you thoroughly read our post.\r\n\r\nThank you!\r\n\r\n- The SOS Team','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1654538522896400385','-',7,'United States','00',40.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-05',1,'2023-05-05',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-05 19:54:30',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
