(20383,'Animator for SaaS market inisghts platform',8,'Introduction\r\n\r\nTrendata has been in the market insights industry for approximately 5 years. During that time numerous customers used the insights to shape their marketing strategies. Up until now those insights were bespoke. But we have seen similarities between the requests, despite them being tailored to specific industries and demands.\r\nBecause of this we’re turning our approach into a SaaS platform. To bring this SaaS platform to market we are looking for a UX/Visual designer to join our virtual team.\r\n\r\nAbout Trendata\r\nBorn as a subsidiary of an online marketing agency. Trendata was born to help provide deeper insights in market demand. With a previous manual task now being automated based on Trendata’s proprietary software the time required to conduct research and the derived from it changed.\r\n\r\nWith the automation of this process, Trendata was born. Slowly moving away from the traditional “keyword research” and pivoting towards market insights. Now, the most important pivot comes. From bespoke insights into standardized but customizable insights in 5 different, marketing related areas:\r\n- Market insights\r\n- Competitor insights\r\n- Brand insights\r\n- Customer / consumer insights\r\n- Product / service insights\r\n\r\nJob Requirements\r\nTrendata’s market intelligence platform is quite extensive. To give the best possible upfront explanation of the platform we are looking for an animator helping us with short to mid-length animations depicting how the platform features work.\r\n\r\nThe work needs to be done in quite a short time frame so flexibility is of the essence.\r\n\r\nIdeally you have a background in SaaS/technical products and are capable of capturing the essence of a message in your designs.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01fc5f92a6a480adde','-',7,'United States','Hengelo',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-08',1,'2023-05-08',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-08 08:01:20',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
(20384,'Logo Design for Pop Art Food Stickers Company | Text-to-image | AI generated Art',10,'Style is Pop-Art, Light-Art, Fun, Mouth-watering, bite-taken-out-of Style. The way I can best describe the style we are after is with the example photos of our work attached. Specifically the style of our Pizza sticker and our donut sticker.\r\n\r\nWe are a soon-to-be Etsy shop creating Stickers. Stickers specifically of people’s favorite foods.\r\n\r\nSo, a design with a similar style to the photos I’ve attached is the goal.\r\n\r\nLooking forward to hearing from you creatives!\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\nSticker Bites Co.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1652969575920148481','https://trello.com/c/1fmLUpLw',165,'United States','Antioch',100.000,'fixed',100.000,'2023-05-08',1,'2023-05-08',1,'na',1,NULL,NULL,1,'2023-05-08 08:07:22','2023-05-24 20:48:54',18,3,NULL,156),
(20385,'UI/UX work for our company\'s website',4,'We are looking for a UI/UX expert to work on updating our company\'s VI and website for a duration of 1 to 4 months. The ideal candidate should have a good understanding of Figma, Graphic Design, Landing Page, Mockup, Prototyping, Business with 10-99 Employees, Style Guide, and Web Design.\r\n\r\nAs the UI/UX expert, your responsibilities will include updating our LOGO, Color palette, Typography, Imagery, User Interface (UI) elements, Brand guidelines, and Consistency, You will start working on updating our website to a user-friendly website design that is visually appealing and easy to navigate. You will be required to develop wireframes and prototypes for the website and ensure that the website is optimized for all devices. You will also be responsible for creating a style guide for the website.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for a candidate who is highly creative and has a good eye for detail. You should have excellent communication skills, prompt in response, and be able to work collaboratively with our team.\r\n\r\nTo apply for this position, please submit a proposal outlining how you can help with the project. Please include links to past completed projects that you have worked on. We look forward to hearing from you soon.\r\n\r\nThe task will begin with some budget milestone tasks first for some Visual Identity and trail some prototype page designs, and we may convert to work hourly if we start the work in the long term\r\n\r\nMilestone 1 ($50): We will give you a reference website and you will quickly turn around with us on some visual identity design for us by referring to that website, LOGO update, Color palette, Typography, Icon, and illustration examples.\r\n\r\nMilestone 2 ($100): Draft on improving the looking and re-design the UI and UX for the blog pages, You will mockup a better design to improve the looking and interaction by referring to the visual guideline in Milestone 1.\r\n\r\nMilestone 3 ($50): revision and delivery','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~016f5ba7477e9370f3','-',7,'United States','Belmont',500.000,'fixed',500.000,'2023-05-08',1,'2023-05-08',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-08 08:08:41',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
(20386,'Branding package: logo, color palette, typography, style guide',2,'An early-phase startup, in the travel & lifestyle space, is looking for a talented designer to design our brand package, including:\r\n1) Logo\r\n2) Color palette (including colorblind colors for our site charts)\r\n3) Brand typography\r\n4) Brand style guide\r\n5) Basic social media graphics (background banners for our social media pages)\r\n\r\nOur initial budget is limited. If the job is successful, we might be able to offer you more work.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~0188879e06f817295c','-',7,'United States','Bangkok',210.000,'fixed',210.000,'2023-05-08',1,'2023-05-08',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-08 08:12:33',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
(20387,'Graphic Design for 4-5 Page \"Rate Card\"',2,'Hi, I\'m looking for a graphic designer to create a 4-5 page PDF \"rate card\" for my business. The rate card will be used to showcase my pricing and services to potential clients (one in particular who\'s asking right now).\r\n\r\nThe ideal candidate is either self-taught or professionally trained in the core elements that make up solid graphic design. It\'s ideal if you have experience in brochure design, and sales and marketing collateral.\r\n\r\nI understand the value of doing a deep dive on brand identity, and the psychology of it all, but right now I\'m looking for \"good is good enough\".. something that looks professional, and matches my website suzannereilley.com\r\n\r\nI can share copy, you make it look beautiful.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested, I\'d love to hear a bit about how you came to learn graphic design, your design process, and I\'d like to check out work you\'ve done for yourself or other clients. I\'m really open to any experience level, as long as you do solid work.\r\n\r\nI also know the value of planning ahead, but a quick-ish turnaround is appreciated on this one!','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~013177fcf38c476d90','-',7,'United States','Mount Carmel',200.000,'fixed',200.000,'2023-05-08',1,'2023-05-08',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-08 08:18:04',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
