(20566,'Accounts Payable Specialist',39,'Job Summary\r\nThe Accounts Payable Specialist will play a critical role in ensuring the financial health of our tech startup by managing our accounts payable processes. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in accounting and finance, with experience in invoicing, collections, and vendor management. You will play a critical role in ensuring timely and accurate payments to our vendors, maintaining detailed records of financial transactions, and helping to improve the efficiency and accuracy of our accounts payable processes.\r\n\r\nWhat you’ll do\r\nManage the accounts payable process, including processing vendor invoices, reconciling vendor statements, and preparing payments.\r\nUpload documentation in the client procurement platforms to ensure timely payments.\r\nTally expenses and create payment schedules, and keep them up to date, ensuring accurate cash flow projections for approval.\r\nMaintain accurate and up-to-date records of all financial transactions related to accounts payable in our accounting system.\r\nEnsure compliance with company policies and procedures, as well as accounting standards and regulations.\r\nContinuously look for opportunities to improve the efficiency and accuracy of our accounts payable processes.\r\n\r\nWhat you’ll bring\r\n2+ years of experience in accounts payable and/or accounts receivable, preferably in a tech startup or high-growth environment.\r\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a focus on accuracy and attention to detail.\r\nProficiency in accounting software, such as QuickBooks, Xero, or NetSuite.\r\nExcellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and external stakeholders.\r\nAbility to manage multiple priorities and deadlines, and to adapt to changing circumstances in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.\r\nFluent in English (verbal and written)\r\n\r\nWho you are\r\nA detail-oriented individual. You have a strong attention to detail and are able to manage large volumes of data and transactions with accuracy and precision.\r\nA problem solver. You have the ability to reduce complex problems down to the right balance of flexibility, power, and ease of use, and are able to develop creative solutions to address financial challenges.\r\nA strong communicator. You have excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and are able to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and external stakeholders to achieve shared goals.\r\nA self-starter. You are able to work independently and proactively, taking ownership of your work and driving results even in the face of ambiguity or uncertainty.\r\nA team player. You value collaboration and are able to work effectively with others, contributing to a positive and supportive team environment.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1655974474747510785?success','-',7,'United States','Philadelphia',20.000,'perhour',20.000,'2023-05-09',1,'2023-05-09',1,'Client may ask for meeting if he opens up for chat',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-09 16:35:30',NULL,21,3,NULL,123),
