(21139,'QuickBooks Online Certified Bookkeeper',39,'We are seeking an experienced and certified QuickBooks Online bookkeeper to assist with the reconciliation of transactions for our small business. This role involves managing financial records between QuickBooks Online, our credit card statements, and bank accounts.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities include:\r\n\r\n- Reconciling transactions from our credit card statements and bank accounts, with an initial focus on bank statements.\r\n- Working with PDF statements stored in our Dropbox folders, most of which have been auto-imported into QuickBooks Online.\r\n- Addressing exceptions where one or two statements may be missing, requiring the creation of an adjusting entry to bridge any gaps for subsequent reconciliation.\r\n- Manually entering statement entries for two to three months where the auto-import from the banking system was unsuccessful. This involves minimal entries, approximately 50 transactions.\r\n- Classifying expenses that average 30 to 50 transactions per month.\r\n- Managing a \'questions account\' for expense items that require further clarification.\r\n\r\nPrevious experience:\r\n\r\n- You should have extensive experience with, and/or certification in QuickBooks Online.\r\n- Familiarity with Basecamp is desirable as we have previously coordinated bookkeeping tasks with bookeepers in great detail through this platform.\r\n- Prior experience reconciling similar basic accounts is highly preferred.\r\n\r\nCommunication:\r\n\r\n- We anticipate a quick onboarding process with an orientation within 3 to 4 days, aiming to complete the project within 15 days.\r\n- We require good English communication skills as real-time conversation via Skype, screen sharing, and Zoom meetings will be essential for project coordination.\r\n\r\nIf you are a diligent and detail-oriented bookkeeper with a proven track record in QuickBooks Online, we would be delighted to hear from you. Your expertise will play a vital role in maintaining the financial health of our business.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1658874940938395649','-',7,'United States','South Charleston',20.000,'perhour',25.000,'2023-05-17',1,'2023-05-17',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-17 19:00:56',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
(21140,'Accountant for Bank Account Reconciliation',39,'We are seeking a highly skilled and detail-oriented Accountant to join our team. As an Accountant, your primary responsibility will be to reconcile 10 bank accounts for our company, ensuring compliance with the Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) standards. These accounts are located in the United States and Nigeria. This is a remote position, and you will have the flexibility to work from anywhere.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nPerform regular bank account reconciliations for 10 accounts in the United States and Nigeria, adhering to the GAAP standards.\r\nMatch transactions and balances between bank statements and internal accounting records while applying GAAP guidelines.\r\nInvestigate and resolve any discrepancies or variances found during the reconciliation process, ensuring compliance with GAAP principles.\r\nIdentify and communicate any financial or operational risks discovered during the reconciliation process, taking into consideration GAAP requirements.\r\nPrepare clear and concise reports summarizing the reconciliation results, following GAAP guidelines for financial reporting.\r\nCollaborate with the finance team to ensure timely and accurate financial reporting in accordance with GAAP standards.\r\nMaintain organized and up-to-date documentation of reconciliation activities, keeping in line with GAAP documentation requirements.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1658872636734222337','-',7,'United States','East Orange',300.000,'fixed',300.000,'2023-05-17',1,'2023-05-17',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-17 19:02:35',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
(21141,'Bookkeeper needed to setup and update records',39,'We are seeking a skilled bookkeeper/invoice drafter contractor to join our team. The successful candidate will keep track of monthly expenses, keep financial records, and draft invoices for us. The ideal candidate should have experience in bookkeeping, accounting, and invoicing. The main goal of this position is to ensure that the accounting and bookkeeping records are accurately maintained and presented in a way that makes tax preparation easy. If you possess a strong bookkeeping, accounting, and invoicing background, we invite you to apply and contribute to our success.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n\r\nFinancial Transaction Management:\r\n- Record and document all financial transactions, including daily purchases, receipts, sales, and payments, with meticulous attention to detail.\r\n- Organize and maintain comprehensive financial records, including receipts, invoices, and other relevant documents, in an orderly manner.\r\n\r\nStatement Reconciliation:\r\n- Reconcile bank and credit card statements regularly, ensuring accuracy and resolving any discrepancies promptly.\r\n\r\nInvoice Preparation and Management:\r\n- Create and send detailed and accurate invoices to clients, including all necessary information to facilitate smooth payment processing.\r\n- Ensure timely delivery of invoices and maintain a systematic record of invoices issued and their respective statuses.\r\n\r\nExpense and Income Tracking:\r\n- Monitor and maintain an up-to-date record of monthly expenses and income, enabling accurate financial reporting.\r\n- Analyze financial data to identify trends, anomalies, and opportunities for improvement.\r\n\r\nFinancial Reporting:\r\n- Prepare monthly accounting reports, including balance sheets, income, and cash flow statements, providing clear and concise information to the management team.\r\n- Present financial reports, offering insights and recommendations to aid decision-making processes.\r\n\r\nCompliance and Accuracy:\r\n- Ensure the accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality of all financial records and information.\r\n- Stay informed about relevant tax laws and regulations to ensure compliance and facilitate easy tax preparation.\r\n\r\nSupport for Tax Preparation:\r\n- Assist in tax preparation by providing timely and accurate financial records to external tax professionals or internal finance personnel.\r\n- Collaborate closely with the tax team to address any queries or requests for information.\r\n\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n- Proven work experience as a bookkeeper or in a similar role, demonstrating strong financial management and record-keeping expertise.\r\n- Thorough knowledge of accounting principles, practices, and procedures.\r\n- Proficiency in using bookkeeping software, such as QuickBooks, and familiarity with other relevant financial tools.\r\n- Excellent organizational and time-management skills to effectively handle multiple tasks and meet deadlines.\r\n- Keen attention to detail and a commitment to maintaining high levels of accuracy in financial records.\r\n- Strong communication and interpersonal skills to liaise effectively with team members, clients, and external stakeholders.\r\n- Self-motivated and able to work independently, taking ownership of assigned tasks and demonstrating a proactive attitude.\r\n- A bachelor\'s degree in accounting or a related field is preferred, although relevant experience will also be considered.\r\n\r\nCompensation will be based on an hourly or project basis, depending on the scope and complexity of the work involved. If you are a passionate and self-motivated individual with a genuine interest in bookkeeping and accounting, we encourage you to apply and join our dedicated team at Krishtel.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1658914934838722561','-',7,'United States','Oakland',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-17',1,'2023-05-17',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-17 19:19:42',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
