(21292,'Bookkeeper',39,'We are currently seeking a reliable and detail-oriented individual to assist with general bookkeeping. The candidate will be responsible for invoicing, accounting responsibilities, and data entry into specific applications.\r\n\r\n1. Process invoices, accounts payable, and receivables using QuickBooks.\r\n2. Assist with day-to-day accounting responsibilities.\r\n3. Conduct data entry into specific applications\r\n4. Maintain accurate and up-to-date employee records\r\n5. Communicate with clients, vendors, and employees in a clear and effective manner.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1659671996663275521','-',7,'United States','00',20.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-19',1,'2023-05-19',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-19 21:49:47',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
(21293,'Bookkeeping and financial report builder',39,'ooking for a skilled bookkeeper and financial report builder to clean up accounts and build various reports for me.\r\n\r\nSo you understand the business model, I run a rent to serviced accommodation business, eg I rent properties from landlords and then run the properties as airbnb or booking.com.\r\n\r\nI have 3 properties currently and additional properties in other companies so I may ask for help to do individual company reporting and cross company reporting/forecasting. It\'s just myself running the business so it would just be myself and you\r\n\r\nInitially this is a project but there\'s the potential for me to take on a full time VA - there\'s financial tasks and a lot of others to do. I suppose it\'d just depend what you are interested in.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nResponsibilities (I\'d still like to hear from you if you can do some but not all of these)\r\n\r\nReconcile last 6 months accounts - breaking this down per property\r\n\r\nAdd receipts to all reconcilled transactions in zero\r\n\r\nOnce financial reports etc are built, consider how the financial systems can be systemised/automated\r\n\r\nTeach me some of the basic reconcilation and reporting functionality in the xero etc\r\n\r\n\r\nBuild following\r\n1. Income Statement (Profit and Loss Statement):\r\n• This report summarizes your revenue, expenses, and net profit or loss over a specific period (e.g., monthly, quarterly, annually). It provides an overview of your business\'s financial performance.\r\n2. Balance Sheet:\r\n• The balance sheet provides a snapshot of your business\'s financial position at a given point in time. It includes your assets (e.g., property, furnishings, cash), liabilities (e.g., mortgages, loans), and owner\'s equity.\r\n3. Cash Flow Statement:\r\n• This report tracks the flow of cash into and out of your business over a specific period. It helps you understand how cash is generated and used, providing insights into your business\'s liquidity and ability to meet financial obligations.\r\n4. Occupancy and Revenue Report:\r\n• This report provides an overview of your property\'s occupancy rates and revenue generated over a given period. It helps you analyze trends, identify peak seasons, and evaluate the financial performance of individual units.\r\n5. Expense Report:\r\n• An expense report details your business\'s expenses, including property maintenance, utilities, insurance, marketing, cleaning services, property management fees, and other costs associated with running your serviced accommodations.\r\n6. Tax Reports:\r\n• Depending on your jurisdiction, you will need to generate tax reports for income tax purposes. These reports summarize your taxable income, deductions, and other relevant information required for filing tax returns.\r\n• VAT forecast and VAT return prep\r\n7. Accounts Receivable/Payable Report:\r\n• This report tracks the amounts owed to you by guests (accounts receivable) and the amounts you owe to suppliers, contractors, or vendors (accounts payable). It helps you manage cash flow and ensure timely payments.\r\n8. Forecasting and Budgeting Reports:\r\n• These reports help you plan and make informed financial decisions. They involve projecting future revenue, expenses, and cash flow based on historical data and anticipated changes in the business environment.\r\nIn this regard -you will need to factor in when the business hit the UK VAT threshold and how this will impact profits\r\n9. Variance Analysis Report:\r\n• This report compares actual financial results to budgeted or forecasted figures, highlighting any significant discrepancies. It allows you to identify areas where you exceeded or fell short of expectations, enabling you to take corrective measures.\r\n10. ROI and Performance Metrics:\r\n• Reports to track key performance indicators (KPIs) per property and across the business (Monthly, quarterly and yearly)\r\n\r\naverage daily rate (ADR)\r\noccupancy rate\r\ncapacity\r\nbooking source percentage\r\ngross operating profit (GOP)\r\n\r\nEssential skills\r\nAdvanced excel skills\r\nExperience working with xero - reconciliation and report building\r\nExperience reconciling and building reports in excel or other systems (Open to recommendations)\r\n*Has some knowledge of UK tax - VAT threshold/Corporation tax etc\r\nAbility to think outside the box\r\nNaturally curios\r\nAbility to work autonomously but equally available for check ins','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1659675461172649985','-',7,'United States','London',150.000,'fixed',150.000,'2023-05-19',1,'2023-05-19',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-19 21:51:02',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
