(21426,'Bookkeeping/Spreadsheet expert',39,'I’ve been running my small business for 5+ years now. I’ve never created a process to track finances because my business has been profitable and it hasn’t been necessary. I’d like to get the ship in shape as I’m starting up other businesses that will need better financial tracking.\r\n\r\nWhat I’m looking for- someone to help me forecast cash flow, track expenses, structure billing more effectively. This person may have a background in bookkeeping or accounting, or they may just be a good spreadsheet person. If things go well I’d love to make this a long term relationship.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661109880344051713','-',7,'United States','Beaverton',50.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-23',1,'2023-05-23',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-23 20:45:26',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
(21427,'QBO Advanced Expert required, Big4 Experienced',39,'We are a prominent real estate group of companies specializing in various areas, including Fix and Flip, notes origination, rentals, and more. As part of our financial management process, we utilize QuickBooks Online Advanced to track transactions at the property level. We are currently seeking a highly skilled professional who possesses an in-depth understanding of QuickBooks Online Advanced to assist us in running a comprehensive analysis on multiple data points and potentially restructuring the chart of accounts. Our primary objective is to optimize the outcomes of our existing transactions.\r\nFollowing will be your tasks:\r\nCollaborate with our team to assess the current structure of the chart of accounts in QuickBooks Online Advanced.\r\nConduct a thorough analysis of multiple data points, including transactional records and financial statements.\r\nIdentify areas for potential restructuring and optimization of the chart of accounts.\r\nDevelop a strategic plan for implementing changes to enhance financial reporting accuracy and efficiency.\r\nAssist in migrating data and making necessary adjustments to align with the revised chart of accounts.\r\nProvide expert guidance on best practices and efficient utilization of QuickBooks Online Advanced for real estate transactions.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661117551096729601','-',7,'United States','Denver',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-23',1,'2023-05-23',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-23 21:11:51',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
(21428,'QuickBooks Online Cleanup of Books and ongoing bookkeeping',39,'I need Bookkeeping and Accounting Catch up & Clean up for previous transactions(Categorize, record and reconcile) in QuickBooks Online.\r\n\r\n1. Monthly Ongoing Bookkeeping Quickbooks Online\r\n2. Categorization, Classifications, and Reconciliation of up to 1 years of transactions\r\n3. Record Invoices and Bills in any accounting system\r\n4. Vendors and Customers management\r\n5. Financial Statements Preparation','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661120551139966977','-',7,'United States','Sarasota',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-23',1,'2023-05-23',1,'NA',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-23 21:25:36',NULL,21,3,NULL,155),
(21429,'Bookkeeper',39,'We are seeking a reliable, detail-oriented, and experienced bookkeeper to join our growing multifamily real estate business. The ideal candidate will have a strong understanding of bookkeeping and accounting principles, excellent organizational skills, and a proven track record of managing financial records for small to medium-sized businesses.\r\n\r\nKey Responsibilities:\r\n- Maintain accurate financial records, including accounts payable, accounts receivable, payroll, and general ledger entries.\r\n- Prepare and submit monthly financial statements, including profit and loss statements, balance sheets, and cash flow statements.\r\n- Reconcile bank accounts, credit card statements, and other financial accounts.\r\n- Manage and maintain accurate tenant ledgers, including rent collection, late fees, and security deposit accounting.\r\n- Work closely with the financial manager to prepare and submit annual budgets and financial forecasts.\r\n- Ensure compliance with local, state, and federal tax regulations and requirements.\r\n- Implement and maintain effective financial controls, policies, and procedures.\r\n- Assist in the preparation of year-end financial statements and coordinate with external auditors.\r\n- Collaborate with other team members to improve financial processes and systems.\r\n- Perform other financial and administrative tasks as required.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\nBONUS - Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in accounting, finance, or a related field.\r\nBONUS - Certification Public Accountant or Certified Bookkeeper.\r\n- A minimum of 2 years of experience in bookkeeping, preferably within the real estate industry.\r\n- Proficient understanding of Accrual Basis Accounting.\r\n- Proficiency in accounting software, such as QuickBooks or similar platforms.\r\n- Excellent organizational and time management skills.\r\n- High attention to detail and accuracy.\r\n- Strong written and verbal communication skills.\r\n- Ability to work independently and as part of a team.\r\n- Willing to work in Mountain Standard Time (8 AM MST - 4 PM MST)\r\n- Job is a FULL TIME position\r\n\r\nPlease respond with the subject line “I’m ready to be part of STT”','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661126599831752705','-',7,'United States','-',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-23',1,'2023-05-23',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-23 21:48:18',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
