(21433,'LOGO & BRANDING: tattoo and piercing studio',10,'Innovative Logo and Brand Designer for 9th Gate Gallery Tattoo and Piercing Studio\r\n\r\nDescription:\r\n\r\nWe are embarking on an exciting journey to establish a cutting-edge Tattoo and Piercing Studio called 9th Gate Gallery, and we are in need of a talented logo and brand designer to create a captivating visual identity for our unique establishment. As we strive to redefine the artistry and experience of tattooing and piercing, we are seeking a skilled designer who can craft a logo that embodies our studio\'s vision, artistic expression, and dedication to exceptional service.\r\n\r\nKey Details:\r\n\r\nProject Type: Logo and Brand Design\r\nClient: 9th Gate Gallery Tattoo and Piercing Studio\r\nConcept: Emphasizing artistic expression, creativity, and exceptional service\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\n- Develop an innovative and visually striking logo that reflects the unique identity of 9th Gate Gallery.\r\n- Create a brand identity that aligns with our studio\'s vision and attracts a diverse clientele.\r\n- Incorporate elements of tattooing, piercing, and artistry into the logo design.\r\n- Design a versatile logo that can be effectively used across various platforms, including digital media, signage, stationery, and merchandise.\r\n- Collaborate closely with our team to understand our studio\'s aesthetic preferences and target audience.\r\n- Present multiple logo concepts and provide revisions based on feedback and input.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n- Proven experience in logo and brand design, with a portfolio showcasing your creative expertise.\r\n- Proficiency in industry-standard design software and tools.\r\n- Ability to interpret and translate our studio\'s values and vision into a visually appealing brand identity.\r\n- Strong understanding of color theory, typography, and composition.\r\n- Excellent communication skills to effectively collaborate with our team and incorporate feedback.\r\n\r\nTimeline and Compensation:\r\n\r\nStart Date: ASAP\r\nCompletion Date: June 2, 2023\r\n\r\nIf you are a talented logo and brand designer with a passion for artistic expression and a keen eye for detail, we invite you to join us in establishing 9th Gate Gallery as a premier tattoo and piercing studio. Share your portfolio and proposal, demonstrating your ability to create captivating visual identities, and let\'s embark on this creative endeavor together. Together, we will set new standards of artistry and create a brand that leaves an indelible mark on the tattoo and piercing industry.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01e64603c171d219ac','-',7,'United States','Canada',350.000,'fixed',350.000,'2023-05-24',1,'2023-05-24',1,'In Process.',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-24 13:38:39',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
(21434,'Accounting and book keeping',39,'Hello,\r\nLooking for a bookkeeper, that hopefully has some accounting knowledge (beyond bookkeeping), particularly for the USA. In case of questions, and in help for preparing the taxes. I do use a CPA company to do the taxes (including form 5471).\r\n\r\nMost of the work is simply to upload statements to Wave accounting software, and reconcile. You will be able to look at past years to see categorizations (as some are in Spanish). However I can always do any category you had doubts, no problem.\r\n\r\nYou will get the password to PaySafe (credit card), and will need to download files from there to our joint pcloud folder, organize the folder and upload to wave.\r\n\r\nThere is a cash excel that needs to be uploaded too. Beyond this, would be great to have an expert eye to see if something seems off.\r\n\r\nI pay taxes in Guatemala and the US - My company is a Belize IBC, that has the Us LLC under it.\r\nSpanish is a plus. English a must, and availability. Most of the time there are no urgencies, but my goal is to have everything ready mid December, so I can get an idea of income, and tax owed. I plan on submitting the PL and balance sheet by mid February.\r\nYou are willing to communicate via email and Whatsapp, be timely, and responsible. Must be trust worthy and detail oriented.\r\n\r\nIt is an ongoing job for the years to come.\r\n\r\nLet me know if this sounds good and if you are available.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661368754265632769','-',7,'United States','La Jolla',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-24',1,'2023-05-24',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-24 13:50:08',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
(21435,'Bookkeeper with Accounting Expertise (Advanced or Native English)',39,'Job Description:\r\n\r\nWe are seeking a highly competent bookkeeper with a strong background in accounting to join our team, initially on a short term contract with the potential of extending into a full-time role.\r\n\r\nYou should have extensive experience in bookkeeping and accounting. Fluency in English is mandatory.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n\r\nSupplier Enquiries and Accounts Payable Management:\r\n\r\n• Respond to supplier inquiries promptly and professionally through the AP inbox.\r\n• Process and review invoices, ensuring accuracy and adherence to company policies.\r\n• Perform regular reconciliations of accounts payable transactions.\r\nCollaborate with suppliers to resolve any payment or invoicing issues.\r\n\r\nBank Reconciliation and Financial Reporting:\r\n\r\n• Conduct regular bank reconciliations to ensure accurate recording of transactions.\r\n• Verify and post financial transactions, ensuring proper classification and documentation.\r\n• Identify discrepancies or errors and work towards their timely resolution.\r\n\r\nPayroll Administration:\r\n\r\n• Prepare fortnightly payroll, including accurate calculation of employee salaries, taxes, and benefits.\r\n\r\nGeneral Bookkeeping Support and Best Practices:\r\n\r\n• Provide comprehensive bookkeeping support, ensuring accurate and up-to-date financial records.\r\n• Implement and adhere to best practices in bookkeeping, following industry standards and regulations.\r\n• Collaborate with the team to develop and improve financial processes and procedures.\r\n• Assist with month-end and year-end closing activities.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n\r\n• Solid experience and educational background in accounting or bookkeeping.\r\n• Fluency in English, with excellent written and verbal communication skills.\r\n• Strong attention to detail and ability to work with numerical data accurately.\r\n• Proficiency in bookkeeping software and tools (e.g Xero, Excel).\r\n• Proven ability to work efficiently and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.\r\n• Familiarity with payroll administration and understanding of labor laws and regulations.\r\n• Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills.\r\n• Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive financial information.\r\n\r\nIf you possess the required qualifications and are dedicated to maintaining accurate financial records while adhering to best practices, we would love to hear from you!\r\n\r\nJoin our team and contribute to our commitment to financial excellence and integrity.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661369988586180609','-',7,'United States','Newtown',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-24',1,'2023-05-24',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-24 13:54:53',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
