(21451,'Create Branding Guidelines For Our Agency',2,'Hey, my name is Jace and my agency www.dineline.co needs help creating brand guidelines for social channels, video editing, etc.\r\n\r\nThe problem that I am experiencing is that every time I talk with a video editor or designer it takes them forever to get up to speed on how to edit the content properly.\r\n\r\nIf I had a guideline for fonts, colors, and logos, then our brand would look more unified across platforms.\r\n\r\nI\'m looking for an expert that has experiencing helping brands with this.','https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~01236057aa1c87b748','-',7,'United States','Culver City',60.000,'perhour',50.000,'2023-05-24',1,'2023-05-24',1,'In Process',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-24 15:19:18',NULL,18,3,NULL,126),
(21452,'E-commerce Bookkeeper for Financial Management and Reporting',39,'We are seeking an experienced and detail-oriented E-commerce Bookkeeper to join our team and handle various financial responsibilities within our thriving e-commerce business. As the Bookkeeper, you will play a crucial role in managing bookkeeping tasks, maintaining accurate financial records, reconciling accounts, generating insightful reports, and ensuring compliance with tax regulations. In addition, you will oversee accounts payable and receivable, manage payroll and tax processing, and provide valuable financial insights to optimize margins and profitability.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n-Bookkeeping: Utilize your expertise in bookkeeping, specifically using QuickBooks Online (QBO), to categorize transactions, reconcile accounts, and generate essential financial reports such as Profit and Loss (P&L), Balance Sheet (BS), and Cash Flow (CF) statements.\r\n-Reviewing CC/Bank Statements: Analyze credit card and bank statements, identifying potential red flags such as discrepancies from the previous month and new vendors.\r\n-Accounts Receivable (A/R): Match A/R figures from different sales channels (e.g., Amazon, Shopify, Wholesale, Target) to bank receipts, ensuring accurate accounting and reconciliation.\r\n-Accounts Payable (A/P): Manage accounts payable processes, including bill payment and wire transfers, utilizing suitable software solutions.\r\n-Payroll, CBP, and 401k Processing: Potentially take charge of payroll, employee benefits administration, and retirement plan processing in the future.\r\n-Tax Preparation: Assist with tax-related tasks, such as handling sales tax, income tax, and tax preparation emails. This may also involve managing international sales tax for countries like the UK, Germany, and Canada.\r\n-Timely Tax Payments: Ensure prompt payment of tax estimates and adherence to tax filing deadlines.\r\n-Controller Functions: Act as a financial watchdog, closely monitoring margins per SKU (Stock Keeping Unit) and sales channels.\r\n-Department Cost vs. Sales Analysis: Generate comprehensive reports that compare the costs of operations and marketing departments against sales, offering valuable insights into profitability and margin trends.\r\n-Profit Margin Watchdog: Continuously monitor and analyze profit margins, identifying areas for improvement and implementing strategies to optimize financial performance.\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n-Proven experience as a Bookkeeper, Controller, or CFO, preferably within an e-commerce or retail environment.\r\n-Strong knowledge of bookkeeping principles and practices, with proficiency in using QuickBooks Online (QBO).\r\n-Familiarity with account reconciliation, financial report generation (P&L, BS, CF), and the ability to identify and resolve financial discrepancies.\r\n-Experience in managing accounts receivable and payable processes.\r\n-Basic understanding of payroll processing and employee benefits administration (CBP, 401k).\r\n-Sound knowledge of tax regulations and experience in tax preparation.\r\n-Analytical mindset with the ability to analyze margins, evaluate sales channels, and compare department costs against sales figures.\r\n-Excellent attention to detail and a commitment to maintaining accurate financial records.\r\n-Strong communication skills to collaborate effectively with team members and provide valuable financial insights.\r\n-Self-motivation and the ability to work independently with minimal supervision.\r\n\r\nThis is a remote position offering flexible working hours. Initially, the workload will require approximately 15-20 hours per week, with the potential for increased hours as our e-commerce business expands.\r\n\r\nIf you are an experienced Bookkeeper with a keen eye for detail and a passion for financial management and reporting within the e-commerce sector, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your application, highlighting your relevant experience and availability, to be considered for this role.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661392598373863425','-',7,'United States','Rocky River',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-24',1,'2023-05-24',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-24 15:25:05',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
