(21515,'Real Estate Bookkeeping',39,'We are seeking a detail-oriented and organized Real Estate Bookkeeper to join our team. As a Real Estate Bookkeeper, you will be responsible for accurately recording and managing financial transactions related to our real estate operations. You will work closely with the finance and accounting team to ensure that financial records are maintained accurately and in a timely manner.\r\n\r\nResponsibilities:\r\n- Attend weekly meetings on Wednesdays at 11:00 CST to provide updates and discuss financial matters.\r\n- Create journal entries for all expenses incurred by the real estate business, ensuring accurate categorization and proper documentation.\r\n- Attach supporting statements and documentation to journal entries for proper record-keeping and audit trail.\r\n- Match deposit transactions in bank accounts to corresponding journal entries, ensuring accurate recording of income and expenses.\r\n- Maintain an accurate balance sheet, reconciling accounts regularly to ensure accuracy and identify any discrepancies or errors.\r\n- Track all loan payments and review transactions to ensure that no unauthorized expenses are included.\r\n- Dispute any incorrect transactions or charges related to loans or other financial activities.\r\n- Reconcile bank statements with the company\'s financial records to ensure accurate and up-to-date information.\r\n- Create new classes in QuickBooks Online (QBO) as needed for proper tracking and categorization of expenses and income.\r\n- Create new chart of accounts in QBO as necessary to accommodate changes or expansion in the real estate business.\r\n- Prepare monthly, quarterly, and annual profit and loss (P&L) statements, analyzing financial performance and providing insights to management.\r\n- Ensure that all balance sheet accounts are reconciled on a monthly basis to maintain accurate financial records.\r\n\r\nQualifications:\r\n- Proven experience as a bookkeeper, preferably in the real estate industry.\r\n- Strong understanding of accounting principles and practices.\r\n- Proficient in using accounting software, preferably QuickBooks Online (QBO).\r\n- Excellent attention to detail and accuracy in recording financial transactions.\r\n- Strong organizational and time management skills.\r\n- Ability to work independently and meet deadlines.\r\n- Strong communication skills, both written and verbal.','https://www.upwork.com/ab/proposals/1661745463055884289','-',7,'United States','Memphis',35.000,'perhour',35.000,'2023-05-25',1,'2023-05-25',1,'Hourly Project',0,'Open this select menu',NULL,1,'2023-05-25 14:47:04',NULL,11,3,NULL,140),
