(233,17,50,'Individual',74,'In-process',NULL,'03/27/2023: Called Benefit Administrative to verify the Phone Number for the Practice. As per the Rep, they are TPA and don\'t have Credentialing requirement and there is no data available in their records for the Practice FAMILY MEDICINE CENTER OF AUSTIN, P.A. Rep Name: Sarah H Ref # SarahH03272023 (Anil  03/16/2023: Called Benefit Administrative to check enrollment status. As per the Rep they can not check the provider\'s individual status, they can only check when we provider Member\'s ID. Rep confirms that they do not provide Credentialing for providers because they are TPA (Third Party Administrator) for different PPO insurance plans. Rep said that, Network Participation depend upon the Insured Member\'s Plan, if provider is contracted with the Primary Insurance Company, then provider will be considered \"In Network\". As per Rep, they do not provide Individual or Group Credentialing, providers needs to contact the Primary Insurance to get them self Credentialed for Any Specific Plan, if the provider is already contracted with the respective insurance company then we can call Benefit Administrative with member ID to check Network Participation and Verify Plan Benefits or Check Claim Status. Rep also confirm that most of there Plans are Open Access and does not requires Credentialing, they follow Medicare fee schedule for Open Access Plans. Rep suggested that we can login to Provider Portal to check if the provider is In Network with Member\'s Plan using Member ID via Online Portal Link: https://www.baslimited.com/provider-login. Rep Name: Roshalle Ref # Roshalle03162023 (Anil)  01/10/2023: Called Insurance Benefit Administrative to check enrollment status. As per the Rep they can not check the provider\'s individual status, they are TPA (Third Party Administration Service) for multiple insurances and it depend upon what insurance is provided by employer to the insured member. They do not do Credentialing by them self, the provider needs to contact the main insurance company to get credentialed, for example if member have Cigna TPA Plan and we are already Credentialed with Cigna Commercial Insurance then we will automatically be in Network for Benefit Administrative and then we can call them with member ID to check if we are In Network or Not and also we can verify the plan benefits. Rep also confirm that most of there Plans are Open Access and they do not require Credentialing, they follow Medicare fee schedule for Open Access Plans. Rep suggested that before the provider files any claim they can register first by sending W9 Form to Email: clientservices@insurancebenefitadministrators.com OR Fax 913-945-4399. It will take 72 business hours to get register, this will help insurance to determine that where to sent claims payments. Rep Name: ZariaA Ref # ZariaA01092023  (Anil)  06/23/2023: Called Benefit Administrative to Confirm Change of Address Procedure. As per the Rep, they do not provide Credentialing for Providers  because they operate as a third party administrator for different PPO Insurance Plans. Rep suggests to contact Primary Insurance to get Credentialing status which depend upon the Primary Insurance for the Insured Member Plan. They do not do Credentialing by them self, the provider needs to contact  the Primary Insurance Company to get Credentialed or updated Demographics. Rep Name: Ray H Ref # RayH06232023 (Anil)','2023-11-03','2023-11-03 14:37:15',NULL),
